{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers","id":579778,"title":"[Beast] Why I don't want them in crossovers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-05T06:52:04-07:00","id":579778,"title":"[Beast] Why I don't want them in crossovers","content":"People are saying that Beasts are really crossover friendly thanks to their innate powers and thematics, but I honestly see nothing of it and I believe Beasts would ruin any game in which players are mostly something else such as werewolves or Vampires.<br /> <br /> <b>Power level</b><br /> First thing, the PL of Beast is off the charts, with free, scene-long perfect-effects at every corner. And then there are Vampires with the capacity to run faster for a turn by spending a point of Vitae.<br /> <br /> <b>Theme</b><br /> Beast's themes are twofold, as far as I know: &quot;Monsters are what they do not what they are&quot;, and Hunger. Both of which can be twisted into what's needed for any other gameline, but then again in a Mage game I don't see a Beast fitting in real well. At best it'll clash thematically, at worst their whole theme goes to trash and it's a Mage game with a Beast in it. <br /> <br /> <b>The Beast Mythos</b><br /> Even if many many people have stated that the Beast mythology is no more true or false than any other, they have so many proofs to back their claim that it basically breaks any other gameline's mythos. It's even worse than playing with mages.<br /> <br /> <b>Mother's Kiss</b><br /> I could also call this power 'Spotlight Stealer' because I can't see a situation in which a player being helped by Mother's Kiss won't get the message that the Beast player believes his powers are worthless without some help.<br /> &quot;I don't think 4 dice is enough, here have a few more&quot; or &quot;I fear that your obfuscate has too many flaws, take some dice to enhance it&quot; will not be received well for many players.<br /> <br /> <b>Thicker Than Water</b><br /> The 'best-friends forever' power which states that Beasts are always on good terms with everyone because reasons. This power only proves a little more that the Beast Mythos is the one and only truth rather than their own vision. Had it been that Beasts always see other monsters with a Good first impression, it would have made a lot more sense.<br /> <br /> <b>Family Dinner</b><br /> So...this power seems to exist to make sure that Beasts never go below 7 in a Vampire game, and always stay at 2 in a Mage game. Also, it removes the whole Hunger theme from them since the Horror that could only feed by harvesting people's fingers is now fine and sated after <i>watching</i> a Kindred take a bite.<br /> <br /> <b>Skeleton Key</b><br /> A power which allow Beasts to almost instantly open gateways to any other world as far as they are aware that such gateways exist. So say a pack of werewolves want to bring the Beast and a few wolf-blooded and maybe a Vampire with them to hunt in the Hisil, the Ritemaster telling them that it will take some time since he has to open the gateway to all of them and that they'll have to take part in a rite that will last an hour, maybe more. And then the Beast just goes &quot;Dude don't, I got this!&quot; and opens the gate. Thanks, Beast, for ruining the scene and grabbing the spotlight again.<br /> <br /> <b>Family Ressemblance</b><br /> This power allows the Beast to remove from the GM's toolbox any kind of paranoia. That's it. Vampire game with a Beast in? No Strixes. Werewolf game? This guy's a Claimed still undercover. Mage game? These two looking at us in the shadow are also mages, not some goons. Changeling? This guy reading the journal is a Huntsman trying to get info before striking. Wanna know what's even worst? Thicker Than Water then allows him to walk up to the antagonist and have coffee with him.<br /> <br /> <b>Final Disclaimer</b><br /> I don't hate these powers, I think they fit thematically with Beast and allow for awesome Beast-only games, but as of now, Beast suffers the same problem that Mage has: They have the answer to every problem and their Mythos explains everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T07:10:42-07:00","id":579800,"title":"","content":"Ok. So? No-one is forcing you. I hope you have fun playing the game your way.<br /> <br /> I am sorry that you will continue to see cross-over questions and story ideas concerning them for quite awhile yet. Ideally this thread won't attract flamers/haters. It is well written, respectful and very clear in it's intent. At least it was when I started typing this post.<br /> <br /> You deserve to have your opinion respected. Ideally others, whom may well naturally, disagree with you won't try to force their thoughts &amp; opinions upon you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T07:27:14-07:00","id":579804,"title":"","content":"Maybe I'm missing something because I haven't read Beast yet, but I thought the idea with Beast and crossover was to play a game where the players are all Beasts and they go and interact with NPCs of other lines, not to have one random Beast player in an otherwise all-vampire game or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T07:32:02-07:00","id":579807,"title":"","content":"As far as I know, both are supposed to be viable play. If it was intended as what you read, Charlaquin, then I must admit that it was gloriously executed. If, however, it was meant as I interpreted it from my reading, then my concerns are still valid.<br /> <br /> FallenEco, my point was to try and have a civilized discussion on the more mechanically lacking aspects of the crossover elements included in this new game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T07:42:34-07:00","id":579814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=579807#post579807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I know, both are supposed to be viable play. If it was intended as what you read, Charlaquin, then I must admit that it was gloriously executed. If, however, it was meant as I interpreted it from my reading, then my concerns are still valid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotcha. I'll have to finally give it a read before I can comment, I just wanted to make suere I understood the intent with the crossover element.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T08:35:25-07:00","id":579862,"title":"","content":"You might have better luck if you provided better reasoning.<br /> <br /> Claiming the power to make other pcs more awesome steals the spotlight? Sure, if the player is having some kind of psychotic break from reality, by that tortured use of logic one pc helping another using the teamwork rules is bashing the other player over the head to mug him of his spotlight.<br /> <br /> Only using it as a judgement that the other PC's powers aren't good enough? First of all, it's not the beast's choice when the supernatural uses their extra dice, and secondly, I have no doubt whatsoever that plenty of players are going to use that boost to enhance their strongest abilities, because rpg players acting like rpg players isn't really a big stretch. <br /> <br /> Family resemblance- Oh how horrible, beasts can do the same thing every mage ever, vampires with auspex, or werewolves with scent the unnatural can do, and that's just off the top of my head, the ability to detect other supernaturals is hardly rare in the nwod.<br /> <br /> Family dinner- Allows beasts to avoid derailing someone else's game by being supportive of vampires or whatever replenishing their energy. That's not a bug, that's a feature.<br /> <br /> Mythos being a problem- Their mythos doesn't necessarily explain anything. Beasts are living nightmares, how odd is it that living nightmares might share a connection with beings that inspire nightmares? Not at all.<br /> <br /> Skeleton Key- You honestly think that helping a group get to the hisil takes away the spotlight from the one splat most intertwined with the hisil and it's inhabitants? Because no, it really really doesn't.<br /> <br /> Length of power effects? Vampires with celerity get a constant benefit from it 24/7, it's rather hard to beat til the end of time for length of effect.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the gist of your argument seems to be 'I don't like it.&quot;<br /> <br /> You know what? That's fine, it's no skin off my nose. Play it without crossover, play it with bluebook splats, play it with do it yourself monsters from hunter/wod 2d ed, whatever way you can have fun with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":391,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","user":"StSword","date":". 07-05-2015, 11:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T09:08:40-07:00","id":579872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=579804#post579804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I'm missing something because I haven't read Beast yet, but I thought the idea with Beast and crossover was to play a game where the players are all Beasts and they go and interact with NPCs of other lines, not to have one random Beast player in an otherwise all-vampire game or something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beast has far less in the way of plot hooks and even just <i>setting</i> than the other lines; which leaves the impression that you're supposed to lean towards using other gamelines to fill in the gaps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T09:17:35-07:00","id":579877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=579872#post579872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beast has far less in the way of plot hooks and even just <i>setting</i> than the other lines; which leaves the impression that you're supposed to lean towards using other gamelines to fill in the gaps.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that was why I figured Beast games would feature NPCs from other game lines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T10:05:34-07:00","id":579901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=579862#post579862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mythos being a problem- Their mythos doesn't necessarily explain anything. Beasts are living nightmares, how odd is it that living nightmares might share a connection with beings that inspire nightmares? Not at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the part of the mythos that the OP is referring to is the idea that all supernatural beings (with a few possible exceptions) are in some way descendants of the same Dark Mother that Beasts claim as their progenitor, a proposition that Werewolves and Mages, at the very least, would find objectionable.<br /> <br /> That said, sticking with those two splats for the moment, Mages <i>know</i> that the Supernal realms exist, and there's arguably concrete evidence of the Awakened City and the Exarchs, for those who want to look for it. Likewise, while most Werewolves may never have a direct encounter with their tribal totem, the fact remains that Father Wolf's immortal firstborn children are still out there and more-or-less cooperating with their fleshed cousins, suggesting that the Uratha probably have a pretty good idea of what they're talking about when it comes to their mythology.<br /> <br /> What I'm trying to say is that the evidence that Beasts have with regard to their own mythos isn't necessarily any more compelling than the evidence other supernatural beings have that might contradict it. Considering the tangled and tortured nature of truth and reality in the World of Darkness (thanks to all sorts of things with reality-altering powers, up to and including quasi-godlike beings that have re-written history wholesale), it's probably possible that all mythologies are both true and false at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 07-05-2015, 01:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T10:30:21-07:00","id":579924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers#post579778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People are saying that Beasts are really crossover friendly thanks to their innate powers and thematics, but I honestly see nothing of it and I believe Beasts would ruin any game in which players are mostly something else such as werewolves or Vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div> Its no secret that crossovers do dilute the game themes. But here's several things you're missing:<br /> <br /> 1) There are multiple kinds of crossovers. One is where everyone is one kind of supernatural, and you run into other kinds through play; you can have Beasts as all PCs that encounter others, or others that meet up with Beasts. Another is a mostly 1 kind of supernatural with others sprinkled in. A third is where everyone's a different kind.<br /> <br /> 2) No one's forcing you to bring in Beasts if you're playing a Vampire or whatever game. You're also not forced to bring the God Machine into Vampire, Wolf, Mage, etc.<br /> <br /> 3) Yes, they are crossover friendly, because they're powers are literally designed to make friends in game. They have abilities that let them get along with other supernaturals and not be locked out if we happen to hop across realms. They have plot hooks and reasons to go out and seek supernaturals, including Family Dinner. They're driven<br /> <br /> 4) Themes are gonna get muddled. This is known already. It was true before, its true during, its true after. Hells, <i>there is a paragraph inside the book that flat out says it! </i> You don't like it, then Beast isn't for you.<br /> <br /> I really think people are beating their head against this crossover thing because they don't understand how crossover actually works. Being crossover friendly just means that they have an easier time of it, rather than instant suspicion. They can notice other supernaturals and be noticed, they can move into the Hisil, Hedge, whatever as the game demands, etc. Its not going to be as tight of a story than if you didn't have a Beast, but that's part of the trade off you get with a crossover game.<br /> <br /> <i>This is a crossover game because Beasts are given every chance and reason to seek out other supernaturals and play with them. Its a central theme in the game. </i>Beast is not a game where you just sit in your own communities. You go out and find other supernaturals. You are driven to find family.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Power level</b><br /> First thing, the PL of Beast is off the charts, with free, scene-long perfect-effects at every corner. And then there are Vampires with the capacity to run faster for a turn by spending a point of Vitae. </div> </div> </div> Oi. This again. As if Majesty and the three physicals aren't the same in Vampire, as if Mages can't have Sight and Armor up all the time, plus other effects. As if vampires and wolves don't have far more potent innate tricks, such as riding the wave / the war form or the innate healing. Or, hells, Predator's aura / aspects. Really, if we discount Atavisms, Nightmares, Disciplines, Gifts, Arcana, Contracts, etc, Beasts are actually the <i>weakest</i> of supernaturals. I'd put my money on an unprepared Mage before the Begotten.<br /> <br /> And that's before we get into the fact that every game has its own niche. No one beats vamps at mind control. Werewolves rock at the hunt. Mages are arcane scholars/academics. The Lost are illusionists and masters of pledge magic (I call them the wish granters, anything you dream up!) Beasts aren't better than anyone else at those niches.<br /> <br /> Game balance is a myth - no two groups are the same, it all comes down to individual players, and managing the splat's drawbacks.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Theme</b><br /> Beast's themes are twofold, as far as I know: &quot;Monsters are what they do not what they are&quot;, and Hunger. Both of which can be twisted into what's needed for any other gameline, but then again in a Mage game I don't see a Beast fitting in real well. At best it'll clash thematically, at worst their whole theme goes to trash and it's a Mage game with a Beast in it. </div> </div> </div> Mages have a hunger for arcane secrets. There's astral exploration they share in common. The Mastigos themes of Adversity and the whole Beast teaching through Nightmares resonate. All you need is one way to make it work, not a thousand excuses why it wouldn't.<br /> <br /> EDIT - Also, you missed the theme of &quot;Choosing your own Family.&quot; That's a big one in Beast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The Beast Mythos</b><br /> Even if many many people have stated that the Beast mythology is no more true or false than any other, they have so many proofs to back their claim that it basically breaks any other gameline's mythos. It's even worse than playing with mages. </div> </div> </div> No more than Mages do with Atlantis, the Wolves do with Pangaea, the vamps do with the strix, the Mummies and Irem... every game has a secret history with in game proof.<br /> <br /> And, lets be honest. Beast's mythos doesn't actually invalidate anyone else's either. This is part of the whole crossover thing. CotC vampires are dealing with the children of the Dark Mother they worship. Werewolves can decide they're dealing with the mother of all spirits, or perhaps other children of Luna herself. The Beast mythos is flexible enough to resonate with anyone else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Mother's Kiss</b><br /> I could also call this power 'Spotlight Stealer' because I can't see a situation in which a player being helped by Mother's Kiss won't get the message that the Beast player believes his powers are worthless without some help.<br /> &quot;I don't think 4 dice is enough, here have a few more&quot; or &quot;I fear that your obfuscate has too many flaws, take some dice to enhance it&quot; will not be received well for many players. </div> </div> </div>Wow. Just... wow. Spotlight Stealer? Really? You've clearly never played a buffer in any game before. No one is going to be pissed at a blessing. If you do have that in your game, then I think that's a player issue.<br /> <br /> And 4 dice is pretty shitty, to be honest - that's still a fairly notable chance of failing. I consider 7 dice to be a good amount to be considered reliable with any dice pool. I'm estatic for boosts at that dice level.<br /> <br /> And doesn't Mother's Kiss comes with a price on the Beast's part?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Thicker Than Water</b><br /> The 'best-friends forever' power which states that Beasts are always on good terms with everyone because reasons. This power only proves a little more that the Beast Mythos is the one and only truth rather than their own vision. Had it been that Beasts always see other monsters with a Good first impression, it would have made a lot more sense. </div> </div> </div> .....<br /> No, they're not &quot;always on good terms.&quot; They <i>start out</i> on Good terms, meaning Beasts make a good first impression, no more. They can very quickly get on bad terms. No, it doesn't prove that the Beast myth is true, it just means that they're supernaturally friendly. If that's proof, its shakey at best. See above for more on the myth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Family Dinner</b><br /> So...this power seems to exist to make sure that Beasts never go below 7 in a Vampire game, and always stay at 2 in a Mage game. </div> </div> </div> Nooooo. It exists to give Beasts an active reason to hunt out other supernaturals and make friends with them. Because <i>this is a crossover game and doing crossover plots is a huge part of it.</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, it removes the whole Hunger theme from them since the Horror that could only feed by harvesting people's fingers is now fine and sated after <i>watching</i> a Kindred take a bite. </div> </div> </div> No, it enhances it, because it showcases many different kinds of supernatural hunger that are out there. Getting a voyeuristic pleasure out of watching someone <i>eat another human being</i> is nothing to sneer at.<br /> <br /> It also highlights the &quot;Choose your own Family&quot; theme that's rampant in the game. This is a game about embracing new family instead of your biological ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Skeleton Key</b><br /> A power which allow Beasts to almost instantly open gateways to any other world as far as they are aware that such gateways exist. So say a pack of werewolves want to bring the Beast and a few wolf-blooded and maybe a Vampire with them to hunt in the Hisil, the Ritemaster telling them that it will take some time since he has to open the gateway to all of them and that they'll have to take part in a rite that will last an hour, maybe more. And then the Beast just goes &quot;Dude don't, I got this!&quot; and opens the gate. Thanks, Beast, for ruining the scene and grabbing the spotlight again. </div> </div> </div> How is this spotlight stealing, exactly? A ritemaster isn't defined by his ability to ferry people across the Gauntlet, its defined by using a host full of rites. Its also defined by being a werewolf shapeshifter.<br /> <br /> And there's still the problem of finding the locus. Without the ritemaster... there would never be a gateway in the first place! That's not suddenly removing spotlights. Its getting over a speedbump where someone rolls some dice so you can actually play the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Family Ressemblance</b><br /> This power allows the Beast to remove from the GM's toolbox any kind of paranoia. </div> </div> </div> A strange new vamp/wolf/mage/etc on the scene, and that removes paranoia? Last I checked, most supers are paranoid of their own kind. Wolves don't get along with others not in their pack automatically, vamps aren't known for playing nice, mages steal secrets from each other, changelings fear betrayal, Loyalists and Bridge Burners, especially ones without Mantles.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Final Disclaimer</b><br /> I don't hate these powers, I think they fit thematically with Beast and allow for awesome Beast-only games, but as of now, Beast suffers the same problem that Mage has: They have the answer to every problem and their Mythos explains everything. </div> </div> </div> Funny thing is that mages don't have the answer to every problem, and they don't try to explain everything. Very few mage fan even try to claim that. Its the people who complain about Mage and not actually play the game who make those claims.<br /> <br /> The same thing here. You're not giving the game its fair shake by playing it and taking everything way out of context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-05-2015, 01:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T10:34:37-07:00","id":579968,"title":"","content":"Thicker than water doesn't do what you're saying it does. All it does is make it so that in a vacuum most supernaturals are inclined towards being alright with the Beast when they first meet. It does nothing to ensure positive relations beyond first impressions before anyone has said or done anything. Hell your logic of spotting the antagonist then walking up and getting coffee still probably ends with the Beast getting killed if the antagonist is still aware who the Beast is with the only difference being that maybe the antagonist feels its nothing personal when they start the killing.<br /> <br /> One person brought it up in the main Beast thread a long time back with the example of a Beast interposing itself between some hunter things, I forget what they're called. trying to capture Changelings for the Fey they serve.* First it requires that the Beast not be blatant about trying to help the Changelings, so they need to show up when there's enough of a gap for it to be believable that the Changelings weren't noticed or something. Second the Beast still needs to be polite about things as retriever is only going to be inclined towards liking the Beast as long as no other factors exist once the Beast starts talking this thing will start having reasons to like or dislike it. The final one was basically be ready to fight or run as the Beast is still getting in the way of the retriever's job and unless the Beast came up with an excellent reason for the retriever to go around the area the best the Beast is getting is being told to stand aside and not interfere anymore. Its all still predicated on the idea that Beast has some way to get the thing to stop long enough to do anything and not that it won't just ram through the Beast while performing the chase going, &quot;excuse me&quot; or something.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *It was a while back through god only knows how much circular fighting about a lot of stuff and I don't play Changeling, so I'll ask for pardon on some things since I'm trying to remember the important details of that bit of discussion after a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T11:05:37-07:00","id":579984,"title":"","content":"Beasts are going to fit extremely well into Mage, in my opinion. Not only do Beasts make an excellent Mystery for 2nd Ed Mages to obsess over, but the Primordial Dream is part of the Mage's (kinda) exclusive Otherworld - the Astral. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: the Ascension - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1191028-redesigned-prime-sphere\" target=\"_blank\">Redesigned Prime Sphere</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1188769-simpler-wonder-creation\" target=\"_blank\">Streamlined Wonder Creation</a><br /> Mummy: the Curse - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/474927-mummy-the-curse-2e-conversion\" target=\"_blank\">Lightweight 2E Conversion</a>; <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/22378-second-sight-tradition-disciples-of-duat\" target=\"_blank\">Disciples of Duat</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/61-octavo","name":"Octavo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar61_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1171"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T11:11:35-07:00","id":579987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers#post579778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People are saying that Beasts are really crossover friendly thanks to their innate powers and thematics, but I honestly see nothing of it and I believe Beasts would ruin any game in which players are mostly something else such as werewolves or Vampires.</div> </div> </div> </div> Welp, this is going to be a fun morning.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Power level</b><br /> First thing, the PL of Beast is off the charts, with free, scene-long perfect-effects at every corner. And then there are Vampires with the capacity to run faster for a turn by spending a point of Vitae. </div> </div> </div>Maybe by First Edition standards, but vampires and werewolves have a lot of powers that don't require fuel and kick all kinds of ass in Second Edition. Atavisms are potent mofos, I grant you, but it's hardly a stretch beyond what Second Edition has set as a standard.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Theme</b><br /> Beast's themes are twofold, as far as I know: &quot;Monsters are what they do not what they are&quot;, and Hunger. Both of which can be twisted into what's needed for any other gameline, but then again in a Mage game I don't see a Beast fitting in real well. At best it'll clash thematically, at worst their whole theme goes to trash and it's a Mage game with a Beast in it. </div> </div> </div> Beasts themes are rolled up in the supernatural family and the hungers and the handling of them. Crossover of any sort requires jury rigging, but Beast isn't any worse for that than any other game, and in fact is broad enough parallel the others on certain fronts.<br /> <br /> Vampires and Beasts share the themes of struggling with addiction and the struggle with being a predator of what they formerly were.<br /> Werewolves and Beasts share the themes of family, hunting, and spiritual consequences.<br /> Mages and Beasts share the themes of occult mysteries and the consequences of power.<br /> Prometheans and Beasts share the themes of alienation and disassociation from reality, particularly in regards to their bodies.(flesh bubbles fair and foul)<br /> Changelings and Beasts share the themes of struggle against narratives(or conceptions of a fated, unfair world) and the intoxication of retreats into fantasy.<br /> Hunters and Beasts share the themes of uniting with uncertain allies against a grim dark world for a better future.<br /> Sin-Eaters and Beasts share the themes of the struggle with grim inevitabilities and the collection and untangling of Jungian mythologies both grand and personal.<br /> Mummies and Beasts share the themes of mythic motivation and enslavement to dark powers.<br /> Demons and Beasts share the themes of being hunted by a world motivated against you and the dual-and-opposites needs of trust and safety.<br /> <br /> Of course you have to bend some things to fit, that happens in any crossover. But it's not that hard to make it work.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The Beast Mythos</b><br /> Even if many many people have stated that the Beast mythology is no more true or false than any other, they have so many proofs to back their claim that it basically breaks any other gameline's mythos. It's even worse than playing with mages. </div> </div> </div> 1)You mean a certain subset of Mage fans.<br /> <br /> 2) They also have a lot of things that go against them. They're a compelling argument, but they fail to interact with just as many things as they do. They might be able to add to the powers of the Curses or the Wyrd or Sekhem, but they lack the powers to truly interface with them and use them the same way anything else does, which is something that you'd imagine an progenitor species would have the ability to do.<br /> <br /> EDIT: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/229044-beast-the-primordial?p=541793#post541793\">Relevant post here.</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Mother's Kiss</b><br /> I could also call this power 'Spotlight Stealer' because I can't see a situation in which a player being helped by Mother's Kiss won't get the message that the Beast player believes his powers are worthless without some help.<br /> &quot;I don't think 4 dice is enough, here have a few more&quot; or &quot;I fear that your obfuscate has too many flaws, take some dice to enhance it&quot; will not be received well for many players. </div> </div> </div>For the record, this is the one that inspired me to respond, because I am utterly baffled by it.<br /> <br /> Speaking as someone who played warlords and bards in 4E DnD, a guy who plays support roles a lot, in fact,I don't see how giving dice to anything is a belittlement. It's a boon to help others kick ass.<br /> <br /> What, is a Cahalith using War Howl a way for werewolves to say &quot;Listen, we just don't think you're kick ass enough, have some help&quot; too? I'm sorry, this <i>baffles</i> me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Thicker Than Water</b><br /> The 'best-friends forever' power which states that Beasts are always on good terms with everyone because reasons. This power only proves a little more that the Beast Mythos is the one and only truth rather than their own vision. Had it been that Beasts always see other monsters with a Good first impression, it would have made a lot more sense. </div> </div> </div> Because low level psychological improvement of initial impressions on creatures who are loosely similar to you in a &quot;like affects like&quot; manner is both game-breaking and cosmology defining.<br /> <br /> Sorry, no. It's an example of Beast' s weird ability to interface with several other monsters, but that can be chocked up to a lot of different things. Most people are going to start off with a good impression of sirens, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Family Dinner</b><br /> So...this power seems to exist to make sure that Beasts never go below 7 in a Vampire game, and always stay at 2 in a Mage game. Also, it removes the whole Hunger theme from them since the Horror that could only feed by harvesting people's fingers is now fine and sated after <i>watching</i> a Kindred take a bite. </div> </div> </div> Family Dinner exists as a way for you to turn the knobs on focus for Beasts between the supernatural family and Hunger, so you're half right. That said, feeding from this is a broader thing. a beast can feed off of a mage fulfilling his Obsessions, which is plainly stated all over the place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Skeleton Key</b><br /> A power which allow Beasts to almost instantly open gateways to any other world as far as they are aware that such gateways exist. So say a pack of werewolves want to bring the Beast and a few wolf-blooded and maybe a Vampire with them to hunt in the Hisil, the Ritemaster telling them that it will take some time since he has to open the gateway to all of them and that they'll have to take part in a rite that will last an hour, maybe more. And then the Beast just goes &quot;Dude don't, I got this!&quot; and opens the gate. Thanks, Beast, for ruining the scene and grabbing the spotlight again. </div> </div> </div>1)It doesn't take werewolves that long, and 2) it costs them less than it costs Beasts. Similar principles apply across the board. It creates options, it doesn't make them the go-to answer for everything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Family Ressemblance</b><br /> This power allows the Beast to remove from the GM's toolbox any kind of paranoia. That's it. Vampire game with a Beast in? No Strixes. Werewolf game? This guy's a Claimed still undercover. Mage game? These two looking at us in the shadow are also mages, not some goons. Changeling? This guy reading the journal is a Huntsman trying to get info before striking. Wanna know what's even worst? Thicker Than Water then allows him to walk up to the antagonist and have coffee with him. </div> </div> </div> Someone else has pointed all the ways that other creatures can do the exact same thing. The only difference is that Beasts have it baked in.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Final Disclaimer</b><br /> I don't hate these powers, I think they fit thematically with Beast and allow for awesome Beast-only games, but as of now, Beast suffers the same problem that Mage has: They have the answer to every problem and their Mythos explains everything. </div> </div> </div>This is less a problem with the games and more a problem with the fandom. People read it and think it answers every problem and explains everything. They are wrong on both counts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-05-2015, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T11:38:35-07:00","id":580001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=579862#post579862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might have better luck if you provided better reasoning.<br /> <br /> Claiming the power to make other pcs more awesome steals the spotlight? Sure, if the player is having some kind of psychotic break from reality, by that tortured use of logic one pc helping another using the teamwork rules is bashing the other player over the head to mug him of his spotlight.<br /> <br /> Only using it as a judgement that the other PC's powers aren't good enough? First of all, it's not the beast's choice when the supernatural uses their extra dice, and secondly, I have no doubt whatsoever that plenty of players are going to use that boost to enhance their strongest abilities, because rpg players acting like rpg players isn't really a big stretch.<br /> <br /> Family resemblance- Oh how horrible, beasts can do the same thing every mage ever, vampires with auspex, or werewolves with scent the unnatural can do, and that's just off the top of my head, the ability to detect other supernaturals is hardly rare in the nwod.<br /> <br /> Family dinner- Allows beasts to avoid derailing someone else's game by being supportive of vampires or whatever replenishing their energy. That's not a bug, that's a feature.<br /> <br /> Mythos being a problem- Their mythos doesn't necessarily explain anything. Beasts are living nightmares, how odd is it that living nightmares might share a connection with beings that inspire nightmares? Not at all.<br /> <br /> Skeleton Key- You honestly think that helping a group get to the hisil takes away the spotlight from the one splat most intertwined with the hisil and it's inhabitants? Because no, it really really doesn't.<br /> <br /> Length of power effects? Vampires with celerity get a constant benefit from it 24/7, it's rather hard to beat til the end of time for length of effect.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the gist of your argument seems to be 'I don't like it.&quot;<br /> <br /> You know what? That's fine, it's no skin off my nose. Play it without crossover, play it with bluebook splats, play it with do it yourself monsters from hunter/wod 2d ed, whatever way you can have fun with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm floored that this post got as many likes, as of now, as any other in the thread, and four times as many as the OP.<br /> <br /> Magnum Opus has been respectful with his opinions, explaining them rationally and politely without resorting to insults or snide remarks.<br /> <br /> Your response indirectly accuses him of having a psychotic break from reality and using &quot;tortured logic,&quot; uses sarcasm and a general all-around nasty tone, and somehow people find it adds more to the community and this forum than the entirely reasonable (whether you agree with it or find it entirely 100% true to the RAI or not) OP.<br /> <br /> This is unacceptable.<br /> <br /> I expect better than 4chan when I come to OPP forums.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T11:40:26-07:00","id":580003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers#post579778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Power level</b><br /> First thing, the PL of Beast is off the charts, with free, scene-long perfect-effects at every corner. And then there are Vampires with the capacity to run faster for a turn by spending a point of Vitae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends a lot on the circumstances and nature of the crossover game in question. It is pertinently discussed in the storytelling chapter from various points, not the least of which is the feelings of the players involved. Depending on who you ask, different 'powerlevels' do not break a crossover game, since power discrepancies exist even within the same splat, just less so because the games are balanced internally. I, for one, really see no issue with a crossover game in which characters have different 'powerlevels' if everyone's having fun, but I get that not everyone would be fine with that. That's fair.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers#post579778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Theme</b><br /> Beast's themes are twofold, as far as I know: &quot;Monsters are what they do not what they are&quot;, and Hunger. Both of which can be twisted into what's needed for any other gameline, but then again in a Mage game I don't see a Beast fitting in real well. At best it'll clash thematically, at worst their whole theme goes to trash and it's a Mage game with a Beast in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book explores common themes between the splats and explains how they can work together (or against each other) rather satisfactorily. (Even with Mages. And let's not forget how they're the two lines that have the most interaction with the Astral.) You can try to follow the suggestions (or not) and extrapolate them. Or, as Charlaquin suggested, you could play a Beast game in which Beasts interact with the other lines peripherally, rather than the kind of chronicle that tosses one Beast in with a group otherwise made of a specific splat.<br /> <br /> (And again, the storyteller section accounts for both options. And both can by all means be viable ways of playing if you handle it well.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers#post579778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Beast Mythos</b><br /> Even if many many people have stated that the Beast mythology is no more true or false than any other, they have so many proofs to back their claim that it basically breaks any other gameline's mythos. It's even worse than playing with mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>They really don't have much 'proof' that does anything except concile the existence of other monsters as related to them - the Dark Mother is their answer to that, and a big answer in their own mythos, but they don't even try to subdue or explain the majority of the 'big' details in the other lines' cosmology far as I see it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers#post579778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Mother's Kiss</b><br /> I could also call this power 'Spotlight Stealer' because I can't see a situation in which a player being helped by Mother's Kiss won't get the message that the Beast player believes his powers are worthless without some help.<br /> &quot;I don't think 4 dice is enough, here have a few more&quot; or &quot;I fear that your obfuscate has too many flaws, take some dice to enhance it&quot; will not be received well for many players.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty negative view of a power that's only useful if the Beast has another supernatural to cooperate with. When I described Beasts and their crossover design to a friend, he really liked all the options Beasts bring to the table that make them excellent team players with other supernaturals. He thought they sounded overall fantastic in making crossover chronicles more interesting and encouraging different supernaturals to work together due to the utility the presence of the Beast allows the whole group.<br /> <br /> In other words, yes you're due your opinion on it, but you should also recognize you're negatively biased.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers#post579778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Thicker Than Water</b><br /> The 'best-friends forever' power which states that Beasts are always on good terms with everyone because reasons. This power only proves a little more that the Beast Mythos is the one and only truth rather than their own vision. Had it been that Beasts always see other monsters with a Good first impression, it would have made a lot more sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how Thicker Than Water works, as people have already pointed out. It's also reliant on the other supernatural not having reasons to actually be wary or antagonistic of the Beast, it which case it's useless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers#post579778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Family Dinner</b><br /> So...this power seems to exist to make sure that Beasts never go below 7 in a Vampire game, and always stay at 2 in a Mage game. Also, it removes the whole Hunger theme from them since the Horror that could only feed by harvesting people's fingers is now fine and sated after <i>watching</i> a Kindred take a bite.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's an alternative way to <i>deal with Hunger</i>, one that encourages Beasts to gather in broods and seek out other supernaturals. It doesn't remove the theme, it plays into it and is a further incentive for crossover.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers#post579778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Skeleton Key</b><br /> A power which allow Beasts to almost instantly open gateways to any other world as far as they are aware that such gateways exist. So say a pack of werewolves want to bring the Beast and a few wolf-blooded and maybe a Vampire with them to hunt in the Hisil, the Ritemaster telling them that it will take some time since he has to open the gateway to all of them and that they'll have to take part in a rite that will last an hour, maybe more. And then the Beast just goes &quot;Dude don't, I got this!&quot; and opens the gate. Thanks, Beast, for ruining the scene and grabbing the spotlight again.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beasts also have no ability whatsoever to find those gateways. As for spotlight stealing, well, see above. It depends entirely on how you look at it. If Beasts help other games monopolize their own strengths and can boost other supernaturals does that make them spotlight stealers?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers#post579778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Family Ressemblance</b><br /> This power allows the Beast to remove from the GM's toolbox any kind of paranoia. That's it. Vampire game with a Beast in? No Strixes. Werewolf game? This guy's a Claimed still undercover. Mage game? These two looking at us in the shadow are also mages, not some goons. Changeling? This guy reading the journal is a Huntsman trying to get info before striking. Wanna know what's even worst? Thicker Than Water then allows him to walk up to the antagonist and have coffee with him.</div> </div> </div> </div>Family Resemblance isn't reliable against targets using an ability to conceal themselves. Yes, it makes a few situations easier, but if dealing with those enemies was as simple as identifying them (and identifying them was that simple), they wouldn't be nearly as dangerous as they actually are.<br /> <br /> And no, Thicker Than Water wouldn't really let them do that unless the antagonist wanted to as well and whatever the Beast wanted to say didn't confict with their interests. Or the Beast's attitude didn't displease them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers#post579778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Final Disclaimer</b><br /> I don't hate these powers, I think they fit thematically with Beast and allow for awesome Beast-only games, but as of now, Beast suffers the same problem that Mage has: They have the answer to every problem and their Mythos explains everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>They really don't have the answer to every problem and their myths don't explain everything. Not even close. Neither do Mage myths.<br /> <br /> As FallenEco put it, no one's forcing you to do crossover. You're in your right to not like its crossover paradigms, but objectively, you're not really being fair to the game either. But you've probably heard these points enough by now.<br /> <br /> Edit: Wow, sniped by everyone in the time I was writing this and doing other stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 07-05-2015, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T11:42:19-07:00","id":580004,"title":"","content":"If it's unacceptable, please flag it for a moderator.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T12:10:35-07:00","id":580032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=580001#post580001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm floored that this post got as many likes, as of now, as any other in the thread, and four times as many as the OP.<br /> <br /> Magnum Opus has been respectful with his opinions, explaining them rationally and politely without resorting to insults or snide remarks.<br /> <br /> Your response indirectly accuses him of having a psychotic break from reality and using &quot;tortured logic,&quot; uses sarcasm and a general all-around nasty tone, and somehow people find it adds more to the community and this forum than the entirely reasonable (whether you agree with it or find it entirely 100% true to the RAI or not) OP.<br /> <br /> This is unacceptable.<br /> <br /> I expect better than 4chan when I come to OPP forums.</div> </div> </div> </div>In what way is it unacceptable? I'll give Opus has some points a paranoia aspect on who's a supernatural is tricky to have when you have individuals who can pick out supernaturals almost at a glance, but as others have pointed out Beast aren't alone in possessing that trait they're just the one who have it a power innate to all of them. The thing is other parts of his argument are utterly wrong,* or make no sense like saying Mother's Kiss insults all the other splats because it gives a buff.<br /> <br /> *See repeated comments on Beast Mythos being an override and how Thicker than Blood only provides a decent first impression.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T12:29:40-07:00","id":580062,"title":"","content":"This feels like reading a post about the Strix being the new metaplot. Your concerns over concepts like Family Dinner feel very weak, and Mother's Kiss is a dice bonus on par with taking a specialty or two, I don't really see that much value in it, at least insofar as stealing the spotlight goes.<br /> <br /> The comment about Mage cosmology overwriting everything else is this really old and tired idea that doesn't have any basis in reality. The idea that Beasts <i>believe</i> in a thing called the Dark Mother and have some kind of sympathetic connection to other monsters in no way invalidates any other game line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T15:04:19-07:00","id":580277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=580001#post580001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm floored that this post got as many likes, as of now, as any other in the thread, and four times as many as the OP.<br /> <br /> Magnum Opus has been respectful with his opinions, explaining them rationally and politely without resorting to insults or snide remarks.<br /> <br /> Your response indirectly accuses him of having a psychotic break from reality and using &quot;tortured logic,&quot; uses sarcasm and a general all-around nasty tone, and somehow people find it adds more to the community and this forum than the entirely reasonable (whether you agree with it or find it entirely 100% true to the RAI or not) OP.<br /> <br /> This is unacceptable.<br /> <br /> I expect better than 4chan when I come to OPP forums.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's just avoid reading oblique accusations to each other in posts that make no reference to specific people, shall we? It plunges what can be called a discussion with a passionate tone (both from the OP and some of those who answered, let's be fair) into a way more hostile conversation where we get from the hypothetic and impersonal to a &quot;I will read every sentence and consider it under the worst possible light&quot; crucible.<br /> <br /> After we get past that, I think Magnus Opus spoke in the same absolutes of StSword - they just happen to have diametrical opposite views. I see no insults there and only a minimal amount of sass from both parts, which happens when you believe in your own reasonings. Calling this 4chan is quite an hyperbole. I agree that, on this sort of forums with this sort of discussions, is easy to cross the line and thus I'm not saying we need a thicker skin but we should also be careful not seeing malevolence as soon as the tone rises a bit.<br /> <br /> As for the like thing, well, I think it's merely due to more people agreeing with someone instead of another. Opinion topics tend to work that way, the &quot;I believe this contributes to the community and the discussion&quot; kinda shifts in the background. It's a &quot;this is what I also think&quot; situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 07-05-2015, 06:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T18:36:13-07:00","id":580427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=580001#post580001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magnum Opus has been respectful with his opinions, explaining them rationally and politely without resorting to insults or snide remarks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey Maina?<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers#post579778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's even worse than playing with mages.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers#post579778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could also call this power 'Spotlight Stealer'</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers#post579778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The 'best-friends forever' power which states that Beasts are always on good terms with everyone because reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers#post579778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, Beast, for ruining the scene and grabbing the spotlight again.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers#post579778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wanna know what's even worst?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers#post579778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast suffers the same problem that Mage has: They have the answer to every problem and their Mythos explains everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>None of this is respectful, polite, or not-snide by any stretch of the imagination that would not damn such a claim with faint praise. For your assessment to be accurate would require qualifiers like &quot;He did not directly call people names,&quot; which I'm given to understand is far from the baseline of genteel discourse even by imageboard standards.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your response indirectly accuses him of [\u2026] using &quot;tortured logic,&quot; </div> </div> </div>When you take &quot;Beasts treat virtually all supernatural beings they interact with in a neutral setting as though they had a baseline 'good' or 'average' impression level for the purposes of the Social Maneuvering systems&quot; to mean &quot;Beasts are automatically best friends forever with everyone&quot; because you have constructed a situation wherein you walk up to the antagonist and convince them to go on a coffee date, and when you take &quot;Beasts can recognize the supernatural and distinguish strains of it that they have previously encountered if the target is unveiled or loses a Clash of Wills first&quot; to mean &quot;Beasts autobreak all supernatural attempts at subterfuge that rely on obfuscation of one's nature,&quot; you are contorting the bounds of good-faith reading. This is not debatable, because the latter presentations are flagrantly hostile and based on objective misreadings.<br /> <br /> Overtly incorrect complaints tend to prompt the same reactions as insults because it's the &quot;My grampa weren't no monkey!&quot; of internet argumentation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T18:44:26-07:00","id":580434,"title":"","content":"Yes, well. Nobody expects an internet forum to be a debate club or focused entirely on logic and reason over bias and emotions. I suppose I just draw the line at suggesting that other posters are psychotic and mentally ill. It's cruel and it does a disservice to people actually suffering from mental illness, which is a topic that touches my life on a daily basis. And no, I don't think that's deliberately assuming the worst. &quot;Players who believe what you are posting must be suffering some psychotic break from reality&quot; cannot really be interpreted any better.<br /> <br /> You're right. The OP isn't perfect. The post I responded to just crossed what I felt to be a line that shouldn't be crossed.<br /> <br /> I didn't want to derail, and I originally wasn't going to post any replies anymore for that very purpose, but you have a valid point so I felt I should clarify where my own biases lie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T19:12:40-07:00","id":580446,"title":"","content":"Mother's Kiss: I might have gone hyperbolic with this one, but let's just say that buffs usually don't go as far as &quot;Here's a buff to your VERY EXISTENCE&quot;. They usually stay in a nice little box, such as Combat (D&amp;D Bards and Cahalith) or Stealth, or Social, or whatever. It's not a buff that states that Obfuscate 1 is now perfect invisibility and the next turn to get a +2L to your attack just because a Beast blew a kiss.<br /> <br /> I think the main of my concern is not with each individual powers, but from the fact that ALL Beasts have them built in, unlike Vampires or Mages or whatever you're throwing at me. I never argued that You Are Meat is too strong or that a Makara should not be a giant fish, I argued that innate abilities of a whole splat basically swat away a lot of powers that other people paid for in XP or built-in with their characters.<br /> <br /> I played a Witch in Pathfinder, basically a buff character. I played an Aes Promethean. I played buff-mages in a lot of LARP, but I've never had such a <i>wrong</i> impression of a buff skill as Mother's Kiss. Mind, maybe it's because it seems so trivial for a Beast, whereas a Bard needs to sing for turns on end and a Mage needs to cast and bring forth arcane knowledge and Prometheans need to surge the Pyros through their very being, transmuting chaos in order. A Beast &quot;blows a kiss&quot; and they have a better result.<br /> <br /> Take any movie or cut-scenes from a video game. If the character is faced with a terrible opponent and in the shadows you see another character simply snap his fingers and then the main character defeats his opponent in a few strikes before we see the shadowy figure grin, who has the spotlight? The audience is led to believe that this success had nothing to do with the main character. That is the way I feel about this power. It doesn't turn the protagonist's sword ablaze. It doesn't imbue him with courage. It doesn't make him see the weak spot in his opponent's defense. It simply...Fate victory because reasons and family and stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The comment about Mage cosmology overwriting everything else is this really old and tired idea that doesn't have any basis in reality. The idea that Beasts <i>believe</i> in a thing called the Dark Mother and have some kind of sympathetic connection to other monsters in no way invalidates any other game line. </div> </div> </div>You're right. If we forget that their mythos basically states that Werewolves and Prometheans are brothers, or that the Judges are in fact the sons and daughters of Tiamat. Same goes for Father Wolf, The Principle, The Exarchs, t<i>he whole underworld, t</i><i>he entirety of the Shadow, all the Gentries and Slashers </i>(but not Hunters, because they're just humans, though Cursed humans are descendants).<br /> <br /> Going from there the players either accept that the Dark Mother is real and it overrides their own Mythos, or they flip the bird to the Beast and no one talks about it anymore (which is not better in my oppinion).<br /> <br /> Family Resemblance: It goes beyond Auspex. Auspex tells you if he is or not a Super. FR tells you what monster he is and what he's good at (with an exceptional) <i>and</i> is totally passive. Auspex is once per scene, a single question, binary answer, active, resistable...and is not innate.<br /> <br /> <br /> Final Disclaimer (again): I certainly didn't feel threatened or aggressed in any way in the replies. Sure, some had some punch to them or some sass, but I did too at some points (mainly using hyperboles) and as such think that it's only fair I'm answered in the same way. I'll try and stay in a civil state of communication for as long as possible, and leave if I feel like this discussion is going nowhere fast, or getting too personnal. I am not perfect, we all argue about stuff, and I may be biased toward not liking the splat.<br /> <br /> Then again a lot of people are biased towards liking it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":2589,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","user":"Magnum Opus","date":"that went through at first. 07-05-2015, 10:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T19:22:40-07:00","id":580451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=580446#post580446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're right. If we forget that it basically states that Werewolves and Prometheans are brothers, or that the Judges are in fact the sons and daughters of Tiamat. Same goes for Father Wolf, The Principle, The Exarchs, t<i>he whole underworld, t</i><i>he entirety of the Shadow, all the Gentries and Slashers </i>(but not Hunters, because they're just humans, though Cursed humans are descendants).</div> </div> </div> </div>You're interpreting the whole family thing as a literal relation when we're dealing with the kind of sympathetic magic that underlies pretty much every part of the New World of Darkness cosmology. Relation isn't a matter of literal descent, so much as conceptual similarity. If you're not seeing how all of the creatures suggested to be Kin could share some kind of conceptual sympathy with primordial creatures of fear, I honestly don't know what to tell you.<br /> <br /> You're making the kind of hyperbolic statements that require you to take statements of suggested relation in the book as if they're some kind of literal blood relation Word from God statement, and that's a bad idea with to do with <i>any </i>of the gamelines nevermind how people have been doing it for years with Mage and it was <i>wrong</i>. You're doing the same thing here. Family as a concept for <i>supernatural dream creatures </i>is incredibly abstract and mystical in nature, and looking at the concepts being tossed around, the idea is that Father Wolf and other early creatures share a sympathy with the Dark Mother and with Beasts that they interpret as a familial bond.<br /> <br /> If you take every description of mythic prehistory as absolutely literal, every game line you can think of is gonna get pretty ridiculous.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T19:27:56-07:00","id":580454,"title":"","content":"Sure, but then if it's not a literal Family Bond, why is the God-Machine out of the equation? It does have a f***ton of relationships with primal fears, doesn't it?<br /> <br /> I get your point though and will have another look at the history of the dark mother with a more....philosophical eye, I suppose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T19:48:18-07:00","id":580472,"title":"","content":"I don't have a direct answer for you, there. I imagine it has to do with the artificial nature of the God-Machine and its creation. If you'll notice, a theme in the metaphysics of the game (particularly in the Neolithic Mage setting that's upcoming) it seems like civilization and people and the state they're in affects the Supernatural. Father Wolf seems to grow weaker and more haggard as Humanity moves away from our previous hunting lifestyle to an agricultural one. I imagine the move into civilization affected people's relationship with the Primordial Dream and the Lessons.<br /> <br /> I mean, there's also the bit about how the Primordial Dream is, well, <i>primordial </i>and seems diametrically imposed to the incredibly complex systems of human civilization, as it's a primal thing that touches us in the lizard brain and all that. The God-Machine is representative of incredibly complex systems that we create and consequently lose control of, because we know longer understand them. I'm certain someone else can phrase it better, but the sort of concept of the Primordial Dream is based firmly in primal, basic, essentially human things, and the God-Machine seems in many ways to be an opposing force to that.<br /> <br /> I imagine that's something they're tapping into with Demons <i>not </i>being kin. Honestly, it sets them up with a sort of unique hook that makes them more interesting when engaged in a Beast game than if they were just considered another source of Kin, and being that they have the connection to the God-Machine, it just makes sense that of all the splats you'd pick to be the exception, it'd be Demons.<br /> <br /> <br /> All that said, I'll say I'm not a huge fan of Beast or its crossover, but I think <i>this </i>reason is a very silly one to be critical of it for, because it's based on the same kind of misconceptions that have been bandied about on other websites about Mage, and it's like a red herring of criticism when there are other much more legitimate critiques to discuss. So that's where I'm coming from with this. I think it's totally fair to not like Beasts for crossover, but the reasons you're bringing to the table seem pretty silly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T19:53:02-07:00","id":580474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=580451#post580451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you take every description of mythic prehistory as absolutely literal, every game line you can think of is gonna get pretty ridiculous.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or Glorantha. Glorantha seems sane. Ish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T19:55:28-07:00","id":580476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=580472#post580472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All that said, I'll say I'm not a huge fan of Beast or its crossover, but I think <i>this </i>reason is a very silly one to be critical of it for, because it's based on the same kind of misconceptions that have been bandied about on other websites about Mage, and it's like a red herring of criticism when there are other much more legitimate critiques to discuss. So that's where I'm coming from with this. I think it's totally fair to not like Beasts for crossover, but the reasons you're bringing to the table seem pretty silly.</div> </div> </div> </div>May I suggest closing topic then? Since visibly my arguments are considered silly or unreasonable by most here and I feel like this thread was a bad idea to start with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T19:59:51-07:00","id":580478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=580454#post580454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but then if it's not a literal Family Bond, why is the God-Machine out of the equation? It does have a f***ton of relationships with primal fears, doesn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>The part where it's a massive hypercomplicated secrecy-oriented emotion-suppressing blind-idiot law of physics that's occasionally implied to be some kind of metaphysical retrovirus whose probably-unwilling concessions to entropy are described as &quot;defect[ors] to humanity&quot; that only possess innate metaphysical connection to themselves and their own desires probably has something to do with its lack of relation to the fundamental (i.e. cosmologically simple) horrormonsters that emerge from the very oldest parts of the human psyche.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465635-replacing-the-god-machine?p=470499#post470499\">The ability to cast &quot;God&quot; as an invader</a> also feeds nicely into the matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T20:00:15-07:00","id":580479,"title":"","content":"As a Mage my auto response to a Beast would be a condescending pat on the head along with an, &quot;Aw, he thinks he <i>knows</i> things! How cute!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T20:09:40-07:00","id":580482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=580446#post580446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mother's Kiss: I might have gone hyperbolic with this one, but let's just say that buffs usually don't go as far as &quot;Here's a buff to your VERY EXISTENCE&quot;. They usually stay in a nice little box, such as Combat (D&amp;D Bards and Cahalith) or Stealth, or Social, or whatever. It's not a buff that states that Obfuscate 1 is now perfect invisibility and the next turn to get a +2L to your attack just because a Beast blew a kiss.<br /> <br /> I think the main of my concern is not with each individual powers, but from the fact that ALL Beasts have them built in, unlike Vampires or Mages or whatever you're throwing at me. I never argued that You Are Meat is too strong or that a Makara should not be a giant fish, I argued that innate abilities of a whole splat basically swat away a lot of powers that other people paid for in XP or built-in with their characters.<br /> <br /> I played a Witch in Pathfinder, basically a buff character. I played an Aes Promethean. I played buff-mages in a lot of LARP, but I've never had such a <i>wrong</i> impression of a buff skill as Mother's Kiss. Mind, maybe it's because it seems so trivial for a Beast, whereas a Bard needs to sing for turns on end and a Mage needs to cast and bring forth arcane knowledge and Prometheans need to surge the Pyros through their very being, transmuting chaos in order. A Beast &quot;blows a kiss&quot; and they have a better result.<br /> <br /> (...)<br /> <br /> Family Resemblance: It goes beyond Auspex. Auspex tells you if he is or not a Super. FR tells you what monster he is and what he's good at (with an exceptional) <i>and</i> is totally passive. Auspex is once per scene, a single question, binary answer, active, resistable...and is not innate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you actually read the effects of Mother's Kiss? Because it costs 1 Willpower, is resisted by Supernatural Tolerance, and at most grants the target a few <i>non-renewable </i>dice that you can distribute between <i>rolled </i><i>powers</i>, or a <i>small narrative boost </i>if they don't have dice pools. Forget spotlight stealing, you are still completely overplaying the strength of the ability. Are you bothered by the fact that it's a very flexible buff that could bring the use of certain powers from uncertain to reliable* at low Experience levels if the conditions are right?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">*And this only as many times as the Beast can afford to use Willpower.**<br /> **And if the benefactor invests the full buff into a single power use, they might get what, like 3 extra dice if the roll went well? The same bonus they could get by <i>spending Willpower themselves.</i></span><br /> <br /> Auspex can also give you more significant information than Family Resemblance in a much broader scope if you ask the right questions, and is absolutely not limited to binary responses. But that really doesn't matter because they're powers with very different purviews.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 07-05-2015, 11:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T20:27:42-07:00","id":580489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers#post579778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">. . .<br /> <br /> <b>Skeleton Key</b><br /> A power which allow Beasts to almost instantly open gateways to any other world as far as they are aware that such gateways exist. So say a pack of werewolves want to bring the Beast and a few wolf-blooded and maybe a Vampire with them to hunt in the Hisil, the Ritemaster telling them that it will take some time since he has to open the gateway to all of them and that they'll have to take part in a rite that will last an hour, maybe more. And then the Beast just goes &quot;Dude don't, I got this!&quot; and opens the gate. Thanks, Beast, for ruining the scene and grabbing the spotlight again. . .</div> </div> </div> </div>As <b>Beast</b> stands now (barring further rewrites), I don't think you could use Skeleton Key in that scenario - at least not if you wanted to catch anything. If you're hunting (whether to actually bring back game, or just to see the local wildlife in their natural habitat), you have to be stealthy. The slightest noise will scare the game. Even something as simple as a twig cracking will send deer running, for example. <br /> <br /> And Skeleton Key is not a subtle power. Its tantamount to a SWAT team breaking in the door, as the Beast rips the gate open, &quot;tearing the door off its hinges&quot;. A process that is immediately obvious to anything on the other side. Any animal, spirit, or (wise) human for miles around would run or hide, long before the hunters were able to cross over. So, assuming you want to catch anything, you'd still need the Ritemaster. <br /> <br /> Personally, I see Skeleton Key being used more as a pursuit power. Where an enemy tries to ditch the Beast for another plane of existence, and the Beast responds by going all Jack Nicholson (in <i>The Shining</i>). Axing in the door (err. . . gate), and shouting, &quot;Here's Johnny!&quot;. Or breaking into an enemy's otherworldly stronghold - we've all had that nightmare where, no matter how hard you try, you can't get all the doors shut before the monster gets in, right?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T20:28:24-07:00","id":580491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=580479#post580479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a Mage my auto response to a Beast would be a condescending pat on the head along with an, &quot;Aw, he thinks he <i>knows</i> things! How cute!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>And then I, as a beast, would be forced to show the Mage exactly how little he knows about the World of Darkness. And then chew upon his face for being so prideful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T20:30:56-07:00","id":580494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=580491#post580491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And then I, as a beast, would be forced to show the Mage exactly how little he knows about the World of Darkness. And then chew upon his face for being so prideful.</div> </div> </div> </div>You would try, my friend, you would certainly try.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T20:35:24-07:00","id":580499,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=580489#post580489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Skeleton Key is not a subtle power. Its tantamount to a SWAT team breaking in the door, as the Beast rips the gate open, &quot;tearing the door off its hinges&quot;. A process that is immediately obvious to anything on the other side. Any animal, spirit, or (wise) human for miles around would run or hide, long before the hunters were able to cross over. So, assuming you want to catch anything, you'd still need the Ritemaster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for clearing that up. We used it wrong in our current game it would seem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T20:53:26-07:00","id":580507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=580446#post580446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mother's Kiss: I might have gone hyperbolic with this one, but let's just say that buffs usually don't go as far as &quot;Here's a buff to your VERY EXISTENCE&quot;. They usually stay in a nice little box, such as Combat (D&amp;D Bards and Cahalith) or Stealth, or Social, or whatever. It's not a buff that states that Obfuscate 1 is now perfect invisibility and the next turn to get a +2L to your attack just because a Beast blew a kiss.<br /> <br /> I think the main of my concern is not with each individual powers, but from the fact that ALL Beasts have them built in, unlike Vampires or Mages or whatever you're throwing at me. I never argued that You Are Meat is too strong or that a Makara should not be a giant fish, I argued that innate abilities of a whole splat basically swat away a lot of powers that other people paid for in XP or built-in with their characters.<br /> <br /> I played a Witch in Pathfinder, basically a buff character. I played an Aes Promethean. I played buff-mages in a lot of LARP, but I've never had such a <i>wrong</i> impression of a buff skill as Mother's Kiss. Mind, maybe it's because it seems so trivial for a Beast, whereas a Bard needs to sing for turns on end and a Mage needs to cast and bring forth arcane knowledge and Prometheans need to surge the Pyros through their very being, transmuting chaos in order. A Beast &quot;blows a kiss&quot; and they have a better result.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually its a dice pool for one scene that depletes, by however many dice are spent, when used because it can only fuel supernatural powers. Its also somewhat variable in how much of a pool it gives, so while it potentially can give a large dice pool of lets say 10 ( assuming the hypothetical Beast has integrity and satiety of 5 each, the supernatural resistance stat of the recipient was 3, and the recipient has family ties for an additional 3. Which requires all of those dice to come out as successes for it to happen) more likely it will yield a dice pool of three or four most of the time. This can certainly be useful, but its hardly a snap of the fingers and then the enemy falls. Also it requires the Beast to do some bleeding while speaking the target's name, while not a lot it is a bit more than just blowing a kiss or snapping your fingers. Really, to me it reads less as &quot;You don't stand a chance without me, so I'll give you power to win,&quot; and more, &quot;You have the best chance of any of us to pull this off, here take some of my power just in case.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=580446#post580446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take any movie or cut-scenes from a video game. If the character is faced with a terrible opponent and in the shadows you see another character simply snap his fingers and then the main character defeats his opponent in a few strikes before we see the shadowy figure grin, who has the spotlight? The audience is led to believe that this success had nothing to do with the main character. That is the way I feel about this power. It doesn't turn the protagonist's sword ablaze. It doesn't imbue him with courage. It doesn't make him see the weak spot in his opponent's defense. It simply...Fate victory because reasons and family and stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div> Or the Shonen action thing where the hero stands up and keeps fighting past their limit because they saw their friends/ loved ones and refused to fall.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=580446#post580446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're right. If we forget that their mythos basically states that Werewolves and Prometheans are brothers, or that the Judges are in fact the sons and daughters of Tiamat. Same goes for Father Wolf, The Principle, The Exarchs, t<i>he whole underworld, t</i><i>he entirety of the Shadow, all the Gentries and Slashers </i>(but not Hunters, because they're just humans, though Cursed humans are descendants).</div> </div> </div> </div> First in a literal sense Beasts view Prometheans as the adopted kids in the family, so the mythos doesn't literally state the Garou are brothers with the Prometheans. On to the next part the Beasts believe that the supernaturals eventually crop back from primordial fear, which some Beasts believe may actually be the Dark Mother and others think she might have just been the first being to come from it, and things have descended and refined from there. Meaning if you decided to take the Dark Mother thing as an absolute that no other splat could refuse or contradict you would be basically going off the idea that if you go back far enough in the evolutionary tree and all mammals came from the same organism. (Which does very little in allowing anyone I know to claim their cat/dog as kin.)<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=580446#post580446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Going from there the players either accept that the Dark Mother is real and it overrides their own Mythos, or they flip the bird to the Beast and no one talks about it anymore (which is not better in my oppinion).</div> </div> </div> </div> Or they can assume its what the Beasts think and may be accurate as far as Beasts think but doesn't work out as well since the Changeling is pretty sure her powers and form are a side-effect of getting dragged off to another world and becoming the plaything of insane fey for who knows how long.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=580446#post580446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Family Resemblance: It goes beyond Auspex. Auspex tells you if he is or not a Super. FR tells you what monster he is and what he's good at (with an exceptional) <i>and</i> is totally passive. Auspex is once per scene, a single question, binary answer, active, resistable...and is not innate.</div> </div> </div> </div> The innate thing is a bit more to deal with, but any supernatural attempt to camouflage<br /> means it goes to a contest of wills. This means that the only easily identifiable supernaturals are the ones who are putting no more effort into hiding themselves than making it so mundane humans don't know what they are. Plus the exceptional only tells you what their best supernatural power is in the vaguest sense i.e. a vampire with high celerity will give you the impression of &quot;vampire decently hungry and amazingly fast.&quot; Which of course also assumes you know the sign means vampire, so if its your first encounter or you've never seen anything to suggest that the smell of blood and grave dirt means vampire, it just means you smell people that reek of grave dirt and blood, but you don't know what it means beyond them not being baseline human.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3400,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","user":"nalak42","date":". 07-05-2015, 11:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T22:42:14-07:00","id":580557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=580494#post580494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You would try, my friend, you would certainly try.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note to self: If I play a Beast or a Mage, be willing to sit down and talk cosmology theory and work with the other and try to come up with more complete models of reality over banana splits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-05T23:48:01-07:00","id":580583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=580557#post580557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note to self: If I play a Beast or a Mage, be willing to sit down and talk cosmology theory and work with the other and try to come up with more complete models of reality over banana splits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bah, that's the <i>boring</i> way! It isn't fun until someone has their innards splattered across the pavement. Afterwards you have to piece the other guy back together and extract information from their remains, that's how you really solve origin mysteries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 07-06-2015, 02:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T00:07:03-07:00","id":580594,"title":"","content":"The only thing i can say about Thicker than Water is... Aren't Afew People/Supernaturals gonna have a Bad second impression. Or Feel like they've been Whammied?<br /> <br /> It Gives a good First impression.. but so Does giving someone a Roofie, and people ARE going to notice that they Remember not being Afraid/Angry/Blindsided Etc by this Creature that claims it's Family... Demons of the Inferno can do that to too get into your Head. Alot of People who are Paranoid WILL Find a Reason to Instantly Hate them once out of the Beast's &quot;Range&quot; or Personal space.<br /> <br /> But that's just me...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T02:13:53-07:00","id":580670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=580594#post580594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only thing i can say about Thicker than Water is... Aren't Afew People/Supernaturals gonna have a Bad second impression. Or Feel like they've been Whammied?<br /> <br /> It Gives a good First impression.. but so Does giving someone a Roofie, and people ARE going to notice that they Remember not being Afraid/Angry/Blindsided Etc by this Creature that claims it's Family... Demons of the Inferno can do that to too get into your Head. Alot of People who are Paranoid WILL Find a Reason to Instantly Hate them once out of the Beast's &quot;Range&quot; or Personal space.<br /> <br /> But that's just me...</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay first that is a horrible analogy. Seriously dude the hell.<br /> <br /> But lets get past the analogy and correct your misconception. First Thicker than Water operates mostly in a vacuum ie they have a good first impression of you until they have data to compare it with. This means there is literally nothing stopping any other supernatural from deciding they think a Beast is scum/stupid/dangerous/annoying/in need of a good killing in the first conversation or before depending on what you said and did during the first meeting. It just means that they will start off the encounter inclined towards the idea that you're an alright sort. This isn't the Beast going into someone's head an tinkering with their brain to make them think that. All the power means is they have a quality that slightly nudges them into the good graces of other supernaturals. <br /> <br /> Second unless a Beast is actively using an atavism or the other supernatural is using a power to let them see what the Beast really is they'll likely assume the Beast is a normal human. So it isn't going to notice that they encountered some weird creature claiming to be family unless the Beast decides to tell it they're family in the first meeting and guess what the data in the supernatural's head is probably going to lead to &quot;got it this person is nuts.&quot; It doesn't negate other emotional states; if a Changeling is freaking out from a pursuit its been running from when a Beast shows up the Changeling doesn't stop being utterly terrified. Best case scenario the Changeling is hoping the Beast isn't a threat because the Changeling has enough problems already and is slightly more inclined to believe the Beast says it isn't there to hurt the Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T02:21:14-07:00","id":580671,"title":"","content":"The good first impression lasts until the Beast does something to screw it up, like abusing their trust or being hostile. At which point the supernatural has actual reason to be miffed with the beast.<br /> <br /> Blood Thicker than Water doesn't have a range limit, it works through an email from the other side of the planet just as well as right next to the supernatural.<br /> <br /> Lastly, how can one honestly detect that their mind has been whammied when they haven't been? Social maneuvering is incapable of getting npcs or pcs to do anything they aren't willing to do.<br /> <br /> So someone so dang paranoid that a beast being able to convince them to come to a BBQ at his house is cause for alarm is so paranoid they wouldn't agree to come to the BBQ in the first place. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T02:37:19-07:00","id":580674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=580670#post580670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay first that is a horrible analogy. Seriously dude the hell.<br /> <br /> But lets get past the analogy and correct your misconception. First Thicker than Water operates mostly in a vacuum ie they have a good first impression of you until they have data to compare it with. This means there is literally nothing stopping any other supernatural from deciding they think a Beast is scum/stupid/dangerous/annoying/in need of a good killing in the first conversation or before depending on what you said and did during the first meeting. It just means that they will start off the encounter inclined towards the idea that you're an alright sort. This isn't the Beast going into someone's head an tinkering with their brain to make them think that. All the power means is they have a quality that slightly nudges them into the good graces of other supernaturals.<br /> <br /> Second unless a Beast is actively using an atavism or the other supernatural is using a power to let them see what the Beast really is they'll likely assume the Beast is a normal human. So it isn't going to notice that they encountered some weird creature claiming to be family unless the Beast decides to tell it they're family in the first meeting and guess what the data in the supernatural's head is probably going to lead to &quot;got it this person is nuts.&quot; It doesn't negate other emotional states; if a Changeling is freaking out from a pursuit its been running from when a Beast shows up the Changeling doesn't stop being utterly terrified. Best case scenario the Changeling is hoping the Beast isn't a threat because the Changeling has enough problems already and is slightly more inclined to believe the Beast says it isn't there to hurt the Changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Bad analogy, What i mean is What is too stop someone who is Natural Paranoid to THINK that this &quot;Thing&quot; has caused them to like them. A Good First Impression on someone who is mistrusting of others would cause a Bigger bad Impression when that person causes suspsision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T03:03:54-07:00","id":580679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=580674#post580674\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah, Bad analogy, What i mean is What is too stop someone who is Natural Paranoid to THINK that this &quot;Thing&quot; has caused them to like them. A Good First Impression on someone who is mistrusting of others would cause a Bigger bad Impression when that person causes suspsision.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's what they call extenuating circumstances. As the pdf puts it the ST is always within their rights to modify how it plays out based on relevant factors, so if there's a character who is so insanely paranoid that they think liking someone means obviously something bad has happened then yeah that'll happen. The thing is again Thicker than Water doesn't apply throughout the entire thing its just a starting point from a standing of not having information. Ie a Beast running into an exceptionally anti-social Garou at the local grocery store and politely asking if they could hand them one of the boxes of cereal that the Garou is standing in front of has a higher chance of succeeding for the Beast than a normal human and might not end with the Garou thinking the Beast is a worthless piece of crap like it might a normal person doing the same thing.<br /> <br /> To put it another way, you seem to be thinking of Thicker than Water as a passive mind control effect. As the pdf puts it,<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Note, too, that Thicker Than Water doesn\u2019t give the Beast\u2019s player any bonus on Social actions beyond Social maneuvering. It simply means that if the Beast reaches out to her kin in a respectful manner, the other being is generally willing to receive it. Thicker Than Water is not a mind control power, but merely a social lubricant. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T03:28:17-07:00","id":580726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=580679#post580679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To put it another way, you seem to be thinking of Thicker than Water as a passive mind control effect. As the pdf puts it,</div> </div> </div> </div>So while it isn't exactly mind control it is still similar to alcohol or anything else that influences people and makes them act in a manner that they wouldn't normally. So while RickmanUK's analogy wasn't exactly a pleasant one, it wasn't really that far off. Thicker than Water is like supernaturally drugging whoever you're talking to so that they become more receptive to what you want.<br /> <br /> That said, it, like all of the other Kinship abilities are all still supernatural effects as far as I can tell. So any power/ability that can detect such things should still give people who possess them a heads up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T06:28:27-07:00","id":580871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=579872#post579872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast has far less in the way of plot hooks and even just <i>setting</i> than the other lines; which leaves the impression that you're supposed to lean towards using other gamelines to fill in the gaps.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is one reason I like the idea of many Beasts going through life much as mortals do; it makes the blue books their setting (and squares with how a lot of them feed via what amount to ordinary human activities).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=579901#post579901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the part of the mythos that the OP is referring to is the idea that all supernatural beings (with a few possible exceptions) are in some way descendants of the same Dark Mother that Beasts claim as their progenitor, a proposition that Werewolves and Mages, at the very least, would find objectionable.</div> </div> </div> </div>As of second edition, werewolves aren't averse to the idea that Mother Moon has descendants beside themselves (that's one theory for what idigam are). If she interbred with a spirit of that dream world Beasts go on about, then maybe Beasts are the result, who's to say? Does that mean Mother Moon's the Dark Mother, or that Mother Moon and the Dark Mother bred to make the Beasts, again no one knows, and does it really matter? My point being that links like this don't mean one game line &quot;wins,&quot; which seems to be a common idea about such things.<br /> <br /> And as you say, Beasts don't have a lot of evidence for their mythology.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=580726#post580726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So while it isn't exactly mind control it is still similar to alcohol or anything else that influences people and makes them act in a manner that they wouldn't normally.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or it's akin to being attractive, charismatic, or a demeanour that makes people feel comfortable. None of those are even vaguely mind control, but they tend to garner good first impressions for the people who have them. Until they mess them up. Beasts have an air about them that's comfortable for supernaturals - if they live up to it, they can make friends more easily, but it doesn't control anyone - if they don't live up to it, they won't get any friends for it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T06:33:57-07:00","id":580874,"title":"","content":"I took it as beasts having a sort of instinct for what a splat considers non-threatening behavior. You're not influencing them, you're sliding into cracks that already exist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T06:40:55-07:00","id":580882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=580446#post580446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the main of my concern is not with each individual powers, but from the fact that ALL Beasts have them built in, unlike Vampires or Mages or whatever you're throwing at me. I never argued that You Are Meat is too strong or that a Makara should not be a giant fish, I argued that innate abilities of a whole splat basically swat away a lot of powers that other people paid for in XP or built-in with their characters.</div> </div> </div> </div> Mages and Changelings need to pay for abilities that let them enter a berserker-like state, while vamps and wolves get it for free. Vamps and wolves need to pay for the ability to sense other supernaturals or magic, but mages get Mage Sight stuff innately. Changelings can make pledges, while mages need to invest in Fate and vamps need to use Invictus Oaths for an equivalent. Don't get me started on innate versus purchased healing abilities.<br /> <br /> All this is just part of every different game's niches. Each of the supernaturals are better at some things than other supernaturals. One of Beast: the Primordial's niches is &quot;making crossover friends.&quot; Furthermore, that's pretty much the extent of a Beast's innate abilities - facilitating crossover play. Their only innate ability that somehow doesn't relate to dealing with other supers? Invoking Lair traits. That's it. <br /> <br /> Vampires are all about the physical and mind controls. Werewolves hunt. Mages study. Prometheans survive, changelings have wishes and illusions, demons are the perfect spies. Every game has its niche with a wealth of innate abilities to support that niche, and you are begrudging the Beast their niche. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Take any movie or cut-scenes from a video game. If the character is faced with a terrible opponent and in the shadows you see another character simply snap his fingers and then the main character defeats his opponent in a few strikes before we see the shadowy figure grin, who has the spotlight? </div> </div> </div> Actually, its the main character who gets the spotlight. There's a lot of dismissive attitudes for support characters. I mean, really. Do you think that the person who makes all the hero's magical equipment gets any attention? Or the holy one who blesses the main character's weapons to smite evil? Of course not. The focus is always on the main character and their skill at using the supporter's magic, and the supporter fades into the background for the final battle as the main character flexes their new muscles. I really have no idea where you get the idea its anything but this - I've never a cut scene, movie, anime, or show where support characters are given heavy spotlight. Its the one who actually takes direct action that gets the recognition.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're right. If we forget that their mythos basically states that Werewolves and Prometheans are brothers, or that the Judges are in fact the sons and daughters of Tiamat. Same goes for Father Wolf, The Principle, The Exarchs, t<i>he whole underworld, t</i><i>he entirety of the Shadow, all the Gentries and Slashers </i>(but not Hunters, because they're just humans, though Cursed humans are descendants). </div> </div> </div> Actually, you really need to read far more in depth. Others have covered this topic in more depth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Family Resemblance: It goes beyond Auspex. </div> </div> </div> But not Mage Sight. Furthermore, Auspex can pierce supernatural concealment, Family Resemblance can't.<br /> <br /> And why do you insist on comparing apples to oranges? Why does it matter if vampires need to buy a power? Beasts are built to fascilitate crossover play, vampires are not. Vampires are built with the ability to bloodbond people, be immortal, and have strong physical and healing abilities, while Beasts can't. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am not perfect, we all argue about stuff, and I may be biased toward not liking the splat.<br /> <br /> Then again a lot of people are biased towards liking it. </div> </div> </div> A bit out of context, but let me say that this is about your conclusions being in a rather false direction, and not bias. You are making sweeping generalities that simply don't make sense. Its fine if you don't like the game. But your conclusions are just so wildly off base that it just doesn't make logical sense, and you are misquoting how the rules work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T06:49:25-07:00","id":580893,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=579872#post579872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast has far less in the way of plot hooks and even just <i>setting</i> than the other lines; which leaves the impression that you're supposed to lean towards using other gamelines to fill in the gaps.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=580871#post580871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is one reason I like the idea of many Beasts going through life much as mortals do; it makes the blue books their setting (and squares with how a lot of them feed via what amount to ordinary human activities).</div> </div> </div> </div> Beast is designed as a crossover game. Not running out to meet other supernaturals is like a vampire without the political squabbles of the All Night Society, or mages without a Mystery to investigate, or forbidding wolves to hunt.<br /> <br /> Its what they <i>do</i>. Wolves hunt, vamps suck blood, mages investigate. And Beasts seek other supernaturals for their family. Its not filling in cracks. Its not about living like a mortal. <i>The crossover stuff is a major part of the game by design</i>. Its something Beasts are actively drawn to do. Its a major feature of the game.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T06:56:53-07:00","id":580903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=580893#post580893\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beast is designed as a crossover game. Not running out to meet other supernaturals is like a vampire without the political squabbles of the All Night Society, or mages without a Mystery to investigate, or forbidding wolves to hunt.<br /> <br /> Its what they <i>do</i>. Wolves hunt, vamps suck blood, mages investigate. And Beasts seek other supernaturals for their family. Its not filling in cracks. Its not about living like a mortal. <i>The crossover stuff is a major part of the game by design</i>. Its something Beasts are actively drawn to do. Its a major feature of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like the crossover stuff. But I also like the idea of it as an extension to the way (player character) mortals also dig into the dark corners of their world.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T07:29:23-07:00","id":580929,"title":"","content":"Vampires without the All-Night Society is a game similar to Interview with a Vampire, a game of dark descent into inhumanity.<br /> Werewolves without the hunt is a game of loss of control, of exploring a dark and twisted world and of making sure your friends and family don't get hurt by your very nature<br /> Mages without a Mystery is a game of god-like hubris and power.<br /> Changelings without the Courts is a game of trauma, trying to reassemble the pieces of your reality and getting a real life back.<br /> <br /> I don't see why these concepts are wrong, so why would Beast be wrong without Crossover? It would simply be a game of Endless Hunger...as stated on the cover of the book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T07:40:39-07:00","id":580940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=580726#post580726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So while it isn't exactly mind control it is still similar to alcohol or anything else that influences people and makes them act in a manner that they wouldn't normally.<br /> <b>*snip*</b><br /> That said, it, like all of the other Kinship abilities are all still supernatural effects as far as I can tell. So any power/ability that can detect such things should still give people who possess them a heads up.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it doesn't. Thicker Than Water helps to prevent you from appearing instantly threatening to an otherwise neutral party, it won't do a bit of good if the person you're approaching is prone to being paranoid toward <i>everyone</i>. Similarly, if someone is a raging supernatural xenophobe, their default behavior for non-(vampire, werebeast, sentient potato chip) is still 'AAAAAKILLITWITHFIRE'. A Pure werewolf isn't going to immediately think you're a Forsaken ally without reason, but if they just saw you BBQing with the local pack then the best you can hope for is an explanation of <i>why</i> they're gutting you.<br /> <br /> To use a real-world example, think of it as a particularly affable black guy starting a conversation with a hardcore white supremacist. The Klansman type's internal response is going to be something along the lines of 'well, he seems like he might be a decent enough person if he weren't a (insert slur of choice here)'.<br /> <br /> As far as Thicker Than Water registering as a supernatural ability, I would say that it's just an innate part of who and what the Beast is, and doesn't show up as distinct from their just standing around. It isn't a power you actively use, after all. I doubt that the Beasts are even aware that Thicker Than Water exists as a discrete ability, and most would probably be confused if someone accused them of using some kind of magic or other influence. <br /> <br /> If I were going to define it in in-character terms (because I'm the kind of person who usually does) I'd say that what's probably happening is that on a subconscious level, the other critter is sensing the Beast's presence in the Primordial Nightmare and the sliver of recognition is enough to prevent them from feeling <i>completely</i> like a stranger. They are fears given flesh, how unfamiliar can they <i>really</i> be? Who has never been afraid of powerlessness, of the unknown, of judgement or pain or disfigurement?<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Hey man, got a light?&quot; Jake drifted up and leaned back against the concrete wall of an office building next to an unfamiliar vampire. The pale man had been watching surruptitiously watching the same apartment window for half an hour, waiting for the lights to go out.<br /> <br /> The vampire barely glanced at him, grunting &quot;Nah, I don't smoke anymore. Do you mind? I'm waitin' for someone.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Mmyeah, 'bout that...&quot; Jake pulled the cigarette out of the corner of his mouth and pocketed it. &quot;Don't freak out, or they'll notice. Nice an' calm here, just a couple guys getting some air and bitching about the weather. There's a pair of vampire hunters up there, just waiting for you to walk into their trap.&quot;<br /> <br /> The vampire froze completely for a moment, stopping in mid-breath, and then slowly turned it's head toward him. &quot;Oh?&quot; It's eyes narrowed and glimmered with an almost invisible bloody light for a moment. &quot;You aren't kindred. What makes you think..&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;That you won't decide I know too much to be healthy? A little gratitude'd be nice, for a start.&quot; Jake shrugged and met the vampire's eyes. &quot;Anyway, you wouldn't want to start a brawl 30 feet from a bunch of nutjobs with molotovs and crossbows, would you? Let's go grab a bite someplace with better reviews, we can talk about it over dinner.&quot;<br /> <br /> ---</i><br /> <br /> (pardon the artistic license on Auspex, I know it doesn't usually look like anything.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T07:58:33-07:00","id":580949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=580903#post580903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the crossover stuff. But I also like the idea of it as an extension to the way (player character) mortals also dig into the dark corners of their world.</div> </div> </div> </div> Crossover isn't really part of mortal chronicles. It is, however, a major part of Beast chronicles. Its the difference between adding flavor by sprinkling in spices, and having those spices being part of the recipe to begin with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=580929#post580929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires without the All-Night Society is a game similar to Interview with a Vampire, a game of dark descent into inhumanity.<br /> Werewolves without the hunt is a game of loss of control, of exploring a dark and twisted world and of making sure your friends and family don't get hurt by your very nature<br /> Mages without a Mystery is a game of god-like hubris and power.<br /> Changelings without the Courts is a game of trauma, trying to reassemble the pieces of your reality and getting a real life back.<br /> <br /> I don't see why these concepts are wrong, so why would Beast be wrong without Crossover? It would simply be a game of Endless Hunger...as stated on the cover of the book.</div> </div> </div> </div> First, let me say that Interview with a Vampire DID have a vampire society that the main characters interacted with. So that's actually a very bad example. Courts aren't the defining aspects of CtL - the defining feature is getting your life back from your abuser. Your counterpoint should be about changelings that don't care about reclaiming their lives. Mages kinda need mysteries, because without them, there is no God-Like power to reach. One comes with the other.<br /> <br /> Next, let me say that there's nothing <i>wrong</i>, per say, but its not the way the default. There's a reason I said it was like Vampire without All Night Society. The politics is the default, but its possible to do other things. When I'm sitting down to a game of Vampire, I'm going to assume politics and covenants are in; that's kind of the general understanding of the game. Same thing with BtP.<br /> <br /> Beasts seeking out other supernaturals is the default plot of the game. You can run without the other supers, but that's like cutting huge chunks out of the game to do it. Crossover isn't filling gaps in. They're the bricks and stones that make up the house, and you're making gaps by pulling it out. So, it is viable, but you're missing a huge chunk of the game that people should. If you invite people to play a game of Beast, they should be sitting down with the expectation that crossover will be there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T08:26:22-07:00","id":580971,"title":"","content":"To sum it up, can we say that my disliking of the crossover elements seems to come from a different focus for the games?<br /> <br /> I argue that Beast's focus should be about the Endless Hunger, fulfilling your desires and being rather selfish in your decisions while trying to create your own family, be it with mortals or with monsters. Which makes all these powers superfluous and unnecessary in my opinion, thus out of context, thus overpowered (as if I told you that Changelings regenerated all bashing and lethal every round because of their Fairy Tale powers, or that a Mummy could eat a mortal to regain fuel)<br /> <br /> Most seem to argue that Beast is about tagging along other Supers and exploring the World of Darkness. In that light the powers might be more appropriate, allowing a Beast to cross between worlds, help their brethren and spot the different societies while focusing on the other gameline's &quot;hunger&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":2589,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","user":"Magnum Opus","date":". 07-06-2015, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T08:50:41-07:00","id":580985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=580971#post580971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To sum it up, can we say that my disliking of the crossover elements seems to come from a different focus for the games?<br /> <br /> I argue that Beast's focus should be about the Endless Hunger, fulfilling your desires and being rather selfish in your decisions while trying to create your own family, be it with mortals or with monsters. Which makes all these powers superfluous and unnecessary in my opinion, thus out of context, thus overpowered;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that everyone has a diffrent view of Beast seeing as people have been talking about non stop and will probaly coninue even when the game is released but my main question is how can you be selfish while trying to create a family? doesn't that go against the main concept of family?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T08:52:04-07:00","id":580986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=580971#post580971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To sum it up, my disliking of the crossover elements seems to come from a different focus for the games.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's unfortunate, because &quot;Choosing your Family&quot; is a focus of the game. I think its clear that Beast just isn't a game for you. Crossover is a major part of the design, and you seem to be falling on the &quot;not&quot; part of &quot;like it or not.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I argue that Beast's focus should be about the Endless Hunger, fulfilling your desires and being rather selfish in your decisions while trying to create your own family, be it with mortals or with monsters. Which makes all these powers superfluous and unnecessary in my opinion, thus out of context, thus overpowered (as if I told you that Changelings regenerated all bashing and lethal every round because of their Fairy Tale powers, or that a Mummy could eat a mortal to regain fuel) </div> </div> </div> 1) Beast can be about more than one thing. Its just as much about choosing your family as it is about hungers. In fact, the crossover <i>helps</i> with the Hunger thing, because you're taking part in feeding lots of different kinds of hunger, opening new avenues to explore.<br /> <br /> 2) Even if we assume they're not necessary, unnecessary powers do not automatically equate to being overpowered. Mother's Kiss is, by no means, overpowered in the slightest. Spending 1 willpower AND spilling blood to have the ability to make a team work action for magic? That's not even close to being powerful. This is where I take issue with your conclusions - you don't like them, I get it, but that doesn't make them overpowered.<br /> <br /> Overpowered is primarily about mechanics with unbalanced effects and numbers, and can be fixed by tweaking said numbers. Unthematic is a question about if its appropriate to have anything like it, with any numbers at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most seem to argue that Beast is about tagging along other Supers and exploring the World of Darkness. In that light the powers might be more appropriate, allowing a Beast to cross between worlds, help their brethren and spot the different societies while focusing on the other gameline's &quot;hunger&quot;. </div> </div> </div> Exactly. Though, I won't call it arguing when the devs have flat out said that Beast is a game designed for crossover. Its just less of an optional flavor, and more the default assumption.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-06-2015, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T09:00:43-07:00","id":580991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=580986#post580986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact, the crossover <i>helps</i> with the Hunger thing, because you're taking part in feeding lots of different kinds of hunger, opening new avenues to explore.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still feel like you're never fulfilling <i>your</i> hungers. You're a dragon that Hoards gold, it's your calling, you crave the glittering metal that fuels human greed, but you've been living off of watching a vamp feed for about a year now, with a side of Werewolves banishing spirits to the Shadow...why does this make sense?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T09:02:28-07:00","id":580994,"title":"","content":"You're collecting the experiences of watching them feed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T09:05:22-07:00","id":580996,"title":"","content":"Family Dinner still seems like saying that we can have a nice meal together in which you have a steak and I just watch, and by the end we're both gloated and I just had the greatest fish &amp; chip ever thanks to you eating that steak","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T09:10:13-07:00","id":581004,"title":"","content":"Well, yes, but you're not a partially-astral embodiment of the concept of predation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T09:13:28-07:00","id":581031,"title":"","content":"Indeed, but let's take the Tyrants for a second, their Hunger is for them to be on top of the food chain. Why would a vampire feeding on someone else make them feel like they're on top of the chain?<br /> <br /> Why would a mage finally understanding a Mystery feed a Ravager bent on destruction?<br /> <br /> Why would a Promethean understanding the meaning of love feed a Nemesis?<br /> <br /> I get that a Predator gets fed when a Vampire or Werewolf sinks its teeth in a prey, but a lot of other things don't really match...especially for high-level feeding. Think about it I might give a try to house ruling Family Dinner to low-satiety only.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T09:24:46-07:00","id":581066,"title":"","content":"You're looking at it all wrong. It's not an alternate method of feeding <i>your</i> hunger. It's a separate thing entirely. Beasts have a sort of of &quot;favourite food&quot;, but they still resonate with the concept of hunger on a broad level, so when they see anything else sate itself that produces a little bit of astral energy they can scavenge. It's not what they usually eat, but it'll keep them going. Like a bland muesli bar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T09:38:40-07:00","id":581079,"title":"","content":"Family dinner is also not very satisfying, at least by the original draft rules: at most you'll be rolling 3 dice per scene. I guarantee that your extended family is usually gonna be too busy to hunt that frequently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T09:47:32-07:00","id":581111,"title":"","content":"BigDamnHero, it's not dice it's points","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T10:24:54-07:00","id":581158,"title":"","content":"Plus, to be fair? Feeding your Hunger isn't exactly easy for Beasts, especially at high Satiety. A collector with a taste for art or jewelry, you not only have to find something that fits that criteria, but also has a personal connection, and you have to take it from the person somehow. Its not exactly on par with a vampire grabbing a bite to eat, or even a wolf going on a hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T10:30:47-07:00","id":581165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=581158#post581158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, to be fair? Feeding your Hunger isn't exactly easy for Beasts, especially at high Satiety. A collector with a taste for art or jewelry, you not only have to find something that fits that criteria, but also has a personal connection, and you have to take it from the person somehow. Its not exactly on par with a vampire grabbing a bite to eat, or even a wolf going on a hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this supposed to go against or with my point of view? Because if Hunger was not meant to be easy to sate, why give them 2 free points every time a Vamp takes a bite?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T10:38:44-07:00","id":581184,"title":"","content":"It's a bit more involved than that. Blood dolls explicitly don't count, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T11:14:53-07:00","id":581209,"title":"","content":"Huh, I had originally assumed that when it said, &quot;Immediately gain X Satiety&quot; that it meant Satiety potential, as per the Feeding rules.<br /> <br /> Now I'll have to have a long think about it. Being able to reliably get 2 Satiety back with a Family Tied super is pretty potent. Certainly makes it worth finding and befriending a super, I'll grant it that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T11:26:49-07:00","id":581259,"title":"","content":"Yeah, It's a crossover carrot. A big old carrot that the guy who doesn't want to bite it is claiming is too big.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T11:29:28-07:00","id":581260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=581259#post581259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, It's a crossover carrot. A big old carrot that the guy who doesn't want to bite it is claiming is too big.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe I don't like carrots? Maybe I'm for the right of carrots to stay whole and uneaten? :P<br /> <br /> Saying that I think this carrot is &quot;too big&quot; is quite spot-on though. Because I still have a whole lunch by my side and I either eat my lunch or the carrot (either you feed the Beast's Hunger or you watch vamps feed, you can sure do both, but you definitely don't <i>need</i> to)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":2589,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","user":"Magnum Opus","date":". 07-06-2015, 02:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T11:55:06-07:00","id":581330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=581031#post581031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed, but let's take the Tyrants for a second, their Hunger is for them to be on top of the food chain. Why would a vampire feeding on someone else make them feel like they're on top of the chain?<br /> <br /> Why would a mage finally understanding a Mystery feed a Ravager bent on destruction?<br /> <br /> Why would a Promethean understanding the meaning of love feed a Nemesis?<br /> <br /> I get that a Predator gets fed when a Vampire or Werewolf sinks its teeth in a prey, but a lot of other things don't really match...especially for high-level feeding. Think about it I might give a try to house ruling Family Dinner to low-satiety only.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Cart before horse&quot; is rapidly becoming a recurring line of mine lately.<br /> <br /> &quot;If someone eats, something gets eaten.&quot; The Hungers are not fed by the Beast's feelings \u2014 Tyrants feed on <i>the powerlessness and submission of their subjects</i>, else they'd just make empty clubs that they were de facto heads of; Collectors feed on <i>the envy and greed of their victims</i>, else they'd not have any compunction against simply amassing great wealth and buying their treasures; Ravagers feed on <i>the loss of security and comfort the people around them feel from seeing that the world has been broken</i>, or else they'd have literally no reason not to just tear off into the wilderness and chop down a tree every couple of days. Loss of innocence is the Beast's gain.<br /> <br /> Family Dinner largely works the same way \u2014 feeding one's supernatural appetites is almost categorically something that comes at the expense of one's human identity, and the splats nearest to not being concerned with that are the ones who already live with one foot in another world that takes time away from their lives to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T11:58:54-07:00","id":581341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=581260#post581260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe I don't like carrots? Maybe I'm for the right of carrots to stay whole and uneaten? :P<br /> <i>need</i> to)</div> </div> </div> </div>#carrotequality","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3268-krzyzstof","name":"Krzyzstof","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3268_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T12:18:56-07:00","id":581366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=581165#post581165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this supposed to go against or with my point of view? Because if Hunger was not meant to be easy to sate, why give them 2 free points every time a Vamp takes a bite?</div> </div> </div> </div> Neither, really, it had nothing to do with you. More of an idle thought on the difficulties of Satiety through regular hunting, as opposed to sources such as a Haunt or goblin fruit for other gamelines. <br /> <br /> Also, you don't get automatic points. You get 1 point for a hunt, and one point for a successful feed. Most of the time, a full hunt-feed is a lot of effort instead of using a herd or a locus, as much effort on the other's part as tracking down a way to fulfill your Hunger.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=581260#post581260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe I don't like carrots? Maybe I'm for the right of carrots to stay whole and uneaten? :P<br /> <br /> Saying that I think this carrot is &quot;too big&quot; is quite spot-on though. Because I still have a whole lunch by my side and I either eat my lunch or the carrot (either you feed the Beast's Hunger or you watch vamps feed, you can sure do both, but you definitely don't <i>need</i> to)</div> </div> </div> </div> Talk about killing a metaphor. Well, enjoy your sour grape lunch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T12:58:42-07:00","id":581394,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I think trying to make Beast &quot;Crossover Friendly&quot; is a tacit admission that the Beast material itself is paper-thin and doesn't hold up on its own, without trying to leech thematics and material off of more stable and established gamelines.<br /> <br /> I advice you to take that statement with mountainous piles of salt, as I haven't read Beast yet, largely due to the above statement making me think reading it is going to be an incredibly arduous experience.<br /> I am a big fan of Crossover, dont get me wrong, but I consider it icing on the cake. Trying to work it into the main book and thematic seems like eating icing straight out of the bucket by itself at best, and an exercise in extream naval gazing at worst.<br /> <br /> But thats just my extreamly uninformed opinion...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T13:01:53-07:00","id":581396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=581394#post581394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But thats just my extreamly uninformed opinion...</div> </div> </div> </div>Please get informed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T13:08:52-07:00","id":581433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers#post579778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People are saying that Beasts are really crossover friendly thanks to their innate powers and thematics, but I honestly see nothing of it and I believe Beasts would ruin any game in which players are mostly something else such as werewolves or Vampires.<br /> &lt;snip&gt;<br /> <b>Final Disclaimer</b><br /> I don't hate these powers, I think they fit thematically with Beast and allow for awesome Beast-only games, but as of now, Beast suffers the same problem that Mage has: They have the answer to every problem and their Mythos explains everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, this is pretty much along the lines of what I was thinking. It also doesn't think about the other splats logically. Beast's psychically prey on humans. This is a problem for both Vampires and Werewolves who are going to be considering humans part of their territory (plus both of these splats have some bad rage issues...so it likely won't end well for a Beast...). Similarly, I'm pretty sure no Mummy is going to tolerate a Beast mentally snacking on her cultusts. I'm not sure why Mages wouldn't find these guys more interesting as lab rats than collaborators. I'm still of the opinion that mounting a Beast's head above the hearth plays really well into some of Changeling's themes. The Hunter problem is obvious. That leaves Sin-Eaters and Prometheans (two game lines with their own collections of problems) and there's really no compelling reason for a team-up.<br /> <br /> I get that Matt want's to do a cross-over facilitating game but right now the text doesn't really support it. He has the right idea -- <i>Family</i> -- but there are insufficient hooks to support it. Part of this is an overfocus in the text on choosing your own family members. IMO all of the family sections needs serious overhaul. If the focus was shifted away from &quot;<i>I choose who my family is</i>&quot; to the familial themes of commitment and obligation more traction could be found. Also asking (and maybe answering) questions like -- I'm a horror now, do I really snack on my mom? -- would provide some personal horror / dilemma for the game.<br /> <br /> Considering a Beast's relationship with mortals as well as supernaturals can open a lot of doors.<br /> <br /> Including some additional merits a la:<br /> <br /> Supernatural Sibling: Your sibling, cousin, etc., has been keeping a secret from you...now that you've become a Beast the scales have fallen from your eyes. <br /> <br /> Could do a similar (and cheaper) merit where you're related to a Ghoul, Proximi, Wolf-Blooded, etc.<br /> <br /> Such a thing could let the devs ask (and not answer) -- why do so many Beasts have relatives (close or distant) that are active in other supernatural communities?<br /> <br /> Finally, I really hope that the spirit rules section is replaced with something thematically appropriate. For instance, if Beast's had a Spawn merit that let them create astral offspring that could populate their lairs, aid them from the twilight, and other things, it would go a long way to expanding the kinds of stories that the game can tell. Such a merit would have to have drawbacks, like it becomes easier for Heroes to place anathema or they gain some other advantage against the Beast.<br /> <br /> I think this can all be fixed with additional rewrites. I'm hoping this game will be as cool as Demon (and not the mess that was Geist 1.0).<br /> <br /> Flame away.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T13:11:05-07:00","id":581436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=581396#post581396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please get informed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would, but the thing is, I'm not a major fan of spending money to prove my own apriori assertion correct.<br /> I think I heard somebody mention something about some teaser material having been released? Is that free? If so, care to provide me with a link to where I might download it, so that I might become less uninformed? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1958-krobeles","name":"Krobeles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1958_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"499"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T13:14:35-07:00","id":581438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=579872#post579872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Beast has far less in the way of plot hooks and even just <i>setting</i> than the other lines; which leaves the impression that you're supposed to lean towards using other gamelines to fill in the gaps.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Honestly, it just makes it feel less complete as a game but I'm already crossing-over all of the game lines anyway so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T13:16:32-07:00","id":581440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=581436#post581436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would, but the thing is, I'm not a major fan of spending money to prove my own apriori assertion correct.<br /> I think I heard somebody mention something about some teaser material having been released? Is that free? If so, care to provide me with a link to where I might download it, so that I might become less uninformed? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. On the Kickstarter campaign page, both the original and revised copies of the text are up for the perusal of any interested parties. It has been that way for over a month now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T13:18:12-07:00","id":581443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=581436#post581436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would, but the thing is, I'm not a major fan of spending money to prove my own apriori assertion correct.<br /> I think I heard somebody mention something about some teaser material having been released? Is that free? If so, care to provide me with a link to where I might download it, so that I might become less uninformed? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>It's literally<i> on the Kickstarter page linked at the top of the forums</i>, dude. They did this with Demon and Dark Eras as well and I'm baffled as to where you thought everyone was getting enough information to make several threads asking about specific parts of the material from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T13:22:32-07:00","id":581447,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=579924#post579924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> EDIT - Also, you missed the theme of &quot;Choosing your own Family.&quot; That's a big one in Beast.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually this is a theme (and feature) of RPG's in general. A game of more substance would engage and focus on the bigger themes of commitment and obligation (note you can still <i>choose your family</i> and focus on those themes). Right now the game talks a lot about &quot;family&quot; but it never actually stops to delve into what that word means. Vampire, Demon, and Werewolf all do demonstrably better jobs at engaging each of their themes. It would not be such a bad thing to take the Family notion and re-examine it from the perspective of some permutations. IMO it should be possible to build multiple types of families using the game; if family is a thematic focus of the game, then additional mechanics should support these multiple builds; otherwise every game of Beast is going to look more than a little cookie-cutter.<br /> <br /> One of the best things Werewolf 2nd does is crack open and fully expand the notion of pack. Beast isn't even doing 10% as good of a job at exploring the notion of family.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T13:25:09-07:00","id":581450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Krobeles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=581394#post581394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I think trying to make Beast &quot;Crossover Friendly&quot; is a tacit admission that the Beast material itself is paper-thin and doesn't hold up on its own</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it was at the time, seeing as when that goal was stated it <i>didn't fucking exist. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T13:44:27-07:00","id":581469,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=580476#post580476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> May I suggest closing topic then? Since visibly my arguments are considered silly or unreasonable by most here and I feel like this thread was a bad idea to start with.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I hope that doesn't happen. If this forum isn't grown up enough to debate and discuss game cornerstones then I fear for the future of OnyxPath. Right now this game is sitting at about a Mummy level of quality. I'd like to at least see it get up to the Demon level if not the Vampire level. We should have some expectations for these games. I certainly don't want it to be another Geist 1.0.<br /> <br /> Honestly, it afforded me an opportunity to voice some of my own (unpopular) opinions. Unlike you, I think that cross-over support is something that should be pursued but not if it's at the expense of overall game quality. My main concern is that the Werewolf notion of pack is, in fact, 100 times more supportive of cross-overs than the current draft's explication of family (and the you choose it) theme. The developers seem to have forgotten that we choose family members in storytelling games anyway (the whole thing is a coop storytelling experience). The notion of family is a good one; I believe that they should keep refining it. They should add whatever mechanics are necessary to support it. And most of all, they should just go ahead and ask -- what is family anyway? Is it the people that you surround yourself with? Is it the people tied to you by the very long lines of lineage? To my mind, we can best explore these questions by focusing on themes of commitment and obligation -- core values of families -- whether they be blood relations or chosen circles of friends and familiars.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T13:53:25-07:00","id":581482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=580994#post580994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're collecting the experiences of watching them feed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wat? Sooo much cognitive dissonance...<br /> <br /> So Beasts are the licensed passive-aggressives of nWoD? Really. I'm not even sure why any Beast would want to do this except in an emergency. They're <b>Horrors</b> with their own mythology and pride. I'm not sure why they have the time of day for other supernaturals...other than because...family? That seems like a weak connection to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T13:56:09-07:00","id":581487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=581259#post581259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, It's a crossover carrot. A big old carrot that the guy who doesn't want to bite it is claiming is too big.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The problem with the carrot is that it's purely mechanical and not really supported by the essential natures of Beasts or the nWoD other supernaturals. There's no compelling narrative reason for it to even exist...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T13:56:15-07:00","id":581488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=581469#post581469\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hope that doesn't happen. If this forum isn't grown up enough to debate and discuss game cornerstones then I fear for the future of OnyxPath. Right now this game is sitting at about a Mummy level of quality. I'd like to at least see it get up to the Demon level if not the Vampire level. We should have some expectations for these games. I certainly don't want it to be another Geist 1.0</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct me if I'm wrong but didn't Mummy win an award? Or at least was nominated? I was sure I saw something like that somewhere a few months ago but I can't find anything right now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T14:00:02-07:00","id":581491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=580940#post580940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as Thicker Than Water registering as a supernatural ability, I would say that it's just an innate part of who and what the Beast is, and doesn't show up as distinct from their just standing around. It isn't a power you actively use, after all. I doubt that the Beasts are even aware that Thicker Than Water exists as a discrete ability, and most would probably be confused if someone accused them of using some kind of magic or other influence.<br /> <br /> If I were going to define it in in-character terms (because I'm the kind of person who usually does) I'd say that what's probably happening is that on a subconscious level, the other critter is sensing the Beast's presence in the Primordial Nightmare and the sliver of recognition is enough to prevent them from feeling <i>completely</i> like a stranger. They are fears given flesh, how unfamiliar can they <i>really</i> be? Who has never been afraid of powerlessness, of the unknown, of judgement or pain or disfigurement?</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that there are beings in the WoD who can understand and actively control their subconscious, Mastigos being what immediately comes to mind though given Changelings mental dealings some of them too (probably with high Clarity) may be capable of detecting these things, Anyways, they should be able to detect the changes/effects influencing their own mind such as this one, and Kinship effects are still supernatural effects, a passive supernatural effect sure, but it's still there to be noticed by anyone who can. And while I agree that it will always start whoever they approach at whatever impression level it states, like all impressions the revelation of new information can always lower it. New information like the nice guy who just approached you is magically influencing you (even if passively and only on a small scale, not that they would know it was passive). <br /> <br /> This isn't something that's going to apply to everyone, since it seems the ability to mess around and monitor your own mind isn't very common among the various splats. I had thought Vampires with Auspex might be able to, but it doesn't appear they can, at least not in the core. Maybe they'll get something like that as a Devotion at some point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T14:00:07-07:00","id":581492,"title":"","content":"In the end, I feel that this thread has come down to people saying something is bad or crappy, not because its actually dissonant or badly executed, but simply because they don't like the themes. <br /> <br /> You know what? You can just say that Beast is not the game for you. You don't like crossover? You don't like the idea of Beast being all about a big supernatural family? Then this game isn't for you. There's a lot of people who do like those things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T14:02:29-07:00","id":581493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=581482#post581482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Wat? Sooo much cognitive dissonance...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That was a bullshit ad-hoc rationalization.My <i>real</i> answer is further down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T14:08:53-07:00","id":581498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=581488#post581488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Correct me if I'm wrong but didn't Mummy win an award? Or at least was nominated? I was sure I saw something like that somewhere a few months ago but I can't find anything right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fortunately I don't put much stock in awards...and Mummy definitely has some problems (becoming a cult-member is like the zombie ant fungus for people; several powers are a bit OP -- easily fixable if you have to sacrifice some (or more) Sekhem). On the whole Beast is headed in the right direction. I don't think we really agree on the cross-over stuff. I also don't think it necessarily needs to be in there but, I do believe that if it's going to be in then it better be at a quality level that makes it feel like an organic component to the game rather than something shoehorned in or Frankenstein stitched on. The essential essence of you op is correct; the whole cross-over portion of Beast requires additional revision and development because it's no where near the quality of the rest of the text (Hero section notwithstanding - though the latest draft is a vast improvement, it still could use more work).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T14:10:42-07:00","id":581502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=581492#post581492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the end, I feel that this thread has come down to people saying something is bad or crappy, not because its actually dissonant or badly executed, but simply because they don't like the themes.<br /> <br /> You know what? You can just say that Beast is not the game for you. You don't like crossover? You don't like the idea of Beast being all about a big supernatural family? Then this game isn't for you. There's a lot of people who do like those things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't like Beast being a game with a Hunger being sated by alternate ways than actually feeding the monster inside you. Here, you have it now.<br /> <br /> I love crossovers and have done it many times now.<br /> <br /> I love the idea of Beast being a game of a huge supernatural family.<br /> <br /> I play with many Beast concepts right now, none of which include using a single Kin power in any significant way because I don't like these powers. Except one, which use <i>only</i> these powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T14:39:50-07:00","id":581551,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=581492#post581492\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the end, I feel that this thread has come down to people saying something is bad or crappy, not because its actually dissonant or badly executed, but simply because they don't like the themes.<br /> <br /> You know what? You can just say that Beast is not the game for you. You don't like crossover? You don't like the idea of Beast being all about a big supernatural family? Then this game isn't for you. There's a lot of people who do like those things.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I missed where people were saying these things. The initial draft of this game was good but could be better. The revisions have made it better but some parts could still use additional work.<br /> <br /> Just asking and answering questions like -- If I hunger for things (collector) what do I get out of feeding from other supernaturals' feedings? -- is immensely helpful. The game doesn't need to answer all of the metaphysical / mythological questions but it should handle the essential logical cause-effect ones. If it wants to be a cross-over game then it should be, but what it presents right now is still only half-baked and thematically weak. It's a collection of mechanical hacks with very little narrative reason for existing beyond the deus ex machina of because...Crossover.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I don't understand why people are being so defensive. It isn't like the game is not going to happen. It is going to happen. That being the case, there's no reason it can't be the best game possible. It should definitely try to outdo Werewolf (which has so many built-in crossover hooks it's impossible to count them all; literally everything can spin towards needing to temporarily or permanently add other supernaturals as allies or packmates).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1630,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","user":"Jacob","date":". 07-06-2015, 05:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T14:51:54-07:00","id":581560,"title":"","content":"I think I might just up and steal Passing Resemblance for Demon; it feels more elegant than Spoofing to me.<br /> <br /> Just make it permanent rather than Scene-length, and have it make you look like a Mortal rather than a Supernatujral and yer done.<br /> <br /> I agree, though, that Beast needs some tightening up; the mechanics don't <i>feel</i> as polished as Demon's were when it was at about this point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T14:56:32-07:00","id":581564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=581488#post581488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Correct me if I'm wrong but didn't Mummy win an award? Or at least was nominated? I was sure I saw something like that somewhere a few months ago but I can't find anything right now.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mummy the Curse and Book of the Deceived both got nominated for the Ennies. I don't remember if either of them won, though I think Mummy did.<br /> <br /> Back onto Beast, I don't know what more to tell people. Kinship powers were the first thing I read about in playtesting, and they really snared me into liking the game. If you don't like Kinship powers, then yeah, try the game without them. World of Darkness is a toolbox setting, it works to try that in theory. As for me and my house, we'll play with them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-06-2015, 06:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T14:59:55-07:00","id":581565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=581551#post581551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just asking and answering questions like -- If I hunger for things (collector) what do I get out of feeding from other supernaturals' feedings? -- is immensely helpful. The game doesn't need to answer all of the metaphysical / mythological questions but it should handle the essential logical cause-effect ones. If it wants to be a cross-over game then it should be, but what it presents right now is still only half-baked and thematically weak. It's a collection of mechanical hacks with very little narrative reason for existing beyond the deus ex machina of because...Crossover.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I don't understand why people are being so defensive. It isn't like the game is not going to happen. It is going to happen. That being the case, there's no reason it can't be the best game possible. It should definitely try to outdo Werewolf (which has so many built crossover hooks it's impossible to count them all; literally everything can spin towards needing to temporarily or permanently add other supernaturals as allies or packmates).</div> </div> </div> </div>Disagreeing with you isn't exactly the same thing as being defensive. For instance, you get the impression, from reading the book, that Beasts are very much defined by their own particular hunger/obsession, and therefore it doesn't make sense to you that they can be sated by taking part in other supernaturals sating their own hunger. Others may have a different perspective; for instance, that all beasts essentially serve the same Hunger, but have adapted to it in different ways. This allows for the possibility that Beasts can share certain feeding methods in common, such as being present for another supernatural being's feeding. Expressing that perspective and asking that you consider it isn't defensiveness, it's discussion.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, one perspective that I'm having a hard time understanding is your view of Werewolf as a super crossover-happy game. Sure, there are plot hooks and comments on how some werewolf powers might interact with other supernaturals, but they're just little bits and pieces scattered through the book, and I don't really think there's anything at all that Werewolves &quot;need&quot; from other supernaturals. Plus, it's really no different from Vampire in this respect; <i>Blood and Smoke</i> has all the same sidebars and plot hooks for how kindred may interact with werewolves or whatnot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3209,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","user":"CatDoom","date":". 07-06-2015, 06:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3209-catdoom","name":"CatDoom","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T15:08:49-07:00","id":581569,"title":"","content":"Belated response but wanted to answer anyways.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=581433#post581433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(...)</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree.<br /> <br /> Maybe you think otherwise, maybe you don't, but to me the theme of Family in Beast The Primordial is very much about acceptance and support. Beasts can find those not only among kin, but with every other monster as well. With vampires, or werewolves or changelings or whatever, they may find understanding and companionship. And in the same way, other supernaturals can find understanding and aid in the Beggoten.They're pretty much equipped for it.<br /> <br /> Of course this won't be the case with every supernatural. It most certainly won't be the case even just among every single Beast. Vampires and werewolves argue internally about territory and socio-cultural matters. By the logic of finding Beasts more interesting as lab rats, you could certainly say the same for most other supernaturals, which is making dangerous assumptions about the methods of all mages. Mummies that care for their individual followers wouldn't tolerate <i>other things</i> taking from their cultists either. Supernaturals come into conflict with different splats, or even among those of the same kind, for the same variety of reasons they may come into conflict with Beasts. When it comes down to the nitty gritty, it depends a lot on individual expectations and feelings. But hence choosing your family.<br /> <br /> I think the book actually does a good job presenting all these paradigms. Also, Demon is one of my favorite books. Mummy is another of my favorite books. I love them both for various reasons, and I think I love Beast just as much for different reasons. And I find the writing on all of them quite fantastic and of comparable quality (even if they are at their best in different places, and Demon is more polished mechanics wise than Mummy or Beast right now).<br /> <br /> You can have your opinion, I won't say it's wrong. But consider that it's a lot more subjective than what you're making it sound like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 07-06-2015, 06:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T16:19:23-07:00","id":581669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=581487#post581487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The problem with the carrot is that it's purely mechanical and <b>not really supported by the essential natures of Beasts or the nWoD other supernaturals. There's no compelling narrative reason for it to even exist... </b></div> </div> </div> </div>...No.<br /> <br /> It's roughly akin to the Strengthen part of ephemeral Influence. Beasts have power over the Astral concept of Supernature in minor ways, so they can buff the concept of Supernature when they encounter it.<br /> <br /> That's the <i>cosmological </i>reason. The <i>narrative </i>is that it gives supernaturals a reason to at least stop talking long enough when the human with a soul of a dragon claims to be an elder cousin of yours, ergo building a family, and the <i>essential </i>reason is that Beasts are direct descendants of the Dark Mother, who they say is the first supernatural creature with a human aspect to ever exist, and even if not is still an Astral entity relating to the very concept of things becoming stranger. They remember their birthright.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T17:18:23-07:00","id":581711,"title":"","content":"They likely also relate to other monsters because as <i>primal embodiments of humanity's fear</i><i>s </i>they have power over the corresponding astral concept (evidenced in their deep connection to the Primordial Dream) and establish links to other supernaturals based on the fears <i>they</i> embody in the astral.<br /> <br /> Which, funnily enough, is also the basis by which they develop Kinship Nightmares.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 07-06-2015, 08:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T20:07:58-07:00","id":581865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=581491#post581491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Except that there are beings in the WoD who can understand and actively control their subconscious, Mastigos being what immediately comes to mind though given Changelings mental dealings some of them too (probably with high Clarity) may be capable of detecting these things, Anyways, they should be able to detect the changes/effects influencing their own mind such as this one, and Kinship effects are still supernatural effects, a passive supernatural effect sure, but it's still there to be noticed by anyone who can. And while I agree that it will always start whoever they approach at whatever impression level it states, like all impressions the revelation of new information can always lower it. New information like the nice guy who just approached you is magically influencing you (even if passively and only on a small scale, not that they would know it was passive).<br /> <br /> This isn't something that's going to apply to everyone, since it seems the ability to mess around and monitor your own mind isn't very common among the various splats. I had thought Vampires with Auspex might be able to, but it doesn't appear they can, at least not in the core. Maybe they'll get something like that as a Devotion at some point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you might be misunderstanding me. My take on it is that they <i>aren't</i> influencing the other party, just that something about them feels faintly familiar. Think of it like a much subtler version of the effect that causes people with supernatural awareness to see the Horror when you use your powers. It an explicitly supernatural effect, but I don't think there's any chance that the viewer will mistake it as something being done to them or some kind of offensive illusion, because it isn't something you are doing to them, it's just something that is happening and they're able to perceive it.<br /> <br /> The effects of Thicker Than Water aren't much different from someone just being unusually attractive, it's just a different kind of magnetism and it's only noticeable to people who aren't completely vanilla human. The actual game mechanics are treated that way too. There's no dice pool for it, there's no resistance or failure chance, it doesn't cost anything, and there's no stated chance to notice anything unusual, the Beast is just naturally inoffensive at first glance.<br /> <br /> I'm sure there's people (abnormally paranoid Mastigos, some Changelings, etc) who'll meet someone they think is moderately likable for no specific reason and freak out because of it, but they're the minority. Most people don't meet someone they have a positive first impression of and then immediately sit down and frantically dissect <i>why</i> they like that person, scrambling for signs of manipulation or NLP or pheromone laced perfume or etc.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I feel like you're looking for a way to treat it as a bigger deal than it actually is or was meant to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T21:55:02-07:00","id":581938,"title":"","content":"As for why a beast can use family dinner, one has to remember what beasts are- They're astral entities with human bodies.<br /> <br /> The astral realm is a place where thought is reality, fear and hunger are tangible things like the mass of a gold bar or the wattage of an electrical current.<br /> <br /> And the normal influences of a horror let loose from their mortal shells? Hunger and fear, that's their primal nature.<br /> <br /> So why wouldn't a beast get sated when a hunger is fed near them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-06T23:48:38-07:00","id":581996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=581865#post581865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you might be misunderstanding me. My take on it is that they <i>aren't</i> influencing the other party, just that something about them feels faintly familiar. Think of it like a much subtler version of the effect that causes people with supernatural awareness to see the Horror when you use your powers. It an explicitly supernatural effect, but I don't think there's any chance that the viewer will mistake it as something being done to them or some kind of offensive illusion, because it isn't something you are doing to them, it's just something that is happening and they're able to perceive it.<br /> <br /> The effects of Thicker Than Water aren't much different from someone just being unusually attractive, it's just a different kind of magnetism and it's only noticeable to people who aren't completely vanilla human. The actual game mechanics are treated that way too. There's no dice pool for it, there's no resistance or failure chance, it doesn't cost anything, and there's no stated chance to notice anything unusual, the Beast is just naturally inoffensive at first glance.<br /> <br /> I'm sure there's people (abnormally paranoid Mastigos, some Changelings, etc) who'll meet someone they think is moderately likable for no specific reason and freak out because of it, but they're the minority. Most people don't meet someone they have a positive first impression of and then immediately sit down and frantically dissect <i>why</i> they like that person, scrambling for signs of manipulation or NLP or pheromone laced perfume or etc.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, I feel like you're looking for a way to treat it as a bigger deal than it actually is or was meant to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>And yet it shouldn't feel familiar, and the only reason it does is because of an innate supernatural power. So they <i>are</i> being influenced, and anyone with a tight lock on their own mind should be able to tell that. And even if it's just something that's happening and they can perceive it, it is still new information being added into the equation after the fact that can be used to adjust their view of the person.<br /> <br /> And being unnaturally attractive, to people who can tell that that is a thing, is as much a red flag as anything else. Take Majesty for example. Even if the person using Awe is covered in blood and gore it only seems to enhance their beauty. To anyone with the ability to guard/perceive their own mind/mental state, this should send out warning signs just the same. Awe also requires no roll, has no chance of failure, nothing to resist, and no cost to activate. This doesn't mean that the effects of the ability can't be detected by powers and abilities designed specifically to detect such mental intrusions. Sure, it's subtle, but most mental influences are, that's why such detection methods exist.<br /> <br /> And as for how 'most people' act, 'most people' don't have the ability to sense when someone else is infringing upon their thoughts and feelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 07-07-2015, 02:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T02:26:40-07:00","id":582060,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=581551#post581551\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just asking and answering questions like -- If I hunger for things (collector) what do I get out of feeding from other supernaturals' feedings? -- is immensely helpful. The game doesn't need to answer all of the metaphysical / mythological questions but it should handle the essential logical cause-effect ones. If it wants to be a cross-over game then it should be, but what it presents right now is still only half-baked and thematically weak. It's a collection of mechanical hacks with very little narrative reason for existing beyond the deus ex machina of because...Crossover.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;You Get Nothing! Good Day Sir!&quot;<br /> <br /> Nah.. what you actually get is the Horror sympathetically Basking in the fear/horror/knowledge that their Family can look after themselves. That they are Eating Right, taking care of themselves, think of it as a sense of Pride? &quot;Ahh Look at Fred, He's gonna be okay that one, now Frank.. He Needs some work&quot;<br /> <br /> That's how I see it. You are essentially getting Table Scraps, But your making sure everyone else is fine. Like the Dad who Subsists on a MacDonalds, while the family has a Home cooked Meal that he Provided for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T05:48:22-07:00","id":582182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=581996#post581996\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet it shouldn't feel familiar, and the only reason it does is because of an innate supernatural power. So they <i>are</i> being influenced, and anyone with a tight lock on their own mind should be able to tell that. And even if it's just something that's happening and they can perceive it, it is still new information being added into the equation after the fact that can be used to adjust their view of the person.<br /> <br /> And being unnaturally attractive, to people who can tell that that is a thing, is as much a red flag as anything else. Take Majesty for example. Even if the person using Awe is covered in blood and gore it only seems to enhance their beauty. To anyone with the ability to guard/perceive their own mind/mental state, this should send out warning signs just the same. Awe also requires no roll, has no chance of failure, nothing to resist, and no cost to activate. This doesn't mean that the effects of the ability can't be detected by powers and abilities designed specifically to detect such mental intrusions. Sure, it's subtle, but most mental influences are, that's why such detection methods exist.<br /> <br /> And as for how 'most people' act, 'most people' don't have the ability to sense when someone else is infringing upon their thoughts and feelings.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree re: Majesty and such. I said unusually attractive instead of unnaturally for exactly that reason. There's nothing magical or concerning about being prettier than average unless it turns into 'that strand of intestines really brings out her eyes'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T07:28:30-07:00","id":582248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=582182#post582182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree re: Majesty and such. I said unusually attractive instead of unnaturally for exactly that reason. There's nothing magical or concerning about being prettier than average unless it turns into 'that strand of intestines really brings out her eyes'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Regardless of how this is spun Thicker Than Water is still a supernatural ability that influences the recipients mental/emotional state. There are powers that detect effects that influences mental/emotional states, and as such they should work just as well against this as they should against something like Majesty. Awe also doesn't necessarily make the user unnaturally attractive, but like Thicker Than Water is still supernaturally influences how the user is perceived by others. And again, there are those out there who can pick up on and notice when their mind, emotions, and perceptions are being messed with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T07:41:22-07:00","id":582259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=582248#post582248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regardless of how this is spun Thicker Than Water is still a supernatural ability that influences the recipients mental/emotional state. There are powers that detect effects that influences mental/emotional states, and as such they should work just as well against this as they should against something like Majesty. Awe also doesn't necessarily make the user unnaturally attractive, but like Thicker Than Water is still supernaturally influences how the user is perceived by others. And again, there are those out there who can pick up on and notice when their mind, emotions, and perceptions are being messed with.</div> </div> </div> </div>...then just play it as such? Since it's not stated as one way or another, and players are generally not considered to be affected by Social Influence rules, it could go one way or another. Your Mastigos has a mind shield that detects Thicker Than Water? Fine. Your Mastigos feels a faint mind <i>influencing</i> (not manipulation) coming his way and decides to be on his guards and suddently feel the power dissipate (because he broke the first impression). That's all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T07:52:12-07:00","id":582288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=582259#post582259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...then just play it as such? Since it's not stated as one way or another, and players are generally not considered to be affected by Social Influence rules, it could go one way or another. Your Mastigos has a mind shield that detects Thicker Than Water? Fine. Your Mastigos feels a faint mind <i>influencing</i> (not manipulation) coming his way and decides to be on his guards and suddently feel the power dissipate (because he broke the first impression). That's all.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I most certainly will, but Mechalith seemed to want to discuss my take on things and compare it to his own interpretation of the rules and so we are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T07:57:49-07:00","id":582291,"title":"","content":"Mechalith's interpretation of the power is to consider it just like the merit that allows you to take a condition to open 2 doors, while you're taking the power like a Vampire's Discipline or his Predatory Aura. Both are valid, as long as you state which is which at game start.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T08:00:07-07:00","id":582292,"title":"","content":"I'd like to see proof that Thicker than Water is really a supernatural effect in the first place. &quot;A natural affinity&quot; doesn't seem to imply supernatural compulsion to me. I think its meant to be a much more mundane solution here - Beasts are naturally friendly with supernaturals as a rule of thumb.<br /> <br /> If someone is paranoid or naturally suspicious? Then that's what adding Doors are for.<br /> <br /> We don't need to make nountains out of molehills here. Hell, we could refluff the entire thing so it ends up reading as &quot;Beasts are naturally skilled at convincing other supernaturals, giving them the equivalent of a Good Impression for Social Maneuvering when determining time between rolls. Determine Impression as normal based on reactions to the initial interaction&quot; and it would be pretty much the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T08:02:13-07:00","id":582293,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=582291#post582291\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mechalith's interpretation of the power is to consider it just like the merit that allows you to take a condition to open 2 doors, while you're taking the power like a Vampire's Discipline or his Predatory Aura. Both are valid, as long as you state which is which at game start.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course we can arbitrarily decide which to go with, but where's the fun in that? Discussing the subject and trying to sway the other person to your side is half the fun!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=582292#post582292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to see proof that Thicker than Water is really a supernatural effect in the first place. &quot;A natural affinity&quot; doesn't seem to imply supernatural compulsion to me. I think its meant to be a much more mundane solution here - Beasts are naturally friendly with supernaturals as a rule of thumb.<br /> <br /> If someone is paranoid or naturally suspicious? Then that's what adding Doors are for.<br /> <br /> We don't need to make nountains out of molehills here. Hell, we could refluff the entire thing so it ends up reading as &quot;Beasts are naturally skilled at convincing other supernaturals, giving them the equivalent of a Good Impression for Social Maneuvering when determining time between rolls. Determine Impression as normal based on reactions to the initial interaction&quot; and it would be pretty much the same thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Apart from the bonds of Family, the advantages of Atavisms, and the limitless potential of Nightmares, Beasts also possess a number of innate traits as a result of their ties to the Soul \u2014 and through it, to the Dark Mother herself. Collectively referred to as Kinship, the Children see these attributes as extensions of their mythic lineage. </div> </div> </div>Innate traits stemming from their ties to the Dark Mother that are seen as extensions of their mythic lineage? Seems pretty supernatural to me. Anyways, suns up, time to go to bed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 07-07-2015, 11:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T09:16:51-07:00","id":582422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=582293#post582293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Innate traits stemming from their ties to the Dark Mother that are seen as extensions of their mythic lineage? Seems pretty supernatural to me. Anyways, suns up, time to go to bed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me clarify myself - Innate trait is not the same thing as a supernatural effect. Sure, you can say its supernatural, because, hell, beasts are supernatural by definition, and the ones beasts relate to are supernaturals. But that's not the same thing as a supernatural effect that manipulates targets' minds, which is what we're all talking about here. As well, the Thicker Than Water section itself uses the phrase &quot;a natural affinity.&quot;<br /> <br /> I fail to see how T.T.W. is that much different than the Pusher merit. You're just that good at relating to people and can make good first impressions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T09:41:58-07:00","id":582442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=582259#post582259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> ...then just play it as such? Since it's not stated as one way or another, and players are generally not considered to be affected by Social Influence rules, it could go one way or another. Your Mastigos has a mind shield that detects Thicker Than Water? Fine. Your Mastigos feels a faint mind <i>influencing</i> (not manipulation) coming his way and decides to be on his guards and suddently feel the power dissipate (because he broke the first impression). That's all.</div> </div> </div> </div> Well if one works under the assumption that thicker than water is active during social maneuvering, then for the hypothetical mastigos to detect anything then the following things couldn't apply-<br /> <br /> 1) the ST would have to determine that there are no circumstances to warrant an at least average impression and that the beast made no effort to make a good first impression, which anyone can do without so much as a roll.<br /> <br /> 2) The beast didn't make a roll to get a better than good impression.<br /> <br /> 3) The beast didn't rely on roleplaying instead of social maneuvering.<br /> <br /> 4) The beast just skips to forcing doors to get automatic results<br /> <br /> Since thicker than water, when it comes to mostly human types like mages, has literally less results than telling the ST that your character &quot;is wearing his good shirt,&quot; I suspect that none of those conditions applying is somewhat unlikely.<br /> <br /> After all, under the rules, without any of those conditions, it could take a beast a month to convince a mage to babysit the beast's pet goldfish, if the mage was willing at all. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T09:50:08-07:00","id":582445,"title":"","content":"I feel as though comparisons of Thicker Than Water to Majesty are skipping over the existence of Alien Allure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T09:55:32-07:00","id":582449,"title":"","content":"Thank you Satchel. There's a marked difference between the two standards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T12:26:12-07:00","id":582619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=581565#post581565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Disagreeing with you isn't exactly the same thing as being defensive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't just basing the defensive observation on responses to me. I do think people are being very defensive but that's pretty much par for the interwebs where no one can express a differing opinion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=581565#post581565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For instance, you get the impression, from reading the book, that Beasts are very much defined by their own particular hunger/obsession, and therefore it doesn't make sense to you that they can be sated by taking part in other supernaturals sating their own hunger. Others may have a different perspective; for instance, that all beasts essentially serve the same Hunger, but have adapted to it in different ways. This allows for the possibility that Beasts can share certain feeding methods in common, such as being present for another supernatural being's feeding. Expressing that perspective and asking that you consider it isn't defensiveness, it's discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure what my impression from the draft text has to do with whether or not folks are being defensive and I agree some points are discussion but there's also alot of snark in this thread too.<br /> <br /> You have an interesting read of the text BTW but I'm not following where Beast's actually share feeding methods. They're more like remora, along for the ride and nibbling up the leftovers. The question of why other supernaturals would tolerate their presence stands. Right now it's just a matter of troupe preference and the built-in deus ex machina of &quot;crossover&quot; supported by some system hacks. That's fine and all but I'd like more than that. I don't see where my desire for more hurts the folks who are already satisfied, unless people are worried that it might mean revisions on par with the whole Soul+Homecoming / Horror+Devouring situation, in which case the discussion points against changes are, indeed, defenses of the status quo. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CatDoom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=581565#post581565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Incidentally, one perspective that I'm having a hard time understanding is your view of Werewolf as a super crossover-happy game. Sure, there are plot hooks and comments on how some werewolf powers might interact with other supernaturals, but they're just little bits and pieces scattered through the book, and I don't really think there's anything at all that Werewolves &quot;need&quot; from other supernaturals. Plus, it's really no different from Vampire in this respect; <i>Blood and Smoke</i> has all the same sidebars and plot hooks for how kindred may interact with werewolves or whatnot.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd encourage you to reread all of the sections pertinent to how Werewolf packs are built because I'm not talking about power compatibility, I'm looking at the ease with which I can include other supernaturals as members of the pack (examples using Vamps actually appear in the text). That's a 180 from the position of W:tF 1st ed where pack was one of the biggest barriers to crossover games (because one couldn't select anything but Werewolves as pack members). That type of option gives me as the storyteller and the players as a troupe a wealth of options for the kinds of crossover stories we want to tell. Right now the Family section lacks anything remotely comparable. I get the Beast's mythos view of other supernaturals but there's nothing there that actually makes narrative sense for the other supernaturals to have anything less than a hostile attitude towards them. <br /> <br /> Recall that vamps and werewolves especially have their own internal beasts that are constantly striving for dominance. I just don't see where either are going to suffer a Beast's existence which makes crossover a hard sell. Similarly Demons are going to worry about something that can chew on their Cover, etc., etc. Now YMMV but I'd like to see the Family aspect of the game (and thereby its crossover bits) beefed up considerably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T12:43:46-07:00","id":582637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=582422#post582422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me clarify myself - Innate trait is not the same thing as a supernatural effect. Sure, you can say its supernatural, because, hell, beasts are supernatural by definition, and the ones beasts relate to are supernaturals. But that's not the same thing as a supernatural effect that manipulates targets' minds, which is what we're all talking about here. As well, the Thicker Than Water section itself uses the phrase &quot;a natural affinity.&quot;<br /> <br /> I fail to see how T.T.W. is that much different than the Pusher merit. You're just that good at relating to people and can make good first impressions.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I'm awake. Innate doesn't mean it isn't supernatural. A werewolfs shapeshifting is innate. A mages attainments are innate. Changeling pledges are innate. All of these things, while innate to the creature that has them, aren't any less supernatural than Gifts and Disciplines and the like. In fact, since you can't not start with at least a few dots in some of these even those are technically innate to some degree. So again, innate doesn't mean it isn't a supernatural ability.<br /> <br /> And as far as how it differs from something like Pusher, well that's easy. It's the source, the origin of the trait is what makes it different. It's the difference between being strong and using whatever form of magic your splat has access to to make yourself strong. In the end, strength dots are strength dots, regardless of where you get them, but if you have the perceptive ability to do so you can still tell the difference. It's the difference between being beautiful and shapeshifting yourself into a more pleasing form. You gain the effects of the Striking Looks merit either way, but anyone who can tell has new information that they can work off of to whatever ends they please.<br /> <br /> And that's the key here. While the effect isn't much different from a mundane effect, the source is just as important. And in this case, the source is an innate supernatural power stemming from your ties to the Dark Mother and/or your own monstrous lineage. And to those who possess the means, these things are, and should be, noticeable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 07-07-2015, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T12:51:17-07:00","id":582646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=581569#post581569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I disagree.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get that already...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=581569#post581569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe you think otherwise, maybe you don't, but to me the theme of Family in Beast The Primordial is very much about acceptance and support. Beasts can find those not only among kin, but with every other monster as well. With vampires, or werewolves or changelings or whatever, they may find understanding and companionship. And in the same way, other supernaturals can find understanding and aid in the Beggoten.They're pretty much equipped for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Acceptance and support don't sound like interesting themes for an RPG. To some extent they come for free just by virtue of it being an RPG (kind of like choosing your family). Source of dilemma and conflict make for much more interesting conflict. The fact is that refining the sections describing Family in no way detracts from you playing it as acceptance and support (even if it does sound like a Care Bears RPG). Now YMMV, but beefing up the sections on Family so that they paint a fuller picture of <i>all kinds</i> of families just adds great material to the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=581569#post581569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course this won't be the case with every supernatural. It most certainly won't be the case even just among every single Beast. Vampires and werewolves argue internally about territory and socio-cultural matters. By the logic of finding Beasts more interesting as lab rats, you could certainly say the same for most other supernaturals, which is making dangerous assumptions about the methods of all mages. Mummies that care for their individual followers wouldn't tolerate <i>other things</i> taking from their cultists either. Supernaturals come into conflict with different splats, or even among those of the same kind, for the same variety of reasons they may come into conflict with Beasts. When it comes down to the nitty gritty, it depends a lot on individual expectations and feelings. But hence choosing your family.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampires and Werewolves don't just argue internally, they compete, they try to establish dominance, they murder one another. How a Beast doesn't end up killed or someone's bitch I don't know but, they definitely can't keep their hands out of other peoples' cookie jars because of their Hunger. It's going to be a social problem when outsiders are chewing on your food, your family, your Cover, your minions, etc. It requires a lot of buy-in from players; ironically we generally hate-on books and movies that rely on the heavy handed tactic of &quot;because it's supposed to&quot;. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=581569#post581569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the book actually does a good job presenting all these paradigms. Also, Demon is one of my favorite books. Mummy is another of my favorite books. I love them both for various reasons, and I think I love Beast just as much for different reasons. And I find the writing on all of them quite fantastic and of comparable quality (even if they are at their best in different places, and Demon is more polished mechanics wise than Mummy or Beast right now).</div> </div> </div> </div>The draft (Beast is no where near being a book yet -- has to go to printers, etc. first) does a good job representing certain themes (not paradigms -- a paradigm is more &quot;how do we X&quot;, think along epistomological lines, e.g., quantitative science is a paradigm, calculus a method, etc.) but if it's going to go with Family as its crossover aid then it could definitely afford to represent additional themes that are important to the concept of Family, especially those that lend themselves to forcing players to face dilemmas and seed conflicts. In the end you make my point for me -- &quot;Demon is more polished mechanics wise than Mummy or Beast right now&quot; -- exactly! I'm arguing that they can polish Beast more before publishing it. In no way does this damage the existing things that you like about it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=581569#post581569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But consider that it's a lot more subjective than what you're making it sound like.</div> </div> </div> </div>Er, isn't that the whole point of having an opinion? Just because it's subjective doesn't mean its wrong or bad.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T13:37:20-07:00","id":582689,"title":"","content":"I said that because you were making some of your points sound like objective statements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T14:17:16-07:00","id":582713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=582637#post582637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I'm awake. Innate doesn't mean it isn't supernatural. A werewolfs shapeshifting is innate. A mages attainments are innate. Changeling pledges are innate. All of these things, while innate to the creature that has them, aren't any less supernatural than Gifts and Disciplines and the like. In fact, since you can't not start with at least a few dots in some of these even those are technically innate to some degree. So again, innate doesn't mean it isn't a supernatural ability.<br /> <br /> And as far as how it differs from something like Pusher, well that's easy. It's the source, the origin of the trait is what makes it different. It's the difference between being strong and using whatever form of magic your splat has access to to make yourself strong. In the end, strength dots are strength dots, regardless of where you get them, but if you have the perceptive ability to do so you can still tell the difference. It's the difference between being beautiful and shapeshifting yourself into a more pleasing form. You gain the effects of the Striking Looks merit either way, but anyone who can tell has new information that they can work off of to whatever ends they please.<br /> <br /> And that's the key here. While the effect isn't much different from a mundane effect, the source is just as important. And in this case, the source is an innate supernatural power stemming from your ties to the Dark Mother and/or your own monstrous lineage. And to those who possess the means, these things are, and should be, noticeable.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Satchel is hitting directly on the distinction I've been trying to make. The key point of contention is that I don't consider it a power. Shapeshifting is a power, Changeling pledges are a power, Atavisms and Nightmares are powers, Thicker Than Water is just a social merit that happens to have a supernatural justification in fluff.<br /> <br /> I think part of the reason I'm averse to your interpretation is that all of your examples are things that someone has to <i>do</i>. Even the Family Resemblance ability is an active attempt to deceive someone that the Beast has to make (and is explicitly noted as having a good chance of backfiring.) There is no way for a Beast to <i>not</i> take advantage of Thicker Then Water.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sisyphus has it easy...","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1647-mechalith","name":"Mechalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"364"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T14:45:41-07:00","id":582731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=582713#post582713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Satchel is hitting directly on the distinction I've been trying to make. The key point of contention is that I don't consider it a power. Shapeshifting is a power, Changeling pledges are a power, Atavisms and Nightmares are powers, Thicker Than Water is just a social merit that happens to have a supernatural justification in fluff.<br /> <br /> I think part of the reason I'm averse to your interpretation is that all of your examples are things that someone has to <i>do</i>. Even the Family Resemblance ability is an active attempt to deceive someone that the Beast has to make (and is explicitly noted as having a good chance of backfiring.) There is no way for a Beast to <i>not</i> take advantage of Thicker Then Water.</div> </div> </div> </div>I consider thicker then water to be similiar to a demons ability to control his emotions everyone gets it in the start and is one of the most useful skill that demons have from start to finish.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T14:49:56-07:00","id":582734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=582637#post582637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I'm awake. Innate doesn't mean it isn't supernatural.</div> </div> </div> </div> Nope. Innate means diddly squat when it comes to the question of being a supernatural <i><b><u>effect</u></b></i> or not. The Undead Flesh (downgrade lethal to bashing damage) is a natural consequence of becoming a supernatural vampire. Same with the distinct lack of need to breathe. That doesn't mean the effect itself is supernatural; its not magic that allows the damage reduction, but the fact that, from a biological standpoint, vampires don't need their organs or lungs. The body is still taking the punishment.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And that's the key here. While the effect isn't much different from a mundane effect, the source is just as important. And in this case, the source is an innate supernatural power stemming from your ties to the Dark Mother and/or your own monstrous lineage. And to those who possess the means, these things are, and should be, noticeable. </div> </div> </div> I disagree with you there. Just because a supernatural critter does something does not automatically make that something into a supernatural event. <br /> <br /> The write up specifically says &quot;a natural affinity.&quot; That implies its actually just a natural feeling that arises from the interaction. I don't consider that to be a supernatural effect, and thus, I don't feel its measurable by a Mastigos scouring for any hint of it with their magics (be it on themselves like Majesty would, with mage sight, through goetic interviews, whatever). <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=582619#post582619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wasn't just basing the defensive observation on responses to me. I do think people are being very defensive but that's pretty much par for the interwebs where no one can express a differing opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div> There's a difference between defensive, and correcting someone when they're mistaken. Including when someone states their opinion as if it was a fact. When you say things, like Werewolf does 10x better with family, something completely and utterly subjective, as if it was an objective truth? We get issues. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T14:55:41-07:00","id":582742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=582731#post582731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I consider thicker then water to be similiar to a demons ability to control his emotions everyone gets it in the start and is one of the most useful skill that demons have from start to finish.</div> </div> </div> </div> Except that's not a supernatural ability. Its a natural state of being for them due to the nature of Covers and their minds being separated from their bodies. In fact, its arguable that, while Going Loud or Burned, you lose that trait. <br /> <br /> As well, if you read Flowers of Hell, you see that the control isn't perfect. They do have to make a conscious decision to show emotions or signs of lying, but there are now mundane rolls associated with doing it. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T15:11:31-07:00","id":582747,"title":"","content":"They keep the trait burned, because nobody has any clue how to read the emotions of a divine mechanical abomination. <br /> <br /> Like &quot;I try to read the emotions on his face.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;He hasn't got one.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T15:13:49-07:00","id":582748,"title":"","content":"Does anyone here not have experience with animal magnetism? Is that why this is such a foreign concept?<br /> <br /> They just are the sort of people that supernatural people are inclined to gravitate to. Whether it's supernatural or a mundane effect of their metaphysical makeup(Is there a difference as a flesh/astral hybrid?), does it really matter? &quot;Oh my god, they are found more likable by things that go bump in the night on first impression provided they aren't wearing a intestinal chain tied up with dildos around their neck&quot; hardly seems like an offensive &quot;OH MY GOD, IT'S DATE-RAPING ME SPIRITUALLY!&quot;* sort of precedent.<br /> <br /> Don't be a dick and slightly more paranoid people are willing to chat with you. Given the veils of secrecy that go around, it strikes me as something that helps Beasts actually approach the supernatural family, which we've established is a theme of the game. There are ways to to subvert it before and after the fact, and It's just one impression step up, meaning congratulations**, you can make social rolls slightly faster. It's hardly game breaking, cosmology altering, or some ridiculous thing.<br /> <br /> Can we cool our jets about this? It's really not the big thing to stress over. Atavisms are closer to deserving this sort of &quot;OH MY GOD&quot; reaction.***<br /> <br /> *Yes, I am aware I am overblowing it grossly.<br /> **San Francisco, you've ruined pizza.<br /> ***Also, if you want to look at really slimy implications of stuff, may I remind you all that Blood Bonding is a thing that exists? This ain't nothing compared to that shit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T16:56:37-07:00","id":582896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mechalith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=582713#post582713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Satchel is hitting directly on the distinction I've been trying to make. The key point of contention is that I don't consider it a power. Shapeshifting is a power, Changeling pledges are a power, Atavisms and Nightmares are powers, Thicker Than Water is just a social merit that happens to have a supernatural justification in fluff.<br /> <br /> I think part of the reason I'm averse to your interpretation is that all of your examples are things that someone has to <i>do</i>. Even the Family Resemblance ability is an active attempt to deceive someone that the Beast has to make (and is explicitly noted as having a good chance of backfiring.) There is no way for a Beast to <i>not</i> take advantage of Thicker Then Water.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is just as much a power as werewolf Shapeshifting is a power. It is no more innate than that is and you yourself call that out as being a power. It is a supernatural ability granted directly to Beasts simply by being Beasts. You do not get this specific ability any other way than by adding on the Beast major supernatural template. Thicker Than Water is a power, specifically a Kinship power. It isn't a merit, it isn't an attribute, it isn't a skill. It is a power, albeit a passive power, but a power nonetheless. End of story.<br /> <br /> Not having to be activated doesn't make something any less of a power. Werewolves regenerate constantly just by doing nothing but being werewolves, and that enhanced regeneration is as detectable as any other power or ability by those with the means to perceive such things. Demons have the ability to lie <i>perfectly.</i> It doesn't take any sort of special action or effort for them to do so, it is just something they can do. Changelings are always hidden behind a passive glamour to make them appear human. This is a constant effect that takes 0 effort to maintain, in fact, it's so persistent it takes a lot of effort to even make it stop for even short periods of time. While their Mask is a fairly potent illusion, it can still be detected by those with the means to do so.<br /> <br /> Long story short, passivity of a supernatural effect makes it no less a supernatural effect. There are examples of this through every line (probably, I don't really know some of the lines well enough to say for sure), and I don't see a thing about Thicker Than Water that would make it an exception.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T17:19:05-07:00","id":582911,"title":"","content":"As a note, with the Mastigos as an example, the best that a beast will get is an Average impression on first impressions when using the doors method of social maneuvering, as a mage is a fundamentally human type, TTW would only give them an average impression, not a good one... now is it a supernatural power? well, let the storyteller adjudicate, thats the point of a storyteller right? its not a mind control power (by the rules specifically) its a social lubricant, its having the right smile when talking about something monstrous, the right pheromones for the beast inside the vampire to smell, the spiritual eddies for the werewolf to recognize or a spirit to comprehend. so, yes, it is somewhat supernatural and it is somewhat not, does it matter? well not really. its on the storyteller. mostly i view this as a way for a chronicle to gloss over having to break into each and every supernatural world and allow beasts to treat supernatural NPC's the way most people treat human NPC's who they are not antagonistic towards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5718-hackthulhu","name":"Hackthulhu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5718_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T17:43:50-07:00","id":582922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hackthulhu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=582911#post582911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a note, with the Mastigos as an example, the best that a beast will get is an Average impression on first impressions when using the doors method of social maneuvering, as a mage is a fundamentally human type, TTW would only give them an average impression, not a good one... now is it a supernatural power? well, let the storyteller adjudicate, thats the point of a storyteller right? its not a mind control power (by the rules specifically) its a social lubricant, its having the right smile when talking about something monstrous, the right pheromones for the beast inside the vampire to smell, the spiritual eddies for the werewolf to recognize or a spirit to comprehend. so, yes, it is somewhat supernatural and it is somewhat not, does it matter? well not really. its on the storyteller. mostly i view this as a way for a chronicle to gloss over having to break into each and every supernatural world and allow beasts to treat supernatural NPC's the way most people treat human NPC's who they are not antagonistic towards.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is it a supernatural power when it just gives an average impression? Yes. It doesn't just stop being a supernatural power because it has a lesser effect on certain creature types. It either is or isn't, at least that's how I see it. And I never said it was a mind control power, I said it was a mind <i>influencing</i> power.<br /> <br /> As for whether or not it matters, my answer has always been 'usually not'. There aren't that many abilities throughout nWoD that I'm aware of that can detect mind influencing (or control even) powers. As far as I can tell Werewolf doesn't have one, Vampire doesn't have one (though such a thing would make a pretty nice Devotion), and Changeling only <i>might</i> end up having one, given their predisposition for emotional effects. Again, the biggest offender here is, as usual, mage. 1/5th of their number <i>do</i> have the ability to pick up on something like this, which is why I even originally brought it up as a relevant possibility.<br /> <br /> So while this isn't something that is <i>likely</i> to come up, depending on various factors in the game being played, it was something to be mentioned offhandedly. That said, it seems to have sprawled out into a discussion of what is and what is not a supernatural effect or something. Anyways, back to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T18:08:23-07:00","id":582929,"title":"","content":"My my, poor criticisms in the thread &amp; no reason to do it insults of the Mummy line and fans, lovely. The Beast ability strikes me as having the same issues that Charm based social influence had in Exalted 2e. Partially it was poor implementation, and part of it was poor interpretation. While I do think that Beast ability needs some clarification I don't think anyone is going to get anything of use by interpreting it deliberately in the worst light.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T18:15:07-07:00","id":582941,"title":"","content":"What makes you think the Beast mythos isn't the true mythos though? It's the same principle as a family tree scattering across the world and eventually diverging into various sub cultures / families. It makes sense even from a real world perspective.<br /> <br /> Beasts are nightmares who prey on people's fears and are born into human forms, Fae and Changelings are the products of dreams and have learned to sustain themselves by feeding on the emotions of humanity, Werewolves are monsters born into a human bodies and drive people to horrified madness if they so much as glimpse their true forms, Vampires sustain themselves by preying upon mortals and literally claim they have &quot;a Beast&quot; within themselves, In fact, with the new 2e vampires, the Beast isn't all about mindless slaughter anymore, but can be directed to more focused goals. Evidence seems to suggest they have a bunch of similarities to each other, but it wasn't until Beast that we began to notice them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Everybody has their own version of history, but statistically speaking, one of those versions has to be correct. ^_^<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 07-07-2015, 09:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T18:45:51-07:00","id":582985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=582941#post582941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What makes you think the Beast mythos isn't the true mythos though? It's the same principle as a family tree scattering across the world and eventually diverging into various sub cultures / families. It makes sense even from a real world perspective.<br /> <br /> Beasts are nightmares who prey on people's fears and are born into human forms, Fae and Changelings are the products of dreams and have learned to sustain themselves by feeding on the emotions of humanity, Werewolves are monsters born into a human bodies and drive people to horrified madness if they so much as glimpse their true forms, Vampires sustain themselves by preying upon mortals and literally claim they have &quot;a Beast&quot; within themselves, In fact, with the new 2e vampires, the Beast isn't all about mindless slaughter anymore, but can be directed to more focused goals. Evidence seems to suggest they have a bunch of similarities to each other, but it wasn't until Beast that we began to notice them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Everybody has their own version of history, but statistically speaking, one of those versions has to be correct. ^_^<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>False dichotomy. None of the setting's splats have to have a correct &quot;version&quot; of history in any meaningful sense at all. 4 people can all tell 4 nonsensical stories that only have bits of coloured facts and interpretations. Beyond that, WHO CARES! The mood and tone of the NWoD is not set up for a &quot;No no no, splat X is objectively factual on X,Y, &amp; Z. So sayeth the Objective Narrator!&quot; People arguing that Beast is correct, or some one else is are missing the point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-07T19:16:46-07:00","id":583048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=582941#post582941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everybody has their own version of history, but statistically speaking, one of those versions has to be correct. ^_^<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Putting asides statistics, a big point of the mystery of the origin has a lot to do with how it doesn't affect the modern day activities. Beast challenges that notion somewhat because they make a case for rejecting humanity(even as they teach it), and possible association postulates an inevitable decline into monstrosity for everyone, but even then that can be overlooked somewhat.<br /> <br /> Soooooo everyone has their own version of history, but relatively speaking, that doesn't matter as much on the street as the academics put it sometimes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T01:05:41-07:00","id":583261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=582941#post582941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everybody has their own version of history, but statistically speaking, one of those versions has to be correct. ^_^<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>No, no it doesn't. What's most likely is that everyone is <i>partially</i> correct but mostly wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T05:49:16-07:00","id":583412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=583261#post583261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, no it doesn't. What's most likely is that everyone is <i>partially</i> correct but mostly wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although, statistically, it's unlikely they'll all be correct/wrong to the same degrees - someone will be more right than most, someone will be less right. (I vote sineaters* - they have more access to eyewitnesses <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ).<br /> <br /> * Notice I didn't say <i>which</i> I vote them for; eyewitness testimony doesn't always have a good track record.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T09:09:20-07:00","id":583515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=582748#post582748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone here not have experience with animal magnetism? Is that why this is such a foreign concept?</div> </div> </div> </div> I call it the Supernatural Kinsey Scale! Except, instead of gender, its a sliding scale of attraction to power!<br /> <br /> Which is why Mummies are dead sexy *rimshot*<br /> <br /> Sorry, I just had to tell the bad jokes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Atavisms are closer to deserving this sort of &quot;OH MY GOD&quot; reaction.*** </div> </div> </div> I really don't understand why people would be having an OMG reaction to Atavisms. Anyone care to explain why its so much worse than, say, Embeds and Exploits? Sure, exp for exp, its arguably more effective to buy up Cyclopean Strength and Lair than Vigor, but Vigor increases base Strength as well as automatic successes, which applies to more than just lifting and throwing, so its debatable which is better there. Dominate 1 seems to be stronger than You Must Obey, imho. Actually, with the exception of You Are Meat (Satiety Spending only) and You Must Obey, I don't think Nightmares are that powerful.<br /> <br /> Seriously, why? Is it just perception? Am I missing something? Is it just the difference between having to buy up Discipline/Renown levels and freeform powers with no prerequisits? All I can think of is that I must be missing something.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ashenrogue</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=582896#post582896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Long story short, passivity of a supernatural effect makes it no less a supernatural effect. There are examples of this through every line (probably, I don't really know some of the lines well enough to say for sure), and I don't see a thing about Thicker Than Water that would make it an exception.</div> </div> </div> </div> Passive supernatural effects do happen. However, not everything about a supernatural must be classifed as supernatural in the first place. That, I think, is the flaw in your argument.<br /> <br /> Is vitae addictive because it magically creates a psychological addiction? Or is it just addictive in the same way that any street drug is, and people crave the rush? In this case, the rush of energy and pleasure is absolutely supernatural, but the addiction is just a craving for touching more of that supernature. Should we be considering a shapeshifted bat using echolocation to find someone supernatural? That's an important distinction, because we'd have to argue if it can &quot;see&quot; through invisibility automatically, or if we'd need a Clash of Wills. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=582941#post582941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Everybody has their own version of history, but statistically speaking, one of those versions has to be correct. ^_^</div> </div> </div> </div> ... actually, everyone else has answered this well enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-08-2015, 12:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T09:38:02-07:00","id":583545,"title":"","content":"For the record, I don't think Atavisms deserve the ZOMG response either. But is something in this entire conversation should get it, Atavisms deserve it more than Thicker Than Water.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T10:15:41-07:00","id":583564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=582734#post582734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> There's a difference between defensive, and correcting someone when they're mistaken. Including when someone states their opinion as if it was a fact. When you say things, like Werewolf does 10x better with family, something completely and utterly subjective, as if it was an objective truth? We get issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Packs in Werewolf are 10x better than the current fluff and mechanics for Family vis-a-vis crossovers. That is a fact. Packed in supernaturals get all of the same Totem benefits as the other pack-members so...honestly, this isn't rocket science, and the draft does need more work or this discussion wouldn't even be happening.<br /> <br /> You're welcome to keep &quot;correcting&quot; me though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T10:25:12-07:00","id":583571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=583515#post583515\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Passive supernatural effects do happen. However, not everything about a supernatural must be classifed as supernatural in the first place. That, I think, is the flaw in your argument.<br /> <br /> Is vitae addictive because it magically creates a psychological addiction? Or is it just addictive in the same way that any street drug is, and people crave the rush? In this case, the rush of energy and pleasure is absolutely supernatural, but the addiction is just a craving for touching more of that supernature.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, it's a lot more nuanced than what you're saying. Everything supernatural is necessarily classified as supernatural; not everything supernatural generates a Clash of Wills though. So yes, the addicting quality of Vitae is supernatural. Vitae itself is supernatural. It turns humans into Ghouls when they drink it and can unnaturally extend their life-spans. Everything about it is, in fact, supernatural. <br /> <br /> Note that for the record I'm not arguing that Thicker Than Water should operate other than it does. IIRC, it does generate a Clash of Wills if the supernatural creature is using Obfuscate or similar power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T10:36:41-07:00","id":583617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=583571#post583571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that for the record I'm not arguing that Thicker Than Water should operate other than it does. IIRC, it does generate a Clash of Wills if the supernatural creature is using Obfuscate or similar power.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's Family Resemblance you're thinking of, seeing as Thicker Than Water just gives you an innate social lubricant for supernatural beings (and, as an extension of that, the ability to use limited Social Maneuvering on &quot;feral&quot; supernaturals).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T10:37:11-07:00","id":583620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=583564#post583564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Packs in Werewolf are 10x better than the current fluff and mechanics for Family vis-a-vis crossovers. That is a fact.</div> </div> </div> </div>No it isn't, because I disagree with you, because it's not a provable statement. I think that Kinship offers greater support for Family and crossovers. That you can include other supernaturals in your pack as a werewolf doesn't help explain why you should invite them or why they would accept your invitation, whereas Beasts have built-in reasons to seek other supernaturals (devise new Nightmares, Family Dinner) and other supernaturals don't, as a whole, have a great reason to say &quot;No thanks, we don't want to hang out with Beasts.&quot;<br /> <br /> Not that other supernaturals say, &quot;Oh awesome, a Beast! Come hang out with us buddy!&quot; but I doubt a Mummy would refuse a Beast who offered to be a cultist, and a Promethean would love some company on those long, lonely nights on the road.<br /> <br /> I don't think Beast needs to answer the question &quot;Why would other supernaturals suffer the existence of Beasts?&quot; when it's clear that it's not an issue.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T10:40:41-07:00","id":583624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=583564#post583564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Packs in Werewolf are 10x better than the current fluff and mechanics for Family vis-a-vis crossovers. <b>That is a fact.</b> Packed in supernaturals get all of the same Totem benefits as the other pack-members so...honestly, this isn't rocket science, and the draft does need more work or this discussion wouldn't even be happening.<br /> <br /> You're welcome to keep &quot;correcting&quot; me though.</div> </div> </div> </div>No.<br /> <br /> I could argue with you, pointing out how the Beast in this case is the totem equivalent here and how much more more beneficial and broad that is, and how much better it is when players benefit from both. I could sit here and argue about how there's a difference between focuses on families and crossover between the two games.<br /> <br /> But honestly, neither of those are what brought me to respond.<br /> <br /> You say that the idea that packs are better than Beasts for the family/crossover aspect is a fact. You, in fact, assert a numerical expression for it.<br /> <br /> You are, quite in fact, wrong.<br /> <br /> What you mean to say is that you feel that the inclusion of anything into a pack is better than what a Beast brings to the table, and you are right to feel like that, and even justify your reasons for believing. But you cannot prove that it's irrefutably better because it's a matter of personal experience.<br /> <br /> Might <i>being</i> in a pack be statistically better than simply being Family Tied to a Beast? Sure, in a contextless void. I'm not going to bother with the numbers validating that concept, because contextless voids aren't something I play with when I do WoD, not often. But in play? A character who can talk to everyone, go anywhere, and boost everyone is more interesting and dynamic for me. In my opinion, Beasts are great for the family thing, because while other groups can include them in, Beasts have the tools to seek them out and bring them in to be included. Does that mean I am right? Are my words fact?<br /> <br /> No, because my experiences and my backgrounds and insights are different from MCN's which are different from Matt's which are different from Atamjakki which are different from yours. We all look and handle these things in different ways. For a lot of us, the fact that a Werewolf pack is a passive benefit that doesn't matter to the spirit of the games in context to each other, for a lot of others, what's the point in declaring yourself as being a cause-of-crossover-convergence when the numbers don't back it.<br /> <br /> We can argue quality all we want, and I'm not going to be the asshole to say art is purely subjective, because it's not. But there is a point where one's enjoyment purely comes from a subjective interaction with the material.<br /> <br /> So, no, it is not a fact, and even if it were possible for it to be so, your assertion that it is 10x better is sorely lacking evidence, so screw that interpretation anyways.<br /> <br /> Your hostility and absolutist stance on your opinions(demonstrated by presenting your opinion as fact) is the most defensive thing I have seen in this entire thread, so you'll forgive me if I ask of you some maturity. Cool down a little bit, soften up a little bit, and talk with us rather than argue with us.<br /> <br /> And for the record, yes, this is something I will keep correcting you on, because it's very poor forum etiquette and a nigh-on useless attitude for expressing an opinion in the hopes of change and revision. People, both forumites and writers, will flat out ignore you with the way you are going.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-08-2015, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T11:13:54-07:00","id":583667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=583564#post583564\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That is a fact.</div> </div> </div> </div> No, its your opinion. You can try to say it true, claim its not rocket science, until you're blue in the face, but you are not objectively correct. That's all it comes down to. You can only speak for yourself, and no one else.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm done with this part of the discussion. Its clear that, for you, &quot;better&quot; means mathematically superior mechanics, while I don't give a care about mechanics and only worry about the themes of the game. We disagree. There's nothing more to be said about it.<br /> <br /> Can we please go back to that Atavism/Nightmares being overpowered thing? I'm actually really curious about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-08-2015, 02:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T11:50:39-07:00","id":583699,"title":"","content":"I'm not so sure Atavisms and Nightmares are overpowered, though. I mean they just aren't. Their regular availability means more they get more use than fuel-dependent splats, but that's balanced by the big guns being tied to Satiety and its' expenditure. The rough balance feels right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T12:08:44-07:00","id":583721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=583667#post583667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Can we please go back to that Atavism/Nightmares being overpowered thing? I'm actually really curious about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since I started this thread I might as well give you my point of view. Atavisms and Nightmares have absolutely 0 cost and offer really strong effects. As you said, especially You Are Meat and You Must Obey.<br /> <br /> Being able to mind-control as many persons as you want as a scene-long effect without any cost? Wow, ok. Being able to constantly spit fireballs, turn after turn, effectively giving you a strong revolver bolted in your mouth? Ok. Being able to <i>supress </i>one's soul(neat word for &quot;removing&quot; but without the metaphysical effects of killing almost every supers in the game) is also really strong.<br /> <br /> As far as atavisms go, Titanic Blow is off the charts. I know Promethean is not updated right now, but it's basically the whole Vitality Transmutation tree into one neat 3XP package.<br /> <br /> I would have been more satisfied with Atavisms if they weren't under the player's total control. It would have been awesome and in theme if atavisms were always in effect rather than activable. With a story-driven drawback like Telepathy and many other supernatural merits.<br /> <br /> Mimir's Wisdom? Fine. You and your wife have an argument, by the end you say you're sorry, that you love her. She says the same, but that little voice in your head creeps in. <i>Lies...</i><br /> Dragonfire? Fine. Someone angers you and you yell at him to shut up. Opening your eyes, you see him ablaze with everyone else panicking.<br /> Limb From Limb? Fine, in a sparring boxing match with a mortal friend you break his arm in a single punch by accident, claw marks all over his arm.<br /> Shadowed Soul? As you try to warn your friend of the hunters in the other room, they seem to ignore your presence and enter in.<br /> Siren's Treacherous Song? As you speak with your friend in the local caf\u00e9, you look around to see the patrons entranced by your sayings, slowly moving towards you like mindless zombies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T12:11:44-07:00","id":583725,"title":"","content":"I generally don't worry too much about the idea of overpowered, but put that way, I can see your point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T12:43:42-07:00","id":583771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=583721#post583721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(neat word for &quot;removing&quot; but without the metaphysical effects of killing almost every supers in the game)</div> </div> </div> </div>does nobody know how the soulless condition works<br /> <br /> is that what is happening<br /> <br /> did people just not read what losing your soul actually does<br /> <br /> because this is at least the second <i>distinct category</i> of failure of comprehension that has been demonstrated on this issue<br /> <br /> You lose the ability to regain as much of your sense of self (i.e. Willpower) from your Virtue and the stability of your self-concept (i.e. your Integrity) starts to waver as you try to shore up your ego with guilty comforts (i.e. indulge your Vice and trigger severe breaking points) until you have the barest scraps of your personal identity and start losing your core personhood (i.e. Willpower dots), whereupon the same stress fractures can eventually prevent you from developing the character further. That's it. That is the entire spectrum of effects that replicating the Soulless Condition on a character presents, aside from incidentals like less resistance to possession. You flip the rates at which you regain Willpower from Virtue and Vice, Integrity eventually drops to 1, whereby your Virtue loses its satisfaction altogether and your Willpower capacity eventually collapses to 0, whereupon you're subject to the effects of the Broken Condition and can't spend Experiences or defend yourself.<br /> <br /> Translating some of these concepts to other supernaturals may not be <i>totally</i> straightforward, but the games with mechanics that specifically interact with soul loss have less dire consequences in store than death, and the bulk of the other character types nevertheless evince a greater degree of influence by wills not their own with falling Integrity-equivalents to begin with, whether in the form of spiritual directives taking greater precedence or just generally having more difficulty relating to and interacting with humanity.<br /> <br /> It may be ambiguous whether the long-term suppression of a vampire's soul might eventually rob them of their ability to regain Willpower through their Mask and fracture their Dirge, but losing Humanity and Willpower and becoming more susceptible to possession are in line with the narrative effects of both soul loss and becoming more monstrous; ditto for the Bone and Blood and Harmony of werewolf souls. Mage has the rules for soul loss baked in, and having demonic Cover degrade in convincingness with the replication of soul loss when it's at least partially a memetic construct whose degradation can often result in the development of inhuman qualities isn't too much of a stretch. We don't yet know if Promethean 2e has different Virtue/Vice equivalents, but losing autonomy and progress on the Pilgrimage is, again, in line with the effects of soul loss while still not being a &quot;you are dead&quot; flag; Mummy is about the farthest of any line from a second edition, but &quot;suppression of the soul&quot; is basically an exact description of what low-to-no Memory represents and the entire reason why that line's character development mechanics incentivize raising Memory and the qualities that correspond to soul-anatomy in the first place.<br /> <br /> You Are Meat has its problems, but &quot;metaphysically speaking this should logically kill or deprotagonize every playable supernatural being it hits&quot; is not one of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 07-08-2015, 03:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T12:52:50-07:00","id":583778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=583721#post583721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since I started this thread I might as well give you my point of view. Atavisms and Nightmares have absolutely 0 cost and offer really strong effects. As you said, especially You Are Meat and You Must Obey.<br /> <br /> Being able to mind-control as many persons as you want as a scene-long effect without any cost? Wow, ok. Being able to constantly spit fireballs, turn after turn, effectively giving you a strong revolver bolted in your mouth? Ok. Being able to <i>supress </i>one's soul(neat word for &quot;removing&quot; but without the metaphysical effects of killing almost every supers in the game) is also really strong.<br /> <br /> As far as atavisms go, Titanic Blow is off the charts. I know Promethean is not updated right now, but it's basically the whole Vitality Transmutation tree into one neat 3XP package.</div> </div> </div> </div> I... think you should hold off on judging these things by 1e standards. Especially Promethean Transmutations - they're arguably weaker than even 1e vampire disciplines or werewolf gifts in a lot of cases. As for 2e games? The Unchained can have the better than the entire electricity transmuation power set before character creation. Demons also put Vulcanus to shame.<br /> <br /> I'm getting the impression that its only overpowered when we compare it to 1e? Is that it, perhaps? <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would have been more satisfied with Atavisms if they weren't under the player's total control. It would have been awesome and in theme if atavisms were always in effect rather than activable. With a story-driven drawback like Telepathy and many other supernatural merits. </div> </div> </div> I think this is a case of player versus character agency. Supernatural powers are always under a <i>player's </i>control. As well as they should be.<br /> <br /> That doesn't mean that a <i>character</i> can control the powers. I've played Mehket in VtR 1e where they couldn't shut off their Auspex - they could never turn it off. A Daeva who's use of Majesty was all unconsciously tied to her appearance, what clothes she wore, what makeup, etc. No conscious control.<br /> <br /> So, you can play things that way, but its not a requirement. I would have no issue with such things happening in game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T13:06:21-07:00","id":583786,"title":"","content":"Hey Satchel,<br /> <br /> Sure, that's how it works for mortals, but for supers?<br /> <br /> Vampires are a flesh bag with a human soul and a monstrous parasite wrestling inside trying to decide wether to go have supernatural politics or kill everyone around (which comes around as the same too many times anyway). Removing the Soul is basically dropping his humanity to 0 in short notice.<br /> Werewolves...would probably act like mortals losing their souls, slowly degrading towards the Spirit side of harmony until they become creatures of the Hisil<br /> Mages have an <i>Awakened Soul. </i>That's the core concept of the game. Removing it would not kill him, sure, but it <i>will</i> remove all of his neat powers<br /> Prometheans don't have a soul so I don't see why this should affect them, and if it does (since this <i>suppress </i>the nearest thing to a soul) then the Promethean is now a stitched together bag of meat.<br /> Changelings should slowly break their clarity into the 0 level<br /> Sin-Eaters should slowly become a walking, fleshy Geist (see prometheans)<br /> Mummies are, somewhat like Vampires, an immortal soul being forced into a body over and over again. The body just appears to be similar every time they're forced into it. Removing this immortal soul <i>should </i>destroy the mummy.<br /> Demons....either they have no soul and then shouldn't be affected, or they <i>are </i>a soul and should die or slumber for a long time.<br /> <br /> I know that most of these are basically &quot;drop your karma to 0 in a medium-long term thing&quot;, but may I remind you that having 0 Karma is defined as losing your character in most gamelines? (Werewolves, stay in the back please)<br /> <br /> And let's say that You Are Meat is a power that will mostly target mortals. Ok? So you roll a couple of dice and within a few weeks that person is either batshit crazy, shot herself in self-realization of her recent actions or went full Hatred and was stopped by the local police/military forces. All for a single dice roll and the equivalent of a lunch break. I'm not saying this isn't in theme with Beast, I'm saying it's <i>narratively</i> over the power-level of the other Nightmares which....force people to run away, remove the ability to roll exceptional success and drain someone of their willpower.<br /> <br /> The only difference between losing your soul and having it suppressed by You Are Meat is that the Nightmare allows for a quest in order to regain it. How the hell are you supposed to discover that you need to quest in the primordial dream in order to regain your soul? <i>You aren't even aware that you lost the thing.</i> And what of monsters that don't dream? Such as Vampires?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T13:07:55-07:00","id":583787,"title":"","content":"Weird slight off topic, but I think they decided to pull You are Meat until they could balance it. I say this because I'm on the Nightmare/Atavism section of the document the only places it gets mentioned are in a tip for creating Nightmares that says they don't have to threaten bodily harm/death and the block list of common Nightmares. It isn't actually in the Nightmares given though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T13:18:04-07:00","id":583793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=583778#post583778\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So, you can play things that way, but its not a requirement. I would have no issue with such things happening in game.</div> </div> </div> </div>You might not, but I know a lot of players who would rage quit if one of their &quot;perfect&quot; powers had a drawback all-of-a-sudden.<br /> <br /> Player: I try to arm-lock him<br /> ST: Not realizing your own strength, you break his arm and he starts screaming in pain and panic.<br /> Player: No I don't! I'm in full control of my powers, I didn't activate it! My character would never do that!<br /> ST: calm down dude it's a narrative effect<br /> Player: No you're ruining my game, I wanted to be stealthy and manipulate this mafia dude!<br /> <br /> Not kidding...this would happen if I tried to release this kind of flaw in Atavisms","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T13:18:41-07:00","id":583795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=583786#post583786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that most of these are basically &quot;drop your karma to 0 in a medium-long term thing&quot;, but may I remind you that having 0 Karma is defined as losing your character in most gamelines? (Werewolves, stay in the back please)</div> </div> </div> </div>1.<br /> <br /> Drop your karma to <i>1.</i><br /> <br /> Which is still playable.<br /> <br /> And is predicated on avoidable actions on your character's part.<br /> <br /> The soul is not the seat of vitality or personality to the degree that the purported metaphysical argument assigns it.<br /> <br /> I don't particularly care about the &quot;mechanically overpowered&quot; argument, seeing as I've already remarked on the more pressing issue of &quot;having a power that makes it super easy to make people lose Integrity in almost any context with no consequence to yourself when you stand to get a massive boon from people losing Integrity kind of breaks the narrative flow&quot; the last time this came up, but &quot;that character should be dead/an NPC&quot; was and is a bad argument.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And what of monsters that don't dream? Such as Vampires? </div> </div> </div>Please stop trying to comment on metaphysics you clearly don't understand, because at least two different books in first edition have covered what vampire dreams are like and second edition hasn't made any explicit changes to the fact of &quot;vampires dream during the daysleep and torpor&quot; \u2014 the nearest change to that part of the metaphysics in particular is that the Fog of Eternity is no longer a consistently-occurring thing that uses torpor as its primary vector.<br /> <br /> Nalak's point remains valid nevertheless and we'll presumably see how the print draft shakes out when it's done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T13:27:08-07:00","id":583800,"title":"","content":"They removed it? Good. It didn't really make sense with the new teaching-via-nightmares thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T13:27:17-07:00","id":583801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=583795#post583795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1.<br /> <br /> Drop your karma to <i>1.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Honest mis-reading. Thank you for the clear-up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't particularly care about the &quot;mechanically overpowered&quot; argument </div> </div> </div>I wrote thematically.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Please stop trying to comment on metaphysics you clearly don't understand </div> </div> </div>Please stop trying to sound condescending and stop me from having a discussion. I haven't read the whole Onyx Path library, that's a fact. Fine. I admit it. Next point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nalak's point remains valid nevertheless and we'll presumably see how the print draft shakes out when it's done. </div> </div> </div>Indeed. We can only wait and see.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T13:29:51-07:00","id":583804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=583786#post583786\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey Satchel,<br /> <br /> Sure, that's how it works for mortals, but for supers?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I get where you are coming from but I'm inclined to believe that it works exactly as Satchel has put it. Conditions and Tilts affect supernaturals in exactly the same ways that they affect mortals (except where the text clearly notes exceptions). I thought this was the whole point to the Condition/Tilt mechanic -- taking some of the guessing game out of the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T13:35:09-07:00","id":583808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=583804#post583804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I get where you are coming from but I'm inclined to believe that it works exactly as Satchel has put it. Conditions and Tilts affect supernaturals in exactly the same ways that they affect mortals (except where the text clearly notes exceptions). I thought this was the whole point to the Condition/Tilt mechanic -- taking some of the guessing game out of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>So...going by that logic, a soul-less Beast (or soul-supressed) would drain the Beast of his satiety rather than placing him in the same state that happens when the Beast goes over Satiety 10?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T13:35:14-07:00","id":583809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=583793#post583793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might not, but I know a lot of players who would rage quit if one of their &quot;perfect&quot; powers had a drawback all-of-a-sudden.<br /> <br /> Player: I try to arm-lock him<br /> ST: Not realizing your own strength, you break his arm and he starts screaming in pain and panic.<br /> Player: No I don't! I'm in full control of my powers, I didn't activate it! My character would never do that!<br /> ST: calm down dude it's a narrative effect<br /> Player: No you're ruining my game, I wanted to be stealthy and manipulate this mafia dude!<br /> <br /> Not kidding...this would happen if I tried to release this kind of flaw in Atavisms</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, no shit somebody would be upset if you did this to them out of the blue. This is the kind of thing that you discuss before the game. If you're the ST, then you need to let your players know &quot;hey, sometimes you won't be able to totally control your atavisms.&quot; If the players don't like that, then you can compromise or you can kick them out. If you're the PC, it's easier, because you can just make it part of your concept. &quot;So, sometimes my character uses atavisms without intending to&quot; (which sounds like it was more the direction MCN was coming from).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2021,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","user":"MagicSwordsman","date":". 07-08-2015, 04:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T13:38:25-07:00","id":583816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=583793#post583793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might not, but I know a lot of players who would rage quit if one of their &quot;perfect&quot; powers had a drawback all-of-a-sudden.<br /> <br /> Player: I try to arm-lock him<br /> ST: Not realizing your own strength, you break his arm and he starts screaming in pain and panic.<br /> Player: No I don't! I'm in full control of my powers, I didn't activate it! My character would never do that!<br /> ST: calm down dude it's a narrative effect<br /> Player: No you're ruining my game, I wanted to be stealthy and manipulate this mafia dude!<br /> <br /> Not kidding...this would happen if I tried to release this kind of flaw in Atavisms</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, that's a completely different matter. In this case, it feels like the ST is controlling what the character is doing. And that tends to be a big no-no. Like I said earlier, players should have full agency, even if characters do not. STs should not dictate what a PC does, unless under mind control. Even then, I generally prefer having that handled via note passing and letting the player roll play it out.<br /> <br /> I would treat this situation like... the results of Social Maneuvering, or something. Give them Conditions that reflect being enraged, or clumsy and new, or something. The player's will have incentives to slip and break arms, or the like, because they want the yummy beats.<br /> <br /> <br /> Its an age old issue. And not only an issue between players and GMs, but between players as well. &quot;I roll to convince the rest of the group to do what I say! Success! You have to obey me!&quot; Yes, that's happened to me before. Its a shitty feeling when you lose control over your character because of stuff like that. That's why I love the Condition system - it rewards you for playing along, and there's really no consequences if its something you absolutely don't want to do. Carrot, not stick.<br /> <br /> Its also why we have the option of failing a roll, and opting for a dramatic failure fora beat. Make things like this interesting. In both cases, its always the player's choice, but we're encouraging crazy stuff!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-08-2015, 04:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T13:42:25-07:00","id":583821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=583816#post583816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Its an age old issue. And not only an issue between players and GMs, but between players as well. &quot;I roll to convince the rest of the group to do what I say! Success! You have to obey me!&quot; Yes, that's happened to me before. Its a shitty feeling when you lose control over your character because of stuff like that. That's why I love the Condition system - it rewards you for playing along, and there's really no consequences if its something you absolutely don't want to do. Carrot, not stick.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know that feeling too well. Also, let's state that my previous example had a before-hand talk about Atavism-failures, thus not related to me grabbing total control of their character out of the blue. How is this any different than the Telepathy flaw?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T13:52:30-07:00","id":583823,"title":"","content":"It's not; in both cases the player was appraised of potential disadvantages. If that player still complained about it, you'd be within your rights to say &quot;look, we talked about this before the game. You don't have total control over your super-strength.&quot;<br /> <br /> That being said, MCN's suggestion, where the player is given a carrot, not a stick, is probably going to be more fun for everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2021-magicswordsman","name":"MagicSwordsman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"194"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T14:05:11-07:00","id":583827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=583821#post583821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know that feeling too well. Also, let's state that my previous example had a before-hand talk about Atavism-failures, thus not related to me grabbing total control of their character out of the blue. How is this any different than the Telepathy flaw?</div> </div> </div> </div> Well, I think the main problem here is &quot;boundaries.&quot; GMs shouldn't determine what a character does. Uncontrolled telepathy, while it is still an uncontrolled ability, is an extension of your senses. And relaying things to the PCs through the senses is considered the GM's domain. How a character acts, feels, or moves, however, is firmly within the player's domain. <br /> <br /> Plus, the telepathy flaw is actually a bonus - it gives the player more information, so they're actually being rewarded in this case. Injuring someone unintentionally, however, is definitely not a bonus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T14:41:27-07:00","id":583862,"title":"","content":"It would be a bit of trick, but Strange has a mechanic for stuff like that called the GM intrusion. If you could work out a method to agree it then you would have more balance on pulling stuff like that. I mean there are certain circumstances where saying your character doesn't have perfect control in all circumstances is more valid than others. I mean there's a difference between breaking a man's arm when trying for an arm lock because you were in a desperate fight and you needed the arm lock to stay in the fight/survive vs trying for the arm lock and shattering it when you're in full control of the fight and are trying to incapacitate the target, so you can talk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T14:47:09-07:00","id":583865,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=583624#post583624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No.<br /> <br /> I could argue with you, pointing out how the Beast in this case is the totem equivalent here and how much more more beneficial and broad that is, and how much better it is when players benefit from both. I could sit here and argue about how there's a difference between focuses on families and crossover between the two games.<br /> <br /> But honestly, neither of those are what brought me to respond.<br /> <br /> You say that the idea that packs are better than Beasts for the family/crossover aspect is a fact. You, in fact, assert a numerical expression for it.<br /> <br /> You are, quite in fact, wrong.<br /> <br /> What you mean to say is that you feel that the inclusion of anything into a pack is better than what a Beast brings to the table, and you are right to feel like that, and even justify your reasons for believing. But you cannot prove that it's irrefutably better because it's a matter of personal experience.<br /> <br /> Might <i>being</i> in a pack be statistically better than simply being Family Tied to a Beast? Sure, in a contextless void. I'm not going to bother with the numbers validating that concept, because contextless voids aren't something I play with when I do WoD, not often. But in play? A character who can talk to everyone, go anywhere, and boost everyone is more interesting and dynamic for me. In my opinion, Beasts are great for the family thing, because while other groups can include them in, Beasts have the tools to seek them out and bring them in to be included. Does that mean I am right? Are my words fact?<br /> <br /> No, because my experiences and my backgrounds and insights are different from MCN's which are different from Matt's which are different from Atamjakki which are different from yours. We all look and handle these things in different ways. For a lot of us, the fact that a Werewolf pack is a passive benefit that doesn't matter to the spirit of the games in context to each other, for a lot of others, what's the point in declaring yourself as being a cause-of-crossover-convergence when the numbers don't back it.<br /> <br /> We can argue quality all we want, and I'm not going to be the asshole to say art is purely subjective, because it's not. But there is a point where one's enjoyment purely comes from a subjective interaction with the material.<br /> <br /> So, no, it is not a fact, and even if it were possible for it to be so, your assertion that it is 10x better is sorely lacking evidence, so screw that interpretation anyways.<br /> <br /> Your hostility and absolutist stance on your opinions(demonstrated by presenting your opinion as fact) is the most defensive thing I have seen in this entire thread, so you'll forgive me if I ask of you some maturity. Cool down a little bit, soften up a little bit, and talk with us rather than argue with us.<br /> <br /> And for the record, yes, this is something I will keep correcting you on, because it's very poor forum etiquette and a nigh-on useless attitude for expressing an opinion in the hopes of change and revision. People, both forumites and writers, will flat out ignore you with the way you are going.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lol. I was merely reusing MCN's &quot;10x&quot; hyperbole. Pay more attention to the conversation.<br /> <br /> As for fact, it's not a matter of numbers more like gears fitting together. If I simply compare the two sets of mechanics to one another then Werewolf which has some very open world mechanics (i.e. doesn't assume that only Humans, Wolf-Blooded, and Werewolves can be in packs) easily comes up on top. The Beast mechanics consist of a couple of hacks and a lot of handwavium. Now you might think that handwavium is better but 30 years of experience tells me differently. Handwavium is headache inducing. So yes, from my set of professional standards for what makes a quality game, it's a fact, the Werewolf rules provide more actual substance that facilitates cross-overs. I fail to see how you're going to refute that with just a couple of hacks and deus ex machina. That's simply less substance so...<br /> <br /> Now we disagree, and you can lecture as much as you want but I don't agree that the points I'm making are poor etiquette. My primary point is that the material on Family is under-developed. And I feel like I've made that. Now the writers and other forumites (as you put it) are free to both disagree with my points and ignore them but that doesn't make you more right.<br /> <br /> I pretty much feel like you've been one of several hostile folks. This isn't my first rodeo, I've been lurking here (and on many another board) for quite some time. IIRC, it's not nice to &quot;correct&quot; people -- comes off as condescending. Disagree all you like but &quot;correcting&quot; people is essentially picking a fight. I wouldn't if I were you. I feel insulted. You're not a school-marm and I'm not a little boy so let's not do this. Civilized conversation, that's the best approach. <br /> <br /> Bonus round -- vis-a-vis facts. Consider what kinds of things social facts and fictional facts are. You have a very quantitative version of facts (evidenced by your text above and your interpretation of my saying it's a fact that werewolf does cross-over better)...social scientists aren't likely to appreciate your position. <br /> <br /> Bonus bonus round -- consider whether or not a game designed to implement crossovers in nWoD using the device of deus ex machina (And this really the device we want to use, when we have things like merits and similar mechanics that look tailor made to help?) is really going to succeed if all we know of Vamps, Werewolf, etc. cultures is correct. Recall that all of these groups are essentially equivalent to violent criminal groups. Do you think they're really going to be non-hostile to complete strangers? It doesn't make much sense to me that they would be. Now you can brush that off with a weak &quot;then don't play Beast&quot; but I ask you, what kind of cross-over game puts me in that position to start with. It just might be the case that folks complaining here and else where have valid gripes. As for me, I see real potential for this game, it's totally a diamond in the rough. I simply want the devs to knock some of those rough edges off. That's not a detraction of the work they've already put into it nor is it a knock against anything you like or you for liking it. That's simply a request to keep revising the draft and make Beast the best possible game that it can be. I have great confidence that the team here can do that. They've already done it with Vampire 2.0, Demon, and now Werewolf 2.0. From the looks of things Mage 2.0 and Changeling 2.0 are heading in the same direction. I have high hopes that they'll be able to rehabilitate Promethean as well (Wastelands and Disquiet effects in 1.0 were simply too much, making it all but unplayable for cross-over troupes like mine).<br /> <br /> I apologize if this comes off as hostile and absolutist but you're going to have to come down off your own hostile and absolutist high horses if we're going to talk like equals. When you can show me that Beast has at least as much substance as Werewolf, then I'll be willing to backtrack on my opinion of the facts as they are. Until then we're going to disagree about those facts (much like some people disagree about the facts regarding climate change and vaccine risks -- which for the record is happening and are far outweighed by their benefits respectively). Fact of the matter is people get confused by what are facts and what are opinions all the time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T15:01:29-07:00","id":583885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=583808#post583808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So...going by that logic, a soul-less Beast (or soul-supressed) would drain the Beast of his satiety rather than placing him in the same state that happens when the Beast goes over Satiety 10?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yep, suffering from the Soulless Condition, progressing into Enervated, until ending up as a Thrall. Makes sense to me. <br /> <br /> However, you do have a point in that there does seem to be a (possibly) unintended interaction between 2nd ed's condition rules and the fact that Beast's &quot;morality&quot; stat fluctuates by design (having unintended consequences). Hopefully a future draft and/or the final product will clarify this but it does make sense to me. A soulless Beast gets progressively hungrier and hungrier, preying on people left and right but never being able to fulfill that hole inside. Eventually the Beast essentially starves to death -- Satiety 1, Willpower 0.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1630-jacob","name":"Jacob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1630_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"681"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T15:08:48-07:00","id":583892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=583865#post583865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">IIRC, it's not nice to &quot;correct&quot; people -- comes off as condescending. Disagree all you like but &quot;correcting&quot; people is essentially picking a fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jacob, do you know what else is more unanimously considered picking a fight?<br /> <br /> <i>Picking a fight.</i><br /> <br /> Demonstrating an awareness of what is and is not likely to set people off is a skill that one would generally expect to be finely honed by the length of time you're purporting to have spent playing with other people and lurking on forums. So far you've instead demonstrated a similar degree of overfocus on demonstrating how witty you can be in the course of sharing an unpopular opinion to any other dime-a-dozen exemplar of bad manners. Framing matters, as does staying on-message, and tossing in quips comparing people who disagree with you to anti-vaxxers is poor practice for both of those things.<br /> <br /> From what you've said, you're likely twice as old as I am; while it may be selfish and symptomatic of a lingering inaccurate sense that maturity ought to increase with age on my part, I feel like I'm not the only one who would prefer that you conduct yourself accordingly in this matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T15:26:54-07:00","id":583908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=583892#post583892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jacob, do you know what else is more unanimously considered picking a fight?<br /> <br /> <i>Picking a fight.</i></div> </div> </div> </div><i>Ahem.</i><br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/736x/ea/5e/6e/ea5e6ee9bf58fc28ca2849637d146703.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> More to the point, on the topic of whether Beast powers are overpowered, my opinion is &quot;Who cares?&quot; The WoD is explicitly <i>not</i> designed around inter-splat balance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T15:33:21-07:00","id":583913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jacob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=583865#post583865\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for fact, it's not a matter of numbers more like gears fitting together. If I simply compare the two sets of mechanics to one another then Werewolf which has some very open world mechanics (i.e. <b>doesn't assume that only Humans, Wolf-Blooded, and Werewolves can be in packs</b>) easily comes up on top. The Beast mechanics consist of a couple of hacks and a lot of handwavium. Now you might think that handwavium is better but 30 years of experience tells me differently. Handwavium is headache inducing. So yes, from my set of professional standards for what makes a quality game, it's a fact, the Werewolf rules provide more actual substance that facilitates cross-overs. I fail to see how you're going to refute that with just a couple of hacks and deus ex machina. That's simply less substance so...</div> </div> </div> </div>In regards to the bolded part, if you are referring to the sidebar on p.90 of <b>Werewolf: the Forsaken Second Edition</b> titled &quot;Others,&quot; I think it would be fair to say that it refers to an <i>option</i>. I mean, sure everything's optional in the sense that the nWoD is designed as a toolbox. However, the rules are written with the assumption that most (if not all) packs are comprised of Uratha, wolf-blooded, and humans. To do otherwise is something that the group needs to discuss.<br /> <br /> As such, I'm not sure how fair it is to compare the two sets of mechanics. It could be (I don't know, I haven't tried) that trying to put some supernatural critters into a pack is (or may be in the future) somewhat difficult.<br /> <br /> YMMV, I suppose, but just thought I'd point that out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/552-strider1276","name":"strider1276","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar552_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"382"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T15:33:23-07:00","id":583914,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:red\">Ok, things are getting very close to personal attack territory here. Everyone please remember to respect other people and respect the conversation.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T15:37:18-07:00","id":583916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=583908#post583908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More to the point, on the topic of whether Beast powers are overpowered, my opinion is &quot;Who cares?&quot; The WoD is explicitly <i>not</i> designed around inter-splat balance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course it's not, but sometimes we'd like some kind of...Power Benchmark? With wiggle-room? You want all players to fall within a certain area of power in a game, or else you fall into the pitfall of players trying to solve a problem, and then the Mage comes around and solve it <i>every time</i>. (Please don't start a fight over the fact I used Mage. I could have used any splat)<br /> <br /> We don't want balance, but it would be nice not to have a player play a character with the power level of a mortal, another one with the power level of a Vampire, another one with the power level of an Exalted and the last one playing Doctor Manhattan. Especially if the player trying to tie everything together is Doctor Manhattan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T15:41:31-07:00","id":583932,"title":"","content":"Barring the satiety expenditure version, which I agree is problematic, doesn't You Are Meat only last for a scene, like most Nightmares? Even in the unlikely event that the victim immediately gives into their vice and fails the subsequent breaking point roll within the scene, they get the integrity back the next day. That's honestly less of an effect than many of the other Nightmares.<br /> <br /> The satiety expenditure effect needs to be toned down though, yeah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T15:50:56-07:00","id":583943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=583908#post583908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More to the point, on the topic of whether Beast powers are overpowered, my opinion is &quot;Who cares?&quot; The WoD is explicitly <i>not</i> designed around inter-splat balance.</div> </div> </div> </div> To an extent. If things are too wildly unbalanced, then we end up with the issue of overshadowing and making others feel redundant. Which is counter productive to the story when only one person can shine. Especially in a game about crossover where its highly likely we'll be dealing with a mixed party. If Beasts could easily be better at mind controlling than vampires, better hunters than werewolves, and magical explorers than mages, then yes, that would be an issue.<br /> <br /> The key to successful crossovers is for everyone to have a niche they like, and then stay in it. If someone naturally crowds them out, then it makes the game less fun. Not all game balance is about white room battles.<br /> <br /> And that is some of what I've seen. Some people claim that a Beast is better at doing werewolf stuff than the werewolves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=583916#post583916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> (Please don't start a fight over the fact I used Mage. I could have used any splat)</div> </div> </div> </div> Eh, it happens. Mages are the academic problem solvers, just like vampires are the go-to targets for beating up other splats. Especially if we're on the werewolf forums! <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zFuMpYTyRjw\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zFuMpYTyRjw\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zFuMpYTyRjw\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zFuMpYTyRjw </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T15:57:02-07:00","id":583951,"title":"","content":"Well, Direction Sense [Advanced] and [Epic] both render a Werewolf somewhat useless in tracking. You Must Obey render a Vampire useless in mind-control, and a few other things, but Beasts cannot full-heal themselves every round, or remove the lightning of a whole building by imprisoning the spirit of technology inhabiting it, or easily identifying the most-likely target to betray the mafia-boss.<br /> <br /> So all-in-all, I think MCN explains it better than I do so listen to what MCN says.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T16:13:44-07:00","id":583965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=583916#post583916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course it's not, but sometimes we'd like some kind of...Power Benchmark? With wiggle-room? You want all players to fall within a certain area of power in a game, or else you fall into the pitfall of players trying to solve a problem, and then the Mage comes around and solve it <i>every time</i>. (Please don't start a fight over the fact I used Mage. I could have used any splat)</div> </div> </div> </div>Beasts are pretty high up, but I don't think they exactly leave other 2nd edition splats behind.<br /> Going through your examples, Dragonfire will mostly be worse than a gun thanks to allowing Defense and it's short range, outside the extremely-limited-use Satiety effect. Fire is also the element with the most powers spread around the NWoD's powersets specifically aimed at defending against it.<br /> You must Obey can only give extremely limited orders and requires a lot of babysitting of your targets. It's basically useless against PCs, as their eyes transform into $ signs and they jump at the chance to get some extra Beats through the Breaking Points. Rember that you also have to succesfully look someone in the eyes to activate it, which you really can't expect to get away with more than once. After that, your opponents will know better.<br /> Titanic Blow seems okay within the context of the other powers Beasts get.<br /> <br /> Unbreakable and Relentless Hunter are probably the closest to overpowered now, but they are manageable.<br /> Unbreakable is a big one, but you just need to keep doing damage.This may be because of bad editing, but it also has some weird holes, as written its Satiety effect doesn't work against thrown weapons. It becomes problematic if your read the sentence about unarmed attacks in the satiety effect as making the Beast immune to all unarmed attacks (regardless of damage type inflicted) and attacks that deal Bashing - instead of just unarmed attacks that deal bashing damage. Another, probably unintended, inteaction: as written Armored Coffin would probably work against it.<br /> Relentless Hunter stands out as probably the most powerful healing effect in the setting for healing Aggravated Damage. But I wouldn't necessarily say it's better than Gauru form regeneration or a Mummy's ability to just keep functioning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/158192-what-s-your-custom-legacy?p=1109906#post1109906\" target=\"_blank\">My custom legacy</a> (2e)- The Disciples of Rathma - Life/Death focused Moros/Thyrsus Legacy, comments appreciated","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/166-joker","name":"Joker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T17:35:35-07:00","id":584010,"title":"","content":"I mean, Nightmares are abilities that draw on the astral meaning of specific fears. They don't directly rot your meat, or make you lost, or take away your memory, or summon bugs to swarm over you. You Are Meat does not really remove a target's soul so much as it inflicts that fear on them on a soul-deep level. They metaphysically suffer the fear of soulessness as such an absolute certainty it becomes real for them, <i>suppressing</i> their soul for the duration.<br /> <br /> Logic would state you don't need to actually have a soul to feel that realized fear exactly as most people do so long as you could understand its significance. But then again, the explanation for why it doesn't work on Beasts is that their soul, the Horror, is too powerful to just suppress.<br /> <br /> Which, as people have argued before, given the full scope of what a Horror is compared to mortal souls or whatever else, does make sense. But I can understand the perspective that certain beings who don't even technically have souls shouldn't be subject to the effect.<br /> <br /> In the end I think it greatly depends on how you look at Nightmares and how you consider those particular beings to interact with the astral concepts involved in their power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T17:58:20-07:00","id":584027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=583951#post583951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, Direction Sense [Advanced] and [Epic] both render a Werewolf somewhat useless in tracking. You Must Obey render a Vampire useless in mind-control,</div> </div> </div> </div> Actually, they don't. There are some very significant drawbacks to both the Direction Sense merits, and the You Must Obey power that make them less than perfect. <br /> <br /> Direction Sense is only good if you directly observe someone before. If you show up to, for instance, a crime scene? The wolf can immediately start tracking a spoor trail. The Beast is clueless. The Beast could divine what happened with Epic DS, but that wouldn't let them track. Furthermore, what people keep getting stuck on is that <i>tracking </i>is not the same thing as the <i>hunt</i>. They're actually not the same thing. Tracking is often part of the hunt, but it is not the whole of it, nor is it a required part. <br /> <br /> All in all, I would say that &quot;oh, I can find someone I've already met&quot; makes a very poor hunter when you need to hunt down Heroes in the territory when you just see the signs of their work. Neither Direction Sense nor Needs Must (which focuses on things that feed your Hunger) really helps in this case. <br /> <br /> You Must Obey doesn't hold a candle to someone under the influence of the Vinculum, and there's no Lashing Out equivalent (trust me, that little gem is handy). At best, you can compare YMO to Dominate 1 with the Normal function, and Dominate 2 with the High Satiety part, but even then, its definitely favoring Dominate. Why? <i>Because Dominate messes with memories. </i>You go up to someone and dominate them? You can tell them that they shot their own mother <i>and they believe it.</i> They'll hand over their blood and money, and never know what happened. And Dominate 1 is free to spam all scene long, no cost. If you use Dominate 2, it lasts even longer.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, YMO forces obedience through fear, and here's the thing. <i>The only way it enforces the order is through Integrity breaking points</i>. If it targeted a character? They could just take the breaking point and ignore the Beast. Generally, the ST won't do that, but it is always a potential option. Dominate doesn't have that issue. Actually, since we're on the part of Integrity breaking points... I take back what I said. It IS like the vinculum, since the blood bond is enforced through breaking points. And, even then, the vinculum is far more effective - the three drinks can be in rapid succession, it lasts a year, and has no limit on the command length. And innate for all vampires.<br /> <br /> Its also debatable how effective YMO is on supernaturals, due to the nature of Integrity equivalents. Harmony and Satiety make no sense mechanically, and neither Cover nor Humanity make sense thematically.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T19:26:41-07:00","id":584078,"title":"","content":"Also pointing something out that some of the power coming from beasts are melee meaning that they dont have much for long range. <br /> Also to point out is that they dont really have any regen unless they are in their lair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T20:04:06-07:00","id":584087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reaperfrost8</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=584078#post584078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also pointing something out that some of the power coming from beasts are melee meaning that they dont have much for long range.<br /> Also to point out is that they dont really have any regen unless they are in their lair.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well when's the last time you heard the epic tale of a hero marching into a monster's lair with a shining sword, and the monster whips out an assault rifle?<br /> <br /> Well okay, Hellsing doesn't count.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for not having much long range, It doesn't sound much like they need it. You've got dragons who breathe fire, creatures who can fly and thus have terrain advantage, and giants who are so powerful, they'll probably reach you before you can reload.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T20:17:34-07:00","id":584100,"title":"","content":"Does Dresden Files count?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T21:11:48-07:00","id":584157,"title":"","content":"Not sure what that is. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-08T21:25:29-07:00","id":584161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=584157#post584157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not sure what that is. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That's okay, we'll just begin arranging your exile now.<br /> <br /> Because apparently I have that power now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T03:08:39-07:00","id":584452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mages have an <i>Awakened Soul. </i>That's the core concept of the game. Removing it would not kill him, sure, but it <i>will</i> remove all of his neat powers </div> </div> </div>Actually no. Not immediately at least. Still enough time to bring awfull pain to the beast who did it (or alternatively use some death magic to help).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2636-menace","name":"Menace","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2636_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"527"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T06:34:16-07:00","id":584621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Menace</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=584452#post584452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually no. Not immediately at least. Still enough time to bring awfull pain to the beast who did it (or alternatively use some death magic to help).</div> </div> </div> </div>Not at all, in fact. It doesn't even turn their magic off, just makes it more dangerous to use.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T06:57:10-07:00","id":584676,"title":"","content":"I remembered the You Are Meat sidebar specifically saying that it did in fact turn a mage's magic off, so I went back to the revised drafts to see if that's still in there in case DaveB had to talk to his fellow writers.<br /> <br /> And, uh, hey guys: You Are Meat is not in the current up-to-date revised draft at all.<br /> <br /> So I guess that settles that one!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T07:46:56-07:00","id":584735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=584621#post584621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not at all, in fact. It doesn't even turn their magic off, just makes it more dangerous to use.</div> </div> </div> </div>This rubs me the wrong way, but I'll hold any comment until I have the book and the complete, final explanation as to why this happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T07:49:52-07:00","id":584736,"title":"","content":"It makes them unable to contain Paradox and causes more Paradox when they use magic. They can replace their soul with another to fix that though, it doesn't even have to be their old soul. They just need -a- soul to help mitigate &amp; absorb Paradox.<br /> <br /> It has to do with how Awakened magic works, and I suspect it also interacts with how the Tremere Liches work as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T08:17:25-07:00","id":584753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magnum Opus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=584735#post584735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This rubs me the wrong way, but I'll hold any comment until I have the book and the complete, final explanation as to why this happens.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When mages are Soulless, they lose Wisdom like a Sleeper loses Integrity. All spells cause Paradox, and they can't attempt to Contain it.<br /> <br /> When they're Enervated, they lose Gnosis along with Willpower. When they hit Thrall, even if they have Gnosis left over, they lose the ability to form imagos.<br /> <br /> If they get an Awakened soul, Gnosis dots come back 1/scene. If they get a Sleeper's soul, it comes back 1/chapter.<br /> <br /> You might have missed us saying it, but the stages of soul loss in second edition (much like the &quot;what have you forgotten&quot; and the &quot;witnessig the supernatural&quot; clauses of Integrity) were designed for Awakening 2e, then had the Mage stripped off them for God-Machine chronicle. In the same way that many of the Conditions were designed with Vampire in mind, and second-ed combat with Werewolf in mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T08:19:15-07:00","id":584757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=584676#post584676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remembered the You Are Meat sidebar specifically saying that it did in fact turn a mage's magic off, so I went back to the revised drafts to see if that's still in there in case DaveB had to talk to his fellow writers.<br /> <br /> And, uh, hey guys: You Are Meat is not in the current up-to-date revised draft at all.<br /> <br /> So I guess that settles that one!</div> </div> </div> </div>;w;<br /> <br /> You Are Meat and Tabula Rasa were honestly my favorite Nightmares from the moment I read them. They're absolutely terrifying. Here's to hoping the former will be put back in after reviewing* how it works.<br /> <br /> Huh, I was under the impression Awakened souls were actually special in and of themselves though. Rather than 'only' being an animating force filling a specific 'shape' which defines the person's actual identity.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">*If that's what it was pulled off the preview file for, rather than just outright removal.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 07-09-2015, 11:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T08:19:45-07:00","id":584758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=584736#post584736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Tremere Liches</div> </div> </div> </div> Mmmm... yummy tremere liches... one of my favorite parts of the game!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T08:29:42-07:00","id":584769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YeOfLittleFaith</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=584757#post584757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh, I was under the impression Awakened souls were actually special in and of themselves though. Rather than 'only' being an animating force filling a specific 'shape' which defines the person's actual identity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm glad that most souls are just an animating force in the nWoD. It brings a uniqueness to how the WoD handles metaphysics in a nicely personal way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T08:37:53-07:00","id":584774,"title":"","content":"They do get their owner's mind stamped into them occasionally. So it's more like animating force / emergency backup brain-vessel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T08:55:01-07:00","id":584805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=584769#post584769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm glad that most souls are just an animating force in the nWoD. It brings a uniqueness to how the WoD handles metaphysics in a nicely personal way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I find that consistent aspect of nWoD metaphysics quite enticing as well. That for the most part, the soul the games deal with is a substance that fills a fixed form, so to speak, rather than being a unique animating power that identifies the individual on its own.<br /> <br /> It makes the exceptions all the more interesting to think about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T09:13:00-07:00","id":584821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=584753#post584753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When mages are Soulless, they lose Wisdom like a Sleeper loses Integrity. All spells cause Paradox, and they can't attempt to Contain it.<br /> <br /> When they're Enervated, they lose Gnosis along with Willpower. When they hit Thrall, even if they have Gnosis left over, they lose the ability to form imagos.<br /> <br /> If they get an Awakened soul, Gnosis dots come back 1/scene. If they get a Sleeper's soul, it comes back 1/chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then I'll have to wait for a more complete metaphysical description of the difference between an Awakened and a Sleepwalker. Is the only real difference being that one signed his name in a Supernal Book? I always saw that as symbolical for the soul understanding reality, rather than the act itself giving you any real power.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=584753#post584753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You might have missed us saying it, but the stages of soul loss in second edition (much like the &quot;what have you forgotten&quot; and the &quot;witnessig the supernatural&quot; clauses of Integrity) were designed for Awakening 2e, then had the Mage stripped off them for God-Machine chronicle. In the same way that many of the Conditions were designed with Vampire in mind, and second-ed combat with Werewolf in mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>Happy to learn this. Now I wonder if anything was designed with the other splats in mind, like equipment and gadgets, Mystery Cult and Mummy or... stuff &amp; changeling. Probably not <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T09:19:16-07:00","id":584824,"title":"","content":"Astral/Dream Mechanics, from what I understand, were a crossbreed between keeping Mage, Changeling, and Beast in line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-09-2015, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T10:41:21-07:00","id":584870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=584824#post584824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Astral/Dream Mechanics, from what I understand, were a crossbreed between keeping Mage, Changeling, and Beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah - the Dream Form mechanics were written for Beast, Mage, and Changeling simultaneously. They came about because of my observation in Mage games of how using your Willpower as Health (as 1st ed astral mechanics did) sucked in 2nd ed, where willpower expenditure and gain is more common. So I took the opportunity to fix it, as all three games with a focus on mindscapes were in writing at the same time, and I was writing one and Developing another.<br /> <br /> The 2nd ed Gauntlet was written for Werewolf with an eye for what Mage would need from a Gauntlet chart, too.<br /> <br /> This sort of thing happens. Not quite nearly enough, but it makes for a more cohesive World of Darkness when it does.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T10:45:25-07:00","id":584873,"title":"","content":"Hey, that's a big part of what the Second Edition is about-refining and connecting pieces.<br /> <br /> And as always, thanks to you and the rest of team for bringing the World together in these ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T11:24:24-07:00","id":584920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=584870#post584870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah - the Dream Form mechanics were written for Beast, Mage, and Changeling simultaneously. They came about because of my observation in Mage games of how using your Willpower as Health (as 1st ed astral mechanics did) sucked in 2nd ed, where willpower expenditure and gain is more common. So I took the opportunity to fix it,</div> </div> </div> </div>And bless you for doing so, that rule always bothered me for pretty much the same reasons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T12:00:27-07:00","id":584978,"title":"","content":"So Geist 2E is gonnaclarify the Underworld for everybody,right?<br /> <br /> Geist 2E's gonna happen, right?<br /> <br /> ...Right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is