s=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=584978#post584978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Geist 2E is gonnaclarify the Underworld for everybody,right?<br /> <br /> Geist 2E's gonna happen, right?<br /> <br /> ...Right?</div> </div> </div> </div>I know the answer to this.<br /> <br /> [REDACTED]. Anything else about this subject will have to wait 'til Gen Con.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T15:43:58-07:00","id":585297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=584870#post584870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yeah - the Dream Form mechanics were written for Beast, Mage, and Changeling simultaneously. They came about because of my observation in Mage games of how using your Willpower as Health (as 1st ed astral mechanics did) sucked in 2nd ed, where willpower expenditure and gain is more common. So I took the opportunity to fix it, as all three games with a focus on mindscapes were in writing at the same time, and I was writing one and Developing another.<br /> <br /> The 2nd ed Gauntlet was written for Werewolf with an eye for what Mage would need from a Gauntlet chart, too.<br /> <br /> This sort of thing happens. Not quite nearly enough, but it makes for a more cohesive World of Darkness when it does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hooray! This is wonderful news!<br /> <br /> I found the mechanics in 1.0 to be kludgy (for Changeling) anyway so this is really positive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T21:34:07-07:00","id":585639,"title":"","content":"Speaking of being soulless, I'm a little leary of Beasts being the exception to the &quot;mages can't yank out supernatural souls&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> I just picture a reaper type collecting beast souls like pokemon for an order of cheese with more cheese.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T21:47:39-07:00","id":585646,"title":"","content":"What do you mean Sword?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T01:14:49-07:00","id":585756,"title":"","content":"At least in first edition mage the soul snatching spells could only target regular humans and mages efectively, because the &quot;soul&quot; of vampire, werewolves, changellings and such were weird as hell and didn't registered as what Awakened magic considered a soul for the most part. If you target a vampire even just to know if it had one it would read as &quot;inconclusive&quot;, same for werewolves (being half spirit messed things up) and CHnagelling's were in tatters.<br /> <br /> We don't know if this holds true for Awakening 2nd though, so maybe is a bit soon to complain?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":195,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","user":"Thorbes","date":". Oh, the irony! 07-10-2015, 04:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T01:34:03-07:00","id":585766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=585646#post585646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do you mean Sword?</div> </div> </div> </div> There's a bit in the revised beast draft that because Beast horrors exist in their lairs in the astral, they don't have the same protection against a mage snatching their souls that other supernaturals enjoy (mages snatching vampire, werewolf, changeling, is a no go, at least without archmastery), and since beast is a second edition book it's safe to assume, I feel, that they are intending that to remain in second edition, since beast says they are an exception. <br /> <br /> The issue I have with that is that if mages can snatch the souls, they can play with them in other ways.<br /> <br /> Put them in other people, put them into a soulless mage, consume the soul for power, put the soul in a trinket to make a beast fetish.<br /> <br /> Beasts become a power up.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T01:55:57-07:00","id":585773,"title":"","content":"To be fair, I'm fairly sure that the entire mages can only mess with the souls of humans and other mages bit was just part of 1es desperate attempt at not having mage make concrete statements about the nature of other lines (like the whole Arcadia thing) mixed with balance based restrictions. Now with a lot of the shared metaphysics being written into the core of the nWoD in general, and the removal of speed bumps in mage, I'm not quite sure how that's going to be handled in 2e.<br /> <br /> I figure if they're going to go ahead and give Beasts the power to do so, thus already opening that particular can of worms, they'll finally get over that particular hesitation for mage and toss out that specific limitation since the statement on monsters souls has already been stated elsewhere. I'd also guess that if they remove it from Beasts, they'll probably keep the rule as it is for mage (or the more likely answer being not acknowledging it at all, essentially telling us to decide for ourselves).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 07-10-2015, 08:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T04:54:07-07:00","id":585874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/579778-beast-why-i-don-t-want-them-in-crossovers?p=585766#post585766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Beasts become a power up.</div> </div> </div> </div> Welcome to lichhood. I fail to see why this is a bad thing, in terms of crossover plot hooks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T05:46:27-07:00","id":585932,"title":"","content":"I just had an idea. Beasts who undergo the Retreat become the Unfettered- an ephemeral being that still enjoys the use of Atavisms. I'd probably houserule it that if they're intelligent enough to remember human speech, they're probably intelligent enough to keep a hold on Nightmares which would convert into Numina. (Maybe, I don't know. Maybe the Nightmares exist on the side. They don't exactly have a cost similar to Essence and Unfettered keep Satiety.) In Mage 2E, 'familiar' isn't a particular kind of ephemeral being, it's a Manifestation. Apply that to one of the Unfettered, boom. Mage with a pet dragon.<br /> <br /> I also realized that Mage 1E actually references Beasts in the fourth chapter of &quot;Secrets of the Ruined Temple&quot;, though I doubt Beasts were a thing then. The Chimerical Beasts, does anyone remember those? Lots of interesting ideas in there- like cults trying to take a bodiless Horror from ancient legend and give it form again, or the idea of the Unfettered trying to become Beasts again by possessing humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T06:30:42-07:00","id":585985,"title":"","content":"An unfettered wanting to become physical again can claim someone, full control, superhuman stats, kept influences, dread powers, it's a pretty sweet deal all told.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T08:40:32-07:00","id":586149,"title":"","content":"Alternatively, there's those cases of Beasts-to-be who refused to truly become one during the decisive moment of their Devouring. What would be said of them, who no longer have any remnant of a human soul to serve as a dam before the full essence of the Primordial Dream, but who have denied their true self and turned their backs on the nightmarish substance supposed to complete them? They who are left with an empty spirit, completely open to that vast plane of humanity's deepest fears?*<br /> <br /> I cannot think of a more suitable vessel for one the Unfettered.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">*This is just my interpretation on what those Beasts who never claim their Horror after suffering through the Devouring end up like, of course. I figure they would be sorely <i>lacking</i> on a fundamental level while simultaneously being very vulnerable to the predations of the Primordial Dream, what with the shreds of human-soul-stuff blocking them from comprehension gone, but no Horror to fill the gap.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 07-10-2015, 11:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T08:50:09-07:00","id":586156,"title":"","content":"And now I'm going to play the Dark Presence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-10T09:03:40-07:00","id":586196,"title":"","content":"For some reason, I want to play Hexxus.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.dr